r_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/9b7da6a2027560d8d22786ded611cf5c0b7fca5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T12:37:48Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T12:37:48Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"build: read prose as prose in the layering scanner, and name the CI step after its chain (BUILD-028, BUILD-027)\n\nreadViews() kept string literals in the code view, so a template literal\nquoting an import line became a phantom edge — and the self-check counter,\nreading the bare view, then reported that the scanner had understood too\nlittle rather than too much. Both template forms hit it, multi-line and\nsingle-line.\n\nThe fix tracks ${ ... } depth recursively: interpolation content stays in\nboth views because it is code, only the literal text is emptied. That also\ncloses a nested template inside an interpolation, which desynchronised the\nflat scanner the same way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017HeB1Dj7BgceyVP54g8Drg","tree":{"sha":"af2a1a9c3dbe811ce215cc2a275769904bcfc1d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/af2a1a9c3dbe811ce215cc2a275769904bcfc1d8"},