s","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/d6da49848b72c3ccabfbd2ed3dabdcad33590551/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T20:13:18Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T20:13:18Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"docs: close out the remediation run for the 2026-08-12 audit\n\nFifteen packages, sixteen commits, and all 28 findings in scope are\nclosed -- four medium and twenty-four low, the whole \"Code & Laufzeit\"\ndomain minus its six info entries.\n\nThe run is breaking. Fifty entries now sit under Breaking Changes, up\nfrom forty-one at the audit commit: two signatures that refuse calls\nwhich used to compile, an overload pair that breaks any reduction to one\nsignature, a prefix on every message the library emits, and a five-name\nObject.keys() where there were nine.\n\nNo version bump. package.json says 1.0.0-dev, and that is a gate rather\nthan a neglected field -- publishPackage.cjs refuses while the suffix is\nthere and main publishes on every push, so dropping it is the release,\nwith no tag and no approval in between. That call belongs to the\nmaintainer. Package 13 wrote the mechanism into CONTRIBUTING so nobody\ntrips it by accident.\n\nWhat the run kept finding was that the audit''s numbers needed\nre-measuring. Eight packages refuted at least one figure or rationale:\nthe 194-line method is 128, the already-corrected allocation count was\nwrong again, one prefixed throw site out of 22 is ten out of 36,\nseventeen disabled Biome rules are sixteen and the sharpest claim about\nthem was void on the audit''s own date, a 9% write-path win sits under\nthe measurement floor, and two \"unreachable\" guards are reachable from\nconsumer code through a registered symbol. The recommendations mostly\nheld; their reasons often did not.\n\nTwo user decisions were revised mid-run for the same reason. API-012''s\napproved path -- exclude the passthrough in the type system -- is\nmeasured impossible, so it reports at runtime instead. READ-013''s guards\nwere to be deleted as dead; they are neither dead nor untested.\n\nThe plan goes in as it stands. What it is worth keeping for is the\nsection listing what this run did not clean up: seven things found in\nthe code along the way, none of them in scope, one of them addressed to\nthe next audit rather than to the library.\n\naudit.html is untouched. The follow-up run verifies against the code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"83cc614fdc3a9c36d16563a27ff41fec248dfda2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/83cc614fdc3a9c36d16563a27ff41fec248dfda2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/d6da49848b72c3ccabfbd2ed3dabdcad33590551","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/d6da49848b72c3ccabfbd2ed3dabdcad33590551","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKGQ2ZGE0OTg0OGI3MmMzY2NhYmZiZDJlZDNkYWJkY2FkMzM1OTA1NTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/43fe1142307eb9462dbd53a71ed118fa5aab66f5","sha":"43fe1142307eb9462dbd53a71ed118fa5aab66f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/43fe1142307eb9462dbd53a71ed118fa5aab66f5"}],"sha":"d6da49848b72c3ccabfbd2ed3dabdcad33590551","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/d6da49848b72c3ccabfbd2ed3dabdcad33590551"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/43fe1142307eb9462dbd53a71ed118fa5aab66f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T20:10:09Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T20:10:09Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"refactor: kebab-case for every module that is not a class (CONS-003)\n\nThree conventions ran side by side with no rule between them.\nPascalCase marked class modules, consistently. Function modules split:\ncreateSignal.ts and createMemo.ts in camelCase, bequiet.ts all-lowercase\nfor a function called beQuiet. Infrastructure modules likewise --\nglobalEffectStack.ts against global-queues.ts, signal-core.ts,\ncollect-errors.ts and object-signals.ts, all five doing the same job.\nhibernate.ts imported both styles two lines apart.\n\nKebab-case for every module that does not export a class. Four modules\nmove, twelve specs follow them, and two specs that never had a module\nlose their camelCase too -- a rule written today cannot carry two\nexceptions in its own directory. Nineteen non-class modules were already\nconform, including all four this run added. The rule itself goes into\nAGENTS.md under Repo conventions, as a rule rather than as a list of\ntoday''s filenames, and it says where it does not apply: rollup/ and\nscripts/.\n\nNothing but names changed, and the build says so: all thirty emitted\n.d.ts are byte-identical once the four filenames and their specifiers\nare normalised, the remaining difference being one JSDoc line in\nEffectImpl.d.ts. The three dist/ bundles are byte-identical including\nthe content-hashed chunk name; only sources and sourcesContent in the\nmaps move. 655 tests, 8/23/1/6 uncovered units -- unmoved.\n\nRenamed with git mv, so history follows: all eighteen come through at\n94-100% similarity.\n\nThe identifiers did not move. createSignal, createMemo and beQuiet are\nwhat they were; only the files they live in are spelled differently.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"8985d977b47b2ee5214d63a2c54a1b24cf62ab0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/8985d977b47b2ee5214d63a2c54a1b24cf62ab0b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/43fe1142307eb9462dbd53a71ed118fa5aab66f5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/43fe1142307eb9462dbd53a71ed118fa5aab66f5","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDQzZmUxMTQyMzA3ZWI5NDYyZGJkNTNhNzFlZDExOGZhNWFhYjY2ZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/4dc10b4db8438732068188f64a131d667a805e3c","sha":"4dc10b4db8438732068188f64a131d667a805e3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/4dc10b4db8438732068188f64a131d667a805e3c"}],"sha":"43fe1142307eb9462dbd53a71ed118fa5aab66f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/43fe1142307eb9462dbd53a71ed118fa5aab66f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/4dc10b4db8438732068188f64a131d667a805e3c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T19:29:12Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T19:29:12Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"docs: say what a version number promises, and what it does not (API-011)\n\nNeither the README nor CONTRIBUTING said which stability guarantee\napplies. That was a gap before this run and a pressing one after it:\nfifty breaking changes now sit under ## Unreleased, package.json says\n1.0.0-dev, and the last published version in the changelog is v0.31.1.\nA consumer installing today could not tell whether they were on a 0.x\nseries with no promises or ahead of a 1.0.0 that would start keeping\nthem.\n\nThe section makes no statement about the present -- no \"currently\", no\nversion number, no outlook on 1.0.0. It says what a number means and\nleaves the reader to compare it with the one they installed, so every\nsentence stays true on both sides of 1.0.0. The npm badge four lines up\nalready answers the where-are-we question, and answers it live.\n\nThree sentences would not have carried it. \"Semver on the published\nsurface\" is empty until the surface is named, and naming it took a\ncorrection: the first version said the surface was the two entry points\nplus the types in lib/**/*.d.ts. Measured, that glob is wider than the\npromise -- eight of thirty declaration files are outside the import\ngraph of either entry point while carrying real, un-@internal\ndeclarations, including a whole UniqIdGen class. tsc emits one per\nsource file; package.json#files ships the lot. The surface is what the\nimport graph reaches, and the text says so.\n\n\"@internal is exempt\" needed the same treatment. Those symbols are cut\nfrom the shipped declarations, so TypeScript will not offer them -- but\nsome stay reachable through the global symbol registry, which is how\npackage 9 found that [$setParentGroup] can build a cycle from consumer\ncode. Invisible in the types, callable at runtime, and now written down\nas such.\n\nThe publish mechanics go in CONTRIBUTING, where whoever edits\npackage.json will read them: dropping the -dev suffix is the release,\nbecause main publishes on push with no tag and no approval in between.\nSemver is a contract between a number and compatibility; a gate would\nnot make any sentence here truer, so the workflow is untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"b414255fed9aad509b2eee934a73c23dc0001305","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/b414255fed9aad509b2eee934a73c23dc0001305"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/4dc10b4db8438732068188f64a131d667a805e3c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/4dc10b4db8438732068188f64a131d667a805e3c","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDRkYzEwYjRkYjg0Mzg3MzIwNjgxODhmNjRhMTMxZDY2N2E4MDVlM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/c3b41631ee078643c0469d9e00a35260cf0ca934","sha":"c3b41631ee078643c0469d9e00a35260cf0ca934","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/c3b41631ee078643c0469d9e00a35260cf0ca934"}],"sha":"4dc10b4db8438732068188f64a131d667a805e3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/4dc10b4db8438732068188f64a131d667a805e3c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/c3b41631ee078643c0469d9e00a35260cf0ca934/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T19:03:49Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T19:03:49Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"docs: one rule for beforeRead, in all seven places that state it (BUG-013, CONS-013)\n\nThe docs said beforeRead fires on tracked reads. Measured against a\nbuilt dist/: it fires on every read through the reader -- tracked or\nnot, since beQuiet() and hibernate() suppress the subscription and not\nthe hook -- and is skipped only where the reader is bypassed, by .value,\nby value(sig), or by a readAsValue: true getter. A destroyed signal\nfires nothing.\n\nThe finding assumed docs/api.md had this right and only the source was\nwrong. It did not: the same wrong rule stood in seven places, and they\nare all written against the source JSDoc package 12a corrected rather\nthan against each other. Two of the claims had never been measured\nbefore -- readAsValue and the destroyed signal -- and both hold.\n\nCLAUDE.md no longer lists Biome rule names. The count it gave was\nalready wrong on the audit''s own date: useImportType had been turned on\nin the previous run, which is the rule whose absence the finding''s\nsharpest sentence rested on. Today it is sixteen off and four on error,\ntwo of those genuine additions from this run. The paragraph points at\nbiome.json and explains only the three that are not obvious, plus the\nfact that three of the sixteen match nothing in this codebase at all --\nwhich \"each a deliberate pattern\" claimed they did.\n\nThe note about comments in biome.json took a round to get right. The\nside-finding it came from said a comment degrades the config silently.\nIt does not: every placement fails pnpm check with a parse error naming\nline and column. What the side-finding actually saw is what happens\nafter that error -- Biome falls back to a default config, loses\nfiles.includes, and buries the parse error under a few hundred\ndiagnostics from files nobody meant to lint. An inline comment does not\neven get that far. The note says that now, because it was measured in\nall three placements rather than carried forward.\n\nThree ASYNC-004 changelog entries meant two different findings from two\ndifferent audits. They carry their dates.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"9b15838a51d6f47d00f8381c04027cf60fa3d027","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/9b15838a51d6f47d00f8381c04027cf60fa3d027"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/c3b41631ee078643c0469d9e00a35260cf0ca934","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/c3b41631ee078643c0469d9e00a35260cf0ca934","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKGMzYjQxNjMxZWUwNzg2NDNjMDQ2OWQ5ZTAwYTM1MjYwY2YwY2E5MzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/738620177c4bc21575c42e718411e8258e47d589","sha":"738620177c4bc21575c42e718411e8258e47d589","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/738620177c4bc21575c42e718411e8258e47d589"}],"sha":"c3b41631ee078643c0469d9e00a35260cf0ca934","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/c3b41631ee078643c0469d9e00a35260cf0ca934"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/738620177c4bc21575c42e718411e8258e47d589/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:43:28Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:43:28Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"docs(src): make the comments say what the code next to them does (READ-004, READ-008, BUG-013, CONS-014)\n\n[RECALL]() claimed the effect runs \"only if it is necessary\" and named\ntwo conditions. It marks the effect dirty; whether it runs is\nautorun-or-a-parked-explicit-run, and the necessity test lives in #run().\nThe audit''s suggested wording was wrong too -- it predates\n#explicitRunRequested, so a parked explicit run does fire. The JSDoc\nfollows the code, not the recommendation.\n\ncreateMemo listed four options and left out batchWrites, the one with\nthe longest justification in the file; it points at CreateMemoOptions\nnow, which cannot drift. createEffect documented a @param dependencies\nthat binds to nothing: the export is typeof EffectImpl.createEffect\ntaking ...args, so the tag names an argument the signature does not\nhave. The third site the audit named is gone -- packages 4a and 4b\nrewrote every createSignal overload.\n\nvalue() promised it was \"equivalent to wrapping the read in beQuiet(),\nbut more convenient\". Measured against a built dist/: beQuiet(() =>\nsig.get()) fires beforeRead, hibernate does too, .value and value() do\nnot. On a {lazy: true} memo whose recompute hangs off beforeRead, that\nis the difference between a value and a permanent undefined. The same\nwrong rule sits in six places in the docs; this is the one the rest will\nbe written against.\n\nobject-signals.ts was the only module on the published surface with no\nJSDoc at all, and the one with the least obvious return values. Four\nblocks, each naming its own undefined case.\n\nComments carried verbatim through packages 6 and 9 named identifiers\nthat no longer exist -- subscriptions for #handles, \"the cancel handle\nbelow\" for the first statement of the same method, unsubscribe() for\nreleaseAll(). SignalAutoMap#create() now states the invariant the\npackage-1 fix rests on, which until now lived only in the plan.\n\nEverything above is a comment. Outside the one test change, the diff has\nno non-comment line in it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"8baef5bd38c028e38702553c825f9b783930080b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/8baef5bd38c028e38702553c825f9b783930080b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/738620177c4bc21575c42e718411e8258e47d589","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/738620177c4bc21575c42e718411e8258e47d589","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDczODYyMDE3N2M0YmMyMTU3NWM0MmU3MTg0MTFlODI1OGU0N2Q1ODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/73c1a3a3d502022014997c4caa99877ad72bfb92","sha":"73c1a3a3d502022014997c4caa99877ad72bfb92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/73c1a3a3d502022014997c4caa99877ad72bfb92"}],"sha":"738620177c4bc21575c42e718411e8258e47d589","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/738620177c4bc21575c42e718411e8258e47d589"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/73c1a3a3d502022014997c4caa99877ad72bfb92/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T17:53:36Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T17:53:36Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"build: take the calendar out of the bundle banner (SEC-001)\n\nEvery build stamped +esm.YYYYMMDD into the version and the current year\ninto the copyright line, so the same commit built on two days produced\ndifferent bytes and a consumer could not check the published artifact\nagainst a rebuild of their own.\n\nThe damage was worse than the finding said: rollup hashes the banner\ninto the chunk name, so the date changed the file name too, and with it\nthe import line inside index.js and decorators.js. Four of six dist/\nfiles drifted, not one.\n\nBoth dates are gone -- the version keeps +esm, the copyright end year is\nwritten out. The year was not obviously in scope, and measuring settled\nit: with the build stamp removed but getFullYear() still computed, the\nsame commit still differs under a process set to 2027. Measured after:\n96 of 96 files across dist/ and lib/ byte-identical, over a year''s\nshift, across timezones and locales, and twice in one process.\n\ncheck:banner hangs in pnpm check, so it blocks in CI. It renders the\nbanner twice under two stubbed clocks and compares, rather than building\ntwice -- a double build can only fake the second day the same way and\nwould cost two full builds that trample the dist/ the gate is running\nagainst.\n\nThe first version of that gate had a hole worth keeping in mind: it\nstubbed Date after its static imports, so anything evaluated at module\ntop level was already captured and invisible to it -- exactly the shape\nthe old makeVersionWithBuild had. It loads both modules through a\ncache-busted dynamic import after stubbing now, and a module-level\nnew Date() in createBanner turns it red instead of passing.\n\nThe chunk name changes once as a result. No public path names it: the\nexports map lists only ./index.js and ./decorators.js.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"7a20635f2c9b3cb623d882ef540f2213f544b504","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/7a20635f2c9b3cb623d882ef540f2213f544b504"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/73c1a3a3d502022014997c4caa99877ad72bfb92","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/73c1a3a3d502022014997c4caa99877ad72bfb92","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDczYzFhM2EzZDUwMjAyMjAxNDk5N2M0Y2FhOTk4NzdhZDcyYmZiOTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/74c85b35edf84c3f5174063bb3d444a46e8f0c88","sha":"74c85b35edf84c3f5174063bb3d444a46e8f0c88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/74c85b35edf84c3f5174063bb3d444a46e8f0c88"}],"sha":"73c1a3a3d502022014997c4caa99877ad72bfb92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/73c1a3a3d502022014997c4caa99877ad72bfb92"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/74c85b35edf84c3f5174063bb3d444a46e8f0c88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T17:12:08Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T17:12:08Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"refactor: give every message the [signalize] prefix, and one gate for all three deprecations (CONS-002, CONS-004)\n\nThe audit said one of 22 throw sites carried the prefix. Counted today:\nten do. It also said the diagnostics carry it throughout; five of eleven\ndo not. The real shape is 36 messages, 20 without -- and the rule now\ncovers all of them, thrown, rejected or reported, because three families\nwith an exception list is not a rule.\n\nWhat holds it is src/message-prefix.spec.ts, and the point of that file\nis that it cannot go quiet. A scanner that stops matching passes in\nsilence, which is worse than no scanner: it asserts a promise nobody\nkeeps. So an unclassifiable message fails rather than being skipped, an\nunknown error class fails, each of the four scans carries a floor one\nstep under its current count, and their sum carries another -- because\none step of slack per scan is affordable once, not three times at the\nsame moment. Every one of those was proven to fire by breaking it.\n\nIt took two rounds to get there. The first version could be silenced by\nmoving a payload into an untyped variable: the scan anchored on\n`reportSignalizeError({`, the floor sat two below the count, and both\nchecked messages went dark with the suite green. It anchors on the call\nnow. Console output was not scanned at all, a custom error class in\nrejection position walked past, and a subdirectory under src/ would have\ntaken its messages out of scope.\n\nconsole is a lint rule rather than a regex, the same trade package 5\nmade for the export list: noConsole is an error everywhere in src/ but\nthe two files that legitimately write there. It catches the computed and\noptional forms; it does not catch a destructured alias, so a sixth\nassertion pins console to those two files by name.\n\nwarnDeprecatedOnce(key, message) replaces one module flag and two\nunconditional calls. The prefix stays with the caller so the scanner\nchecks one rule, and a separate spec drives all three deprecation paths\nin one module graph and compares the set of messages -- three of them\nfrom one site would satisfy a count, not a set.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"e2d0a23127f0ac3ec0d18ec21bba454976aafa14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/e2d0a23127f0ac3ec0d18ec21bba454976aafa14"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/74c85b35edf84c3f5174063bb3d444a46e8f0c88","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/74c85b35edf84c3f5174063bb3d444a46e8f0c88","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDc0Yzg1YjM1ZWRmODRjM2Y1MTc0MDYzYmIzZDQ0NGE0NmU4ZjBjODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/2d5c28ff949aa99840d1c9256d909d8285a96462","sha":"2d5c28ff949aa99840d1c9256d909d8285a96462","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/2d5c28ff949aa99840d1c9256d909d8285a96462"}],"sha":"74c85b35edf84c3f5174063bb3d444a46e8f0c88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/74c85b35edf84c3f5174063bb3d444a46e8f0c88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/2d5c28ff949aa99840d1c9256d909d8285a96462/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T15:23:26Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T15:23:26Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"refactor(group): name the registers after what they hold, and count the collections that are there (READ-005, READ-003, READ-013)\n\n#otherSignals held every signal ever bound under a name, the active one\nincluded, and the name pointed readers of #removeSignal() and\n#releaseFromName() the wrong way. It is #signalsByName now, and\n#signalKeys -- which called the same concept a key -- is #namesBySignal.\nPrivate fields throughout: the emitted .d.ts are byte-identical to the\ncommit before this one, all 29 of them.\n\nThe allocation comment was wrong, and not in the way the audit said. It\nhad already been corrected once, to \"five Sets, three Maps, a WeakMap\nand a WeakSet\", and that correction is wrong too: the unsubs Set inside\nthe [$groupResources] wrapper is not in the count. Eleven collections,\nsix Sets, three Maps, a WeakMap and a WeakSet -- eight of the nine the\nearly store lookup skips are fields, the ninth is the wrapper''s own. The\n\"race\" it warned about is re-entrant construction; a single-threaded\nruntime has no other kind.\n\nREAD-013 asked for the two busy bits in hasSignal() and signal() to go,\non the grounds that attachGroup()''s Floyd walk is the only place that\nbuilds an edge. It is not. [$setParentGroup] writes #parentGroup with no\nwalk at all, its symbol is in the global registry, it survives into the\nbundle, and a consumer script against a freshly built dist/ builds a ↔ b\nwith it -- at which point those bits are what stops the recursion. They\nare also witnessed, and have been since the last run. So they stay, the\nfinding closes on the other branch it offered, and the comment that\nclaimed a forest now names the edge that breaks it.\n\nCarried in from package 1: #removeSignal() aborted when a throwing\nunsubscribe came out of #dropSignalSubscription(), leaving the signal in\n#signals and #directSignals with its destroy subscription already gone.\nIt collects now, like every other teardown in this class -- registers\ncleared and the error still raised, not swallowed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"df397bff16383b9ea9b6d1d9742e8a251bf2d40c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/df397bff16383b9ea9b6d1d9742e8a251bf2d40c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/2d5c28ff949aa99840d1c9256d909d8285a96462","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/2d5c28ff949aa99840d1c9256d909d8285a96462","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDJkNWMyOGZmOTQ5YWE5OTg0MGQxYzkyNTZkOTA5ZDgyODVhOTY0NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/2c252bee9e0528d0a4ff56e85bbdbadea182912a","sha":"2c252bee9e0528d0a4ff56e85bbdbadea182912a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/2c252bee9e0528d0a4ff56e85bbdbadea182912a"}],"sha":"2d5c28ff949aa99840d1c9256d909d8285a96462","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/2d5c28ff949aa99840d1c9256d909d8285a96462"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/2c252bee9e0528d0a4ff56e85bbdbadea182912a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T14:38:51Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T14:38:51Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"perf: hoist the default comparator, and count error handlers instead of scanning for them (PERF-006, PERF-005)\n\nSignalImpl#writer built a fresh `(a, b) => a === b` on every write. The\naudit claimed 9% on the bare write path; measured across twelve rounds\nand all six orderings, that does not hold -- a byte-identical copy of\nthe library runs 2.9% slower than the original just for sitting in a\ndifferent place, which is wider than the effect. The fix carries for a\ndifferent, measured reason: scavenges per 20M writes drop from 143 to\n76, and the escape analysis that flattens an object literal does not\nflatten a closure. Roughly 48 bytes of garbage per write, on the\nhottest operation the library offers.\n\nemitEffectError() asked getSubscribedEventNames(queue).includes(...)\nbefore reporting. Every live effect subscribes to that queue under its\nown id, so the check built an array with one entry per live effect and\nwalked it: 16 microseconds at 8000 effects, measured, and the shape that\nbreaks the \"errors are rare\" assumption reports once per run -- 25\nwrites produced 26 reports. A module-level counter answers in 0.013.\nreportSignalizeError() ran the same scan a second time on the same path,\nso a reported error with no handler registered scanned twice; both are\ngone.\n\nA counter can be wrong where a scan cannot, and wrong here means a\nsilent error. So: eventize''s unsubscribe is idempotent, which the\naudit''s suggested shape did not account for -- a second call would have\ndecremented twice and muted a handler that was still registered. Every\nhandle carries a released latch, decrementing happens before\nunsubscribing, and the direction is deliberate: undercount and fall back\nto the console, never overcount and report into the void.\n\nNine witnesses, and the counter was attacked rather than trusted:\ntriple and interleaved unsubscribes, a handler removing itself mid\ndelivery and one registering mid delivery, a throwing handler,\nre-entrancy three deep, object listeners, crossed unsubscribes across\ntwo queues, full group teardown, and 600 dropped groups through three\nforced collections. One overcount path exists and is written down rather\nthan guarded: registering an EffectImpl itself as an object listener\nties the subscription to that effect''s destroy(). It needs a method\nunder an internal symbol to reach, EffectErrorCallback is a function\ntype, and a guard against it would be dead code under a 100% gate.\n\nThe counter lives in its own leaf module. Putting it in effects.ts\ntype-checks and compiles, and rollup rejects it: effects.js ->\nEffectImpl.js -> effects.js.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"290ddc713048757836742edde7d434cca9718e41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/290ddc713048757836742edde7d434cca9718e41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/2c252bee9e0528d0a4ff56e85bbdbadea182912a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/2c252bee9e0528d0a4ff56e85bbdbadea182912a","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDJjMjUyYmVlOWUwNTI4ZDBhNGZmNTZlODViYmRiYWRlYTE4MjkxMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/ac9a9ed3a93b0bc1519ac9da942be53df80095b8","sha":"ac9a9ed3a93b0bc1519ac9da942be53df80095b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/ac9a9ed3a93b0bc1519ac9da942be53df80095b8"}],"sha":"2c252bee9e0528d0a4ff56e85bbdbadea182912a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/2c252bee9e0528d0a4ff56e85bbdbadea182912a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/ac9a9ed3a93b0bc1519ac9da942be53df80095b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T13:33:23Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T13:33:23Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"refactor(effects): put EffectImpl''s methods on the prototype and its last field behind # (PERF-009, READ-006)\n\nrun, runImmediately and destroy were bound arrow properties: one closure\nper instance, three of them sharing a context that only died with the\nlast. They are prototype methods now. childEffects was the one data\nfield still using erasable TS private among thirteen # fields, which\nmade it an ordinary enumerable own property -- readable and writable\nfrom outside on an instance that onCreateEffect() hands to application\ncode. Writing to it derailed destroy() with a TypeError. It is\n#childEffects now.\n\nMeasured, because the audit''s reasoning was wrong even though its\nrecommendation was right: this saves 232 bytes per EffectImpl, and no\ntime at all. The bench''s own run-to-run spread is 6.9%, wider than any\ngap between the two versions. The finding said \"a closure over 132\nlines\" -- run has been three lines since the last run took #run() apart.\nIt is an allocation fix, and it says so.\n\nThe Effect facade keeps its arrows, and that is load bearing rather than\ninconsistent: Signal#onChange() destructures destroy off the facade and\nhands it back as the caller''s unsubscribe, and createMemo() passes\nrunImmediately and destroy on detached. The comment on Effect#onDestroy()\nused to recommend cleaning that binding up. It now says the opposite,\nand why.\n\nFour witnesses, written before the change: the facade stays bound (green\nboth before and after -- the only thing standing between onChange() and\na silent break, proven by reverting the facade and watching it go red),\nchildEffects is gone from Object.keys(), an outside write no longer\nderails destroy(), and the three methods live on the prototype against a\nwritten-out five-name key list.\n\nTwo breaking edges, both listed: a detached FailingEffect#destroy now\nthrows instead of working, and Object.keys() on an EffectImpl returns\nfive names where it returned nine. The lib/Effect.d.ts output is\nbyte-identical; lib/EffectImpl.d.ts changes exactly the two signatures\nand drops the field.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"c9e7e20e8474925164254e0509f226986c774992","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/c9e7e20e8474925164254e0509f226986c774992"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/ac9a9ed3a93b0bc1519ac9da942be53df80095b8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/ac9a9ed3a93b0bc1519ac9da942be53df80095b8","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKGFjOWE5ZWQzYTkzYjBiYzE1MTlhYzlkYTk0MmJlNTNkZjgwMDk1Yjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/c397785ac3dafea548ac863f660561f0fd084732","sha":"c397785ac3dafea548ac863f660561f0fd084732","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/c397785ac3dafea548ac863f660561f0fd084732"}],"sha":"ac9a9ed3a93b0bc1519ac9da942be53df80095b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/ac9a9ed3a93b0bc1519ac9da942be53df80095b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/c397785ac3dafea548ac863f660561f0fd084732/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T12:49:09Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T12:49:09Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"refactor(link): take nextValue() apart, after pinning what held it together (READ-014)\n\n#nextValue was the longest method in the codebase on both axes -- 128\nlines, 65 of them code -- holding four settle paths, an ordering promise\nbetween three subscriptions, and one shared unsubscribe. The comments\ncarried that; the structure did not.\n\nThe refactor came second. First, twenty mutations against the method as\nit stood, to find out which of its promises any test actually held. Ten\nwere witnessed. Eight turned out to be order-independent, measured\nagainst seven scenarios rather than assumed. Two were observable and\nwitnessed by nothing: swapping the two guards makes nextValue({signal})\non a destroyed link reject with the destroy error instead of the abort\nreason, and dropping the shared release from the abort path leaves two\nlink-side subscriptions standing for good. The suite stayed green for\nboth. They have witnesses now, written before a line moved, each one\nred under its own mutation and only its own.\n\nThen the cut: a module-private NextValueRead<ValueType> holding the\nsubscription bracket, its shared releaseAll() and the four settle paths,\nplus SignalLink.#consumeGeneration(cursor). #nextValue is 99 lines now,\n37 of them code. It misses #run()''s 91-line mark and that is the mark\nbeing wrong, not the cut being shallow: 62 of the 99 lines are comment\nor blank, the K1 block alone is 18, and cutting deeper would mean\ndeleting the comments that carry the ordering promises.\n\nGuards, subscribe sequence and the K1 block stand word for word, in the\norder they stood in. What moved, moved verbatim.\n\nEquivalence is not asserted, it is measured: all twenty mutations run\nagainst both the old and the new version kill the byte-identical set of\nnamed tests. 625 tests, 8/23/1/6 uncovered units -- unmoved. The emitted\nlib/**/*.d.ts are byte-identical to HEAD; only SignalLink.js differs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"fb8938e5c7bc7cab6ffab3bf7b5e4937d1c22abe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/fb8938e5c7bc7cab6ffab3bf7b5e4937d1c22abe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/c397785ac3dafea548ac863f660561f0fd084732","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/c397785ac3dafea548ac863f660561f0fd084732","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKGMzOTc3ODVhYzNkYWZlYTU0OGFjODYzZjY2MDU2MWYwZmQwODQ3MzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/6648a6c5d4fb922870022374ca2f46b4ea477408","sha":"6648a6c5d4fb922870022374ca2f46b4ea477408","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/6648a6c5d4fb922870022374ca2f46b4ea477408"}],"sha":"c397785ac3dafea548ac863f660561f0fd084732","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/c397785ac3dafea548ac863f660561f0fd084732"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/6648a6c5d4fb922870022374ca2f46b4ea477408/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:58:10Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:58:10Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"refactor: name every export of the entry point, and drop the commented-out link option (API-017, IMPL-001)\n\nThe type star fell in an earlier run and the comment above the type list\nalready said why: a star publishes every future export of a module\nunasked. Two value stars stood four lines below it. Adding an export to\nlink.ts published it, and no gate said a word.\n\nBoth are named lists now, and the promise moved to the top of the file\nwhere it covers the whole of it: what is listed here is the published\nsurface, and a module export that is not listed is not published.\n\nTwo things hold it, and the second is not redundant. Biome''s\nperformance/noReExportAll fails pnpm check on a value star. It does not\nsee `export type *` -- measured -- which is exactly the form the old\ncomment warned about, so index.public-surface.spec.ts catches both star\nforms and any drift in the value list, against a written-out list of its\nown rather than a second derivation from index.ts. There is no tool for\nthe type half: tsc erases types and nothing reflects on them. That rests\non the rule, and it says so.\n\nWhat this does not do, and the file says that too: a new export added to\na module still goes unnoticed. It just no longer publishes itself.\nPublishing costs two deliberate edits now instead of none.\n\nThe published surface does not move: 63 names before, 63 after -- 33 on\nthe value side through the built dist/, 30 type-only through the\ncompiler, measured on both axes before and after.\n\nLinkOptions loses its commented-out twoWay, typo and all. It never\nreached lib/ -- tsc only carries declaration-bound doc comments -- so\nthere is nothing for a consumer to notice and no changelog line for it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"aa314fd3b93cc844b68f80b0df1393c22f0558a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/aa314fd3b93cc844b68f80b0df1393c22f0558a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/6648a6c5d4fb922870022374ca2f46b4ea477408","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/6648a6c5d4fb922870022374ca2f46b4ea477408","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDY2NDhhNmM1ZDRmYjkyMjg3MDAyMjM3NGNhMmY0NmI0ZWE0Nzc0MDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/a85c312065f401d6d33b4007fca19fd9b4b46c78","sha":"a85c312065f401d6d33b4007fca19fd9b4b46c78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/a85c312065f401d6d33b4007fca19fd9b4b46c78"}],"sha":"6648a6c5d4fb922870022374ca2f46b4ea477408","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/6648a6c5d4fb922870022374ca2f46b4ea477408"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/a85c312065f401d6d33b4007fca19fd9b4b46c78/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:29:16Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:29:16Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"fix: the passthrough says what it throws away (API-012)\n\ncreateSignal(existingSignal, params) returns the signal it was handed,\nso nothing in params has anything to configure -- attach excepted, since\nit is applied behind the branch. lazy, compare and beforeRead were\ndropped on the floor without a word. The passthrough is documented; the\nsilent discard was not.\n\nExcluding it in the type system was the first choice and is measured\nimpossible: overload resolution still falls through, and any type test\nthat keeps a signal off the value overload breaks decorators.ts, the one\ncall site this library makes itself. So it reports at runtime, through\nthe channel API-009 opened -- source: ''ignored-option'', on every such\ncall, the same shape createMemo({name}) without {attach} already uses.\n\nThe list of dropped keys is written out rather than derived from\nObject.keys(params), and that is load bearing: decorators.ts hands its\nown options object straight through, and the name/readAsValue in there\nare the decorator''s business, not dropped signal options. A derived list\nwould report them and be wrong on exactly that call. A type-level\ntripwire keeps the written-out list honest -- add a key to SignalParams\nand the build fails at that line with a message saying where to put it.\nA plain type alias would not have fired: unused, it is never resolved,\nand noUnusedLocals kills it first. It is a declare const, and it emits\nnothing into lib/.\n\nTwo doors reach the branch that {lazy: true} can no longer walk through\nas a literal, since package 4a closed that: a SignalParams<T> variable,\nand the factory overload -- createSignal(sig.get, {lazy: true}) compiles\nthere because a SignalReader<T> is both a SignalLike<T> and the () => T\nit asks for, and isSignal() routes it back here at runtime. Both are\nwitnessed. The factory-door witness asserts identity with the source\nsignal, which the factory branch structurally cannot produce.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"5277b6c5a18d9f9b0225aee7ce690081224a8fb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/5277b6c5a18d9f9b0225aee7ce690081224a8fb6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/a85c312065f401d6d33b4007fca19fd9b4b46c78","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/a85c312065f401d6d33b4007fca19fd9b4b46c78","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKGE4NWMzMTIwNjVmNDAxZDZkMzNiNDAwN2ZjYTE5ZmQ5YjRiNDZjNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/dbc7b9a0ead0ff9a5aafb28994f17b5888ebf31a","sha":"dbc7b9a0ead0ff9a5aafb28994f17b5888ebf31a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/dbc7b9a0ead0ff9a5aafb28994f17b5888ebf31a"}],"sha":"a85c312065f401d6d33b4007fca19fd9b4b46c78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/a85c312065f401d6d33b4007fca19fd9b4b46c78"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/dbc7b9a0ead0ff9a5aafb28994f17b5888ebf31a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T10:55:54Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T10:55:54Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"fix(types): a signal with no initial value says so, and no lazy flag at construction (API-013, BUG-014)\n\ncreateSignal<number>() handed back a Signal<number> holding undefined.\nThe type said number, the value was undefined, and a consumer compiling\nwith strictNullChecks got no warning at all -- the promise was only\nfalse for the people who had asked for it to be true. There is a fourth\noverload now, initialValue?: undefined, returning Signal<Type |\nundefined>. Without a type argument the result stays Signal<unknown>,\nbecause unknown | undefined is unknown.\n\ncreateSignal(1, {lazy: true}) was the constructor half of the defect\npackage 3a closed on set(): it compiled, stored the value where the\nfactory belongs, and left the first read to die with \"TypeError:\nthis.valueFn is not a function\". Both the value and the no-init overload\ncarry the same three clauses now. The no-init overload needs them most:\nundefined is the one value that reaches it, so without them it is the\nhole every other clause falls through.\n\nThe clause checks the params type the compiler infers, and the docs\ndescribe it by what that inference produces rather than by a list of\nshapes -- three outcomes, because two earlier wordings each had one of\ntheir own examples standing outside them. A pattern index key survives\nExclude intact and is refused although it shares nothing; a bare type\nparameter leaves the conditional deferred and is refused although it\nadds nothing.\n\nWhat it costs, beyond the shapes that name a key the options do not\ndeclare: the weak-type check is gone for a params variable whose keys\nare wholly disjoint. It used to be TS2769, it is silently accepted now,\nand it does nothing at runtime. Object literals are still caught, by\nfreshness. set() lost the same check in 3a; for createSignal it is new,\nand it is written down in all five places rather than discovered later.\n\nsmoke/tsconfig.json compiles as a consumer, with strictNullChecks on.\nThat is what the package claims to be, and it is the only profile under\nwhich API-013 can be witnessed at all -- with the flag off, Type |\nundefined collapses to Type and the directive would never fail. Every\nexisting smoke witness was re-measured under both profiles: same errors,\nsame lines, nothing masked.\n\ndecorators.ts:56 now says why its <T> is load bearing. It is the only\ncaller in the repo balancing on that edge, and dropping the argument\nfails with a message that names neither the cause nor the option.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"585be61348f947180d211c477a9cd247795d82ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/585be61348f947180d211c477a9cd247795d82ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/dbc7b9a0ead0ff9a5aafb28994f17b5888ebf31a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/dbc7b9a0ead0ff9a5aafb28994f17b5888ebf31a","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKGRiYzdiOWEwZWFkMGZmOWE1YWFmYjI4OTk0ZjE3YjU4ODhlYmYzMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/0e4299da1748bb3c43cb5ea900fe457a89ea76fc","sha":"0e4299da1748bb3c43cb5ea900fe457a89ea76fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/0e4299da1748bb3c43cb5ea900fe457a89ea76fc"}],"sha":"dbc7b9a0ead0ff9a5aafb28994f17b5888ebf31a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/dbc7b9a0ead0ff9a5aafb28994f17b5888ebf31a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/0e4299da1748bb3c43cb5ea900fe457a89ea76fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T09:36:10Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T09:36:10Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"fix(types): give link() an overload pair so a callback target types its parameter (TYPE-007)\n\nlink(sig, (v) => …) reported TS7006 under noImplicitAny and fell\nsilently to any without it. LinkableTarget<T> is a union with more than\none call signature -- SignalReader<T> is itself callable -- and\nTypeScript builds no contextual type against that. The annotated form\ncompiled, the idiomatic one did not.\n\nTwo overloads now, signal target first. Both orderings accept and refuse\nexactly the same calls, but only this one puts link(src, dst) and\nlink(src, dst.get) on the overload that signalImpl(target) matches at\nruntime -- measured with branded return types, not reasoned about. A\nline comment sits above the first head, because both overloads return\nthe same type and no test would catch a swap.\n\nThe cost is one rule, and it took three rounds of measurement to state\nit as a rule instead of a list: link carries two signatures, and\nanything that reduces it back to one -- an assignment to a narrower\nsignature, generic inference, a utility type -- lands on the callback\nsignature. The docs give four faces of that rule as examples and say so:\na call whose target is statically a union mixing callback and signal, a\ngeneric pass-through written as a call signature, link passed as a bare\nvalue against a monomorphic signature, and Parameters<typeof link>. Each\nround of \"here are the N shapes that break\" was short by one.\n\nThe two unannotated callback examples in docs/recipes.md are untouched.\nThey did not compile under noImplicitAny before this; they do now.\n\nWitnessed twice, in src/ under tsc and in the smoke test against the\nshipped declarations -- with a positive check that v is the source''s\nvalue type, not merely that TS7006 is gone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"9fc2dc6423e63f8fcc967ef8e0312c107174519e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/9fc2dc6423e63f8fcc967ef8e0312c107174519e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/0e4299da1748bb3c43cb5ea900fe457a89ea76fc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/0e4299da1748bb3c43cb5ea900fe457a89ea76fc","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDBlNDI5OWRhMTc0OGJiM2M0M2NiNWVhOTAwZmU0NTdhODllYTc2ZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/5dc66d7badd39cdd805f41a9042c1b17ec88ec28","sha":"5dc66d7badd39cdd805f41a9042c1b17ec88ec28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/5dc66d7badd39cdd805f41a9042c1b17ec88ec28"}],"sha":"0e4299da1748bb3c43cb5ea900fe457a89ea76fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/0e4299da1748bb3c43cb5ea900fe457a89ea76fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/5dc66d7badd39cdd805f41a9042c1b17ec88ec28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T08:44:52Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T08:44:52Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"fix(types): refuse a lazy value write and an async hibernate at compile time (BUG-014, ASYNC-004)\n\nset(5, {lazy: true}) type-checked, stored the value where the factory\nbelongs, and left the next read to die with \"TypeError: this.valueFn is\nnot a function\" -- in whatever effect happened to read first. The value\noverload now carries the mirror of the factory overload''s condition, so\na statically true lazy closes it.\n\nInferring P from the params literal costs the excess-property check, and\nthat check is what catches {lasy: true}: the typo one keystroke away\nfrom the flag this fix is about. So the value branch also names its keys\nexactly, via Record<Exclude<keyof P, keyof SignalWriterParams<T>>,\nnever>, guarded by three branches that let an index signature through\nuntouched -- string, number and symbol each measured as their own hole,\neach with its own witness in the spec.\n\nNine call shapes that used to compile no longer do, all of them a params\ntype whose key set reaches past keyof SignalWriterParams<T>. They are\nlisted in the JSDoc, in docs/api.md, in recipes, in pitfalls 4a and in\nthe changelog, each with the repair that was measured to work: name the\nparams type. A spread repairs none of them. The trade was put to the\nmaintainer and taken deliberately -- a loud error with a one-line fix\nbeats a silent {lasy: true} at the most-used signature in the library.\n\nhibernate() gets the signature beQuiet() has had since the last run:\n() => NonThenable<T>. An async callback returns its pending promise at\nthe first await, the finally restores the saved batch, quiet counter and\neffect stack right there, and everything past that await runs outside\nthe hibernation it appears to be inside. The one call shape that breaks\nnew -- the generic pass-through -- is the same edge beQuiet() already\ncarries, measured, not assumed.\n\nBoth fixes are witnessed twice: in src/ under tsc, and in the smoke test\nagainst the shipped declarations, which is where the audit measured them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"ca739896ba30b4de9c3fdae02ba09c64708b784c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/ca739896ba30b4de9c3fdae02ba09c64708b784c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/5dc66d7badd39cdd805f41a9042c1b17ec88ec28","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/5dc66d7badd39cdd805f41a9042c1b17ec88ec28","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDVkYzY2ZDdiYWRkMzljZGQ4MDVmNDFhOTA0MmMxYjE3ZWM4OGVjMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/4d467935661bbe00c9faa23ec887de35b2897fe0","sha":"4d467935661bbe00c9faa23ec887de35b2897fe0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/4d467935661bbe00c9faa23ec887de35b2897fe0"}],"sha":"5dc66d7badd39cdd805f41a9042c1b17ec88ec28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/5dc66d7badd39cdd805f41a9042c1b17ec88ec28"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/4d467935661bbe00c9faa23ec887de35b2897fe0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T07:31:20Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T07:31:20Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"fix: let an empty memo name mean no name in both branches (CONS-015)\n\ncreateMemo(fn, {name: ''''}) took two different answers out of two tests\nsix lines apart. The attach branch asked `if (options?.name)` and fell\nthrough to attachSignal(), filing the memo unnamed -- right, but\nsilently. The branch without attach asked `!= null`, so it reported an\nignored option for a name that was never there.\n\nOne normalization up front settles both: `options?.name || undefined`,\nwhich is exactly the rule decorators.ts has been applying with\n`options?.name || context.name`. The empty string is the only falsy\nvalue the `string | symbol` type admits beyond null and undefined, so\nSymbol('''') stays a name -- symbols are always truthy.\n\nThe witness is the branch that was wrong: {name: ''''} without attach now\nreports nothing. The other test pins the branch that was already right,\nagainst a later cleanup that would pass '''' on to attachSignalByName().\n\nFive doc sites said the old thing and now say this one. decorators.ts\ngets no code -- its `||` already spelled the rule out; it gets a JSDoc\nline and a test, so a later switch to `??` cannot flip the convention\nwithout turning something red.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"ffaf062956c7fa1c13d5891bcd41085873176c29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/ffaf062956c7fa1c13d5891bcd41085873176c29"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/4d467935661bbe00c9faa23ec887de35b2897fe0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/4d467935661bbe00c9faa23ec887de35b2897fe0","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDRkNDY3OTM1NjYxYmJlMDBjOWZhYTIzZWM4ODdkZTM1YjI4OTdmZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/09af8ec9501e57e1ae93f9f2a2c51f1dd6cf73da","sha":"09af8ec9501e57e1ae93f9f2a2c51f1dd6cf73da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/09af8ec9501e57e1ae93f9f2a2c51f1dd6cf73da"}],"sha":"4d467935661bbe00c9faa23ec887de35b2897fe0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/4d467935661bbe00c9faa23ec887de35b2897fe0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/09af8ec9501e57e1ae93f9f2a2c51f1dd6cf73da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T07:17:28Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T07:17:28Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"fix: hold the teardown together when an unsubscribe throws, and release displaced automap entries (CONS-005, MEM-012)\n\nclear() promised to dismantle the group \"to the end and deregister it\",\nand four of its five teardown loops backed that up with a collect().\nThe fifth -- the sweep over #signalDestroySubscriptions -- did not, so a\nthrowing unsubscribe escaped before #groups.clear(), before the parent\ndetach, before store.delete(key). It now collects like the four above\nit. #dropSignalSubscription() takes its own bookkeeping out of both\nregisters in a finally, so a throwing handle no longer leaves a dead\nentry in the map and the held-resources set.\n\nThe witness for that loop needs an entry that survives loop three, and\nonly one shape produces it: a destroy-queue listener registered before\nthe group''s own that throws first, so the group''s bookkeeping listener\nnever gets its turn. SignalLink registers exactly that way. The seam is\na wrapped on() that hands back a throwing handle for a marked id on\nglobalDestroySignalQueue alone -- matching on the id would also catch\nthe value/effect subscriptions, since a signal id is an event on both\nglobal queues.\n\nfromProps(obj, propKeys) deduplicates propKeys before the create loop.\nA key named twice used to build a second signal over the first, and the\ndisplaced one kept its destroy-queue subscription with nothing left\nholding its key: clear() and delete() could not reach it, and it stayed\nin getSignalsCount() until the process ended.\n\nThe guard the plan also asked for -- release a taken key inside\n#create() -- is not here. With the dedup in place and get() behind its\nhas() check, #create() cannot be reached with a live key, and the dead\nbranch fails the 100% gate this file is held to.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"a722c84a63362173e8f59bdacb6f31a5c38f740f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/a722c84a63362173e8f59bdacb6f31a5c38f740f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/09af8ec9501e57e1ae93f9f2a2c51f1dd6cf73da","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/09af8ec9501e57e1ae93f9f2a2c51f1dd6cf73da","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDA5YWY4ZWM5NTAxZTU3ZTFhZTkzZjlmMmEyYzUxZjFkZDZjZjczZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/1ab6b402a92b8ec3bba8a9471a5c566804a49477","sha":"1ab6b402a92b8ec3bba8a9471a5c566804a49477","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/1ab6b402a92b8ec3bba8a9471a5c566804a49477"}],"sha":"09af8ec9501e57e1ae93f9f2a2c51f1dd6cf73da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/09af8ec9501e57e1ae93f9f2a2c51f1dd6cf73da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/1ab6b402a92b8ec3bba8a9471a5c566804a49477/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T06:46:57Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T06:46:57Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"docs: record the 2026-08-12 follow-up audit\n\nScore 68.0, up from a raw -130.5 that the scale had clamped to zero.\nNot a change in depth: the same scope was read as last time, plus the 54\nlow/info points that were never commissioned, each re-checked against\nthe code. Seven of them fell away.\n\nNo critical, no high. What is left splits in two: 28 findings in the\nruntime core -- four medium, twenty-four low -- and 20 in the project\nharness, where the doc gate goes unlinted and pnpm audit lists five\nadvisories, all in devDependency chains.\n\nThree open questions carry over, the sharpest being that the moment\n1.0.0-dev loses its suffix is also the moment main publishes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"3e7a56c39f65b223745cba2997f0cb3a90a166cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/3e7a56c39f65b223745cba2997f0cb3a90a166cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/1ab6b402a92b8ec3bba8a9471a5c566804a49477","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/1ab6b402a92b8ec3bba8a9471a5c566804a49477","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDFhYjZiNDAyYTkyYjhlYzNiYmE4YTk0NzFhNWM1NjY4MDRhNDk0Nzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/dc18245e488dfb2365f95b45c9882c34902d444d","sha":"dc18245e488dfb2365f95b45c9882c34902d444d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/dc18245e488dfb2365f95b45c9882c34902d444d"}],"sha":"1ab6b402a92b8ec3bba8a9471a5c566804a49477","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/1ab6b402a92b8ec3bba8a9471a5c566804a49477"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/dc18245e488dfb2365f95b45c9882c34902d444d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T21:29:08Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T21:29:08Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"docs: close out the remediation run for the 2026-08-08 audit\n\nForty-one packages, forty-two commits, and all 71 findings in scope are\nclosed -- both critical, all seventeen high, all fifty-two medium.\nSeventy were fixed. One, PERF-008, was measured out of existence: the\ndelivery frame it wanted to skip costs 2.1% at most, and the counter the\naudit recommended costs 17.2%.\n\nNo version bump. package.json says 1.0.0-dev and publishPackage.cjs\nrefuses to publish while it does -- that is a deliberate gate, not a\nneglected field, and the next version is already named. Releasing is the\nmaintainer''s call. The run is breaking either way: an export removed,\ntype parameters tightened until previously valid consumer code stops\ncompiling, beQuiet() returning a value, and two paths that throw where\nthey used to return quietly. Forty-one breaking changes are listed, in\nthe order a migrator reads them.\n\nThe plan goes in as it stands, endstate and all. What it is worth\nkeeping for is the section listing what this run did not clean up:\nfifteen things found in the code along the way, none of them in scope,\nthree of them traps for the next audit rather than for the library --\namong them the bench harness noise floor of two to five per cent, which\nis what PERF-008 died on, and an identifier that means two different\nthings on either side of an audit boundary.\n\naudit.html is untouched. The follow-up run verifies against the code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"2187259647b14dd740b18a906b299e7bdb245a59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/2187259647b14dd740b18a906b299e7bdb245a59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/dc18245e488dfb2365f95b45c9882c34902d444d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/dc18245e488dfb2365f95b45c9882c34902d444d","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKGRjMTgyNDVlNDg4ZGZiMjM2NWY5NWI0NWM5ODgyYzM0OTAyZDQ0NGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/5624c72a24f24de56e7f0f73a721a7a1386ba673","sha":"5624c72a24f24de56e7f0f73a721a7a1386ba673","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/5624c72a24f24de56e7f0f73a721a7a1386ba673"}],"sha":"dc18245e488dfb2365f95b45c9882c34902d444d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/dc18245e488dfb2365f95b45c9882c34902d444d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/5624c72a24f24de56e7f0f73a721a7a1386ba673/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T21:25:01Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T21:25:01Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"docs(changelog): put the breaking changes where a migrator looks first (CONS-008)\n\nThe Unreleased block holds 224 entries, and the 41 things that break a\nconsumer''s build sat below 104 bug fixes. They are the first section\nnow, uninterrupted, each one self-contained with its finding id -- a\nmigrator scanning only that section gets the whole list.\n\nThe bug fixes are bucketed by the API their first sentence changes:\neffects and memos, links, SignalGroup, batching, signals and counters.\nEach bucket keeps its own chronological order, so nothing about when\nsomething happened was lost.\n\nNothing was reworded that carried a claim, and the breaking changes\nwere not shortened -- their length is the migration guide. Six entries\noutside that section lost a trailing clause, and eleven continuations\ngot their own subject so they can be read where they now stand.\n\nVerified two ways: byte-identical from v0.31.1 onward, and the entry\nmultiset before and after differs in exactly the intended edits, with\nno entry added or dropped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"298afd53fcbf09e606936d886d663595d9f5fa05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/298afd53fcbf09e606936d886d663595d9f5fa05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/5624c72a24f24de56e7f0f73a721a7a1386ba673","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/5624c72a24f24de56e7f0f73a721a7a1386ba673","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDU2MjRjNzJhMjRmMjRkZTU2ZTdmMGY3M2E3MjFhN2ExMzg2YmE2NzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/a4c0568d00a70023e357cf6ae3f56a433e873b58","sha":"a4c0568d00a70023e357cf6ae3f56a433e873b58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/a4c0568d00a70023e357cf6ae3f56a433e873b58"}],"sha":"5624c72a24f24de56e7f0f73a721a7a1386ba673","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/5624c72a24f24de56e7f0f73a721a7a1386ba673"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/a4c0568d00a70023e357cf6ae3f56a433e873b58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T21:09:54Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T21:09:54Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"docs(changelog): make the Unreleased entries say what actually happened (CONS-008, CONS-009, API-016)\n\nThirty-nine commits landed in one Unreleased block, and it had drifted\nin four ways. Six entries described a state that a later entry in the\nsame block undoes -- link teardown counted as leaking its queue\nsubscriptions, which MEM-001 had already fixed twelve entries above.\nTwo numbers were wrong: two GC spec files where there are four, a\ntarball of 42 files where it is 48. Four breaking changes were missing\nentirely, among them beQuiet() changing from void to T and the\nAggregateError shape a write now throws when several effects fail. And\none entry described a method change that never shipped.\n\nEach correction is anchored to the commit or the code it describes,\nbecause nothing in this repository reads this file: biome takes only\nsource, check:refs skips it by design, no script parses it. It does\nship, though -- it is in package.json#files -- so a wrong number here\ntravels.\n\nThe identifier collisions are disambiguated where an identifier really\nmeans two things in this block, and not otherwise. Stamping the rest\nwould have meant guessing: the rule of thumb that an undated id is\npre-run is disproven by two entries, and no evidence distinguishes the\nthree earlier audits for the ones that remain.\n\nNothing at or below v0.31.1 was touched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"abe29268d1a06bae0ecf907dda7a38531f40f14a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/abe29268d1a06bae0ecf907dda7a38531f40f14a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/a4c0568d00a70023e357cf6ae3f56a433e873b58","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/a4c0568d00a70023e357cf6ae3f56a433e873b58","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKGE0YzA1NjhkMDBhNzAwMjNlMzU3Y2Y2YWUzZjU2YTQzM2U4NzNiNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/a5781c8509017247ec4f473ab9844e3a44fd034a","sha":"a5781c8509017247ec4f473ab9844e3a44fd034a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/a5781c8509017247ec4f473ab9844e3a44fd034a"}],"sha":"a4c0568d00a70023e357cf6ae3f56a433e873b58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/a4c0568d00a70023e357cf6ae3f56a433e873b58"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/a5781c8509017247ec4f473ab9844e3a44fd034a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T20:36:22Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T20:36:22Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"docs: keep the comments that still carry their weight, drop the ones that only look like it (READ-010, READ-012)\n\nSeven comment passages went. None of them was the last record of\nanything: each was checked against where else the claim lives, and in\ntwo cases the surviving text argues it more fully than the one deleted.\nWhat went are percentages standing in for arguments -- \"12 of 14\ncovered\", \"which the config holds at 100%\" -- where the reasoning\nunderneath survives untouched, and a lifetime note repeated for the\nfourth time three screens from its source.\n\nlink.ts carried two contradictory timings for the same operation, and\nthe reason turns out to be neither wrong: measured over five processes,\nthere are three regimes, not one. 59 microseconds warm; 96 for a signal\nwritten for the first time in a process that is otherwise warm; half a\nmillisecond as the first thing a fresh process does. The old 75, 116\nand 600 are one per regime, in that order, each 20-30% above what its\nown regime measures today. They never contradicted each other -- they\nanswered three questions while all claiming to answer one.\n\nREAD-012 asked for less comment. It gets more: 1.151 to 1.162, because\nthe PERF-008 measurement had nowhere else to live, and the whole point\nof a comment like that is that it is the only record in the published\npackage. The audit''s premise had already been measured wrong before\nthis package started.\n\nlink(sig, (v) => ...) still types v as any, and that stays: the fix is\nan overload pair, which is an API decision and not a documentation one.\nThe behaviour and its workaround are written down instead.\n\nSame 596 tests, same 8/23/1/6 uncovered units.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"7fe35c1793b384cff26d1f8e38d23735622e1808","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/7fe35c1793b384cff26d1f8e38d23735622e1808"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/a5781c8509017247ec4f473ab9844e3a44fd034a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/a5781c8509017247ec4f473ab9844e3a44fd034a","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKGE1NzgxYzg1MDkwMTcyNDdlYzRmNDczYWI5ODQ0ZTNhNDRmZDAzNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/99ac38cc8605b63b74ee883b32e7405a585cdf99","sha":"99ac38cc8605b63b74ee883b32e7405a585cdf99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/99ac38cc8605b63b74ee883b32e7405a585cdf99"}],"sha":"a5781c8509017247ec4f473ab9844e3a44fd034a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/a5781c8509017247ec4f473ab9844e3a44fd034a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/99ac38cc8605b63b74ee883b32e7405a585cdf99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T20:15:57Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T20:15:57Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"docs: hold every number against its source, and stop citing line numbers (READ-009, CONS-010)\n\nThe benchmark file still quoted figures from 5cb75f4, and the coverage\nconfig still counted 411 tests where there are 596. Both now say what\nis true, or say nothing where a number was never worth keeping.\n\nThe line references got a different treatment. Outside the remediation\nplan there were 23 of them in the whole documentation, all in\nAGENTS.md, and 16 pointed at the wrong line -- one reference to\nEffectImpl.ts was carried forward twice by earlier packages and was\nalready stale each time it was touched. A notation that is 70% wrong is\nnot maintained, it is abandoned: symbol names replace them, and\nscripts/check-doc-refs.mjs refuses the pattern outright as part of\n`pnpm check`. The plan and the changelog are exempt; history is allowed\nto point at where things were.\n\nThe tarball figures make the same argument against themselves. The\nfirst measurement was already stale by the time the package finished,\nbecause the documentation being edited is itself in the tarball --\nappending ten comment lines to the README moves the kilobytes. So the\nkilobytes are gone and the file count stays, with a sentence saying\nwhich kind of number this file keeps and why.\n\nSame 596 tests, same 8/23/1/6 uncovered units.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"ce6ed92dee5447c39180a37d0afea5e73f3aa6ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/ce6ed92dee5447c39180a37d0afea5e73f3aa6ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/99ac38cc8605b63b74ee883b32e7405a585cdf99","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/99ac38cc8605b63b74ee883b32e7405a585cdf99","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDk5YWMzOGNjODYwNWI2M2I3NGVlODgzYjMyZTc0MDVhNTg1Y2RmOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/5ef939d0c3d8edd03feab6a4933a0e8941b3eee6","sha":"5ef939d0c3d8edd03feab6a4933a0e8941b3eee6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/5ef939d0c3d8edd03feab6a4933a0e8941b3eee6"}],"sha":"99ac38cc8605b63b74ee883b32e7405a585cdf99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/99ac38cc8605b63b74ee883b32e7405a585cdf99"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/5ef939d0c3d8edd03feab6a4933a0e8941b3eee6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T19:40:16Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T19:40:16Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"docs: make the API documentation say what the API does (API-005, API-009, API-010, API-015)\n\nTwo concept tables told readers to write `new SignalGroup()`, which has\nnot compiled since the constructor went private -- TS2673, measured.\ncreateMemo({name}) without {attach} dropped the name in silence; it\nreports now, through the channel package 24 built, with a source of its\nown. Three deprecated call sites carry a real @deprecated tag and reach\nlib/. And the seven members of Signal, the class a consumer touches\nmost, had no documentation at all: lib/Signal.d.ts went from one\ncomment to eight.\n\nDocumentation is the one thing in this repo no test touches, and this\nrun has shipped three sentences that were merely plausible. So every\nsentence here carries one of four kinds of proof: it compiles as a\nsnippet against lib/, an existing test asserts it by file and line, it\nshows up in the emitted .d.ts, or it is a count with its command. The\nreview checked the proofs rather than the claims, and found the one\nsentence that had slipped through: holding the onChange() handle is not\nthe only way to end that subscription -- inside an effect body the\ninternal effect is a child, and the parent takes it with the handle\nnever called. Measured, corrected, and hibernate() named as the way out.\n\nThe @deprecated tag on SignalReader forces an overload order: put the\ngood signature first and nine call sites break with TS2554. Deprecated\nfirst, and the tag still lands where an editor shows it.\n\nSame 8/23/1/6 uncovered units; two new tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"9da410e413d468c0995389de6ad674de91459f6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/9da410e413d468c0995389de6ad674de91459f6f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/5ef939d0c3d8edd03feab6a4933a0e8941b3eee6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/5ef939d0c3d8edd03feab6a4933a0e8941b3eee6","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDVlZjkzOWQwYzNkOGVkZDAzZmVhYjZhNDkzM2EwZTg5NDFiM2VlZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/2dded95f04c3d9ca017b7426da0e005d0d6f08e3","sha":"2dded95f04c3d9ca017b7426da0e005d0d6f08e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/2dded95f04c3d9ca017b7426da0e005d0d6f08e3"}],"sha":"5ef939d0c3d8edd03feab6a4933a0e8941b3eee6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/5ef939d0c3d8edd03feab6a4933a0e8941b3eee6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/2dded95f04c3d9ca017b7426da0e005d0d6f08e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T19:03:10Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T19:03:10Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"refactor: take EffectImpl.run() apart (READ-011, part 2 of 2)\n\n156 lines holding eleven instance fields and five locals in one frame,\nwhere the dynamic branch, the lifecycle and the snapshot/prune pairing\nwere only separable by reading all of it. The pairing is a\nTrackedReadScope now, with its own mayCommit(); the two branches are\nrunStaticCallback and runDynamicCallback. What stays in #run() is\nlifecycle -- guards, batch, depth, teardown -- and it is 91 lines.\n\nNothing else changed, and that is the whole claim. 57 lines moved word\nfor word, 40 are scaffolding, seven have no counterpart: four locals\nand the composite commit condition, which is now mayCommit() unchanged\ndown to the short-circuit order. No comment was deleted or reworded --\nwhat has gone stale is for the documentation package to decide.\n\nThe proof is not a green suite. Twelve of the orderings inside run()\nwere mutated one at a time before and after: each kills the same named\ntests, not merely the same number of them. The two orderings whose\nmutation never actually ran in the survey were run afterwards and both\nhave a witness too, including the one this refactor moves.\n\nMeasured on the hot path with an A/A control alongside: the control\nreads 2%, one session drags every case including an untouched control\ndown by 3%, the next session reverses the sign. The rollback threshold\n-- 5% median across two independent sessions, confirmed by p75 -- is\nnot met by any case, which is the honest way of saying the machine is\nlouder than the change.\n\nExactly equivalent: same 594 tests, same 8/23/1/6 uncovered units.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"4a92d2798f7d3b3b27d7ba2de3f9c0c7786493e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/4a92d2798f7d3b3b27d7ba2de3f9c0c7786493e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/2dded95f04c3d9ca017b7426da0e005d0d6f08e3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/2dded95f04c3d9ca017b7426da0e005d0d6f08e3","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDJkZGVkOTVmMDRjM2Q5Y2EwMTdiNzQyNmRhMGUwMDVkMGQ2ZjA4ZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/a34c4f6dfeba7d912abd6d6196f1eeac8bbb388f","sha":"a34c4f6dfeba7d912abd6d6196f1eeac8bbb388f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/a34c4f6dfeba7d912abd6d6196f1eeac8bbb388f"}],"sha":"2dded95f04c3d9ca017b7426da0e005d0d6f08e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/2dded95f04c3d9ca017b7426da0e005d0d6f08e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/a34c4f6dfeba7d912abd6d6196f1eeac8bbb388f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T18:28:16Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T18:28:16Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"test: pin down the one ordering promise in run() that had no witness (READ-011, part 1 of 2)\n\nBefore taking run() apart, twenty-three orderings inside it were\nmutated one at a time to find out what actually holds its equivalence.\nTwelve fall on a named test. Eight are genuinely order-independent.\nThree had no witness at all, and of those only one is observable\nthrough the public surface: `shouldRun = false` sits after the cleanup,\nso a cleanup that calls run() itself still finds the run due and gets\nits third pass. Move that line one statement earlier and the nested run\ndisappears in silence.\n\nIt has a test now, and the test earns its place: with the line moved,\nexactly one test fails, `expected 2 to be 3`, and no other.\n\nThe other two stay unwitnessed on purpose. The maxDepth guard behind\nthe depth increment only affects the instance that overflowed, and no\nfinding asks for more. Hoisting isTracking is unreachable from outside\nat all -- beQuiet and hibernate both restore it in a finally.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"868987cb97a9316fa8e0e2cf4d05b7d624a2c65f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/868987cb97a9316fa8e0e2cf4d05b7d624a2c65f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/a34c4f6dfeba7d912abd6d6196f1eeac8bbb388f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/a34c4f6dfeba7d912abd6d6196f1eeac8bbb388f","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKGEzNGM0ZjZkZmViYTdkOTEyYWJkNmQ2MTk2ZjFlZWFjOGJiYjM4OGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/010e9d49d8540f2f13e6a50b4542ba102a725aea","sha":"010e9d49d8540f2f13e6a50b4542ba102a725aea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/010e9d49d8540f2f13e6a50b4542ba102a725aea"}],"sha":"a34c4f6dfeba7d912abd6d6196f1eeac8bbb388f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/a34c4f6dfeba7d912abd6d6196f1eeac8bbb388f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/010e9d49d8540f2f13e6a50b4542ba102a725aea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:57:04Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:57:04Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"refactor: stop createSignal from dragging in the effect subsystem (ARCH-002)\n\nTwo edges pulled all of effects and EffectImpl into any bundle that\ntouched createSignal: the deprecated signalReader(callback) form, and\nSignal#onChange(). Both now go through a leaf module that effects.ts\nfills in on load. Measured against a freshly built dist/, a consumer\nimporting nothing but createSignal: 17,087 -> 10,539 bytes minified\n(-38.3%), 5,790 -> 3,868 gzipped, with EffectImpl gone from the output.\nBreaking one edge alone saves nothing -- that was measured too.\n\nHalf the audit''s reasoning does not survive the measurement. The other\nsubsystem it blames, SignalGroup, hangs off the attach option and stays\nregardless; only removing that option would move it, which no finding\nasks for. And a bundle using the full surface now pays for the\nindirection: +262 bytes minified, +1.0%. That is in the changelog next\nto the win.\n\nThis is the library''s second load-bearing top-level side effect, and\nunlike the sentinel from ARCH-001 it is not optional -- lose the\nassignment and onChange() throws. In the bundled dist/ it cannot be\nlost, which is what ships. In the multi-module lib/*.js form it can,\nand does: a bundler eliminates effects.js for its unused exports\nwithout noticing that its last line is what makes a surviving call\nwork. lib/*.js is not published -- files ships only lib/**/*.d.ts --\nand AGENTS.md now carries that as a constraint rather than a footnote.\n\nThe witness catches a missing registration, not a late one: delaying it\nby a microtask leaves every test green while a consumer throws at module\ntop level. Verified, and the guard that would have caught it was built,\nmeasured never to fire under Vitest, and thrown away rather than shipped\nas false cover.\n\nExactly equivalent: same 8/23/1/6 uncovered units, onChange and the\ndeprecated form behave identically before and after.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"77a1c134c750a8271243abcd5eecca9c1c0adbd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/77a1c134c750a8271243abcd5eecca9c1c0adbd7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/010e9d49d8540f2f13e6a50b4542ba102a725aea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/010e9d49d8540f2f13e6a50b4542ba102a725aea","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDAxMGU5ZDQ5ZDg1NDBmMmYxM2U2YTUwYjQ1NDJiYTEwMmE3MjVhZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/69263694c851990915f278bf28adfc12ef5a5a46","sha":"69263694c851990915f278bf28adfc12ef5a5a46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/69263694c851990915f278bf28adfc12ef5a5a46"}],"sha":"010e9d49d8540f2f13e6a50b4542ba102a725aea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/010e9d49d8540f2f13e6a50b4542ba102a725aea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/69263694c851990915f278bf28adfc12ef5a5a46/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:15:16Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:15:16Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"feat: let two copies in one process notice each other (ARCH-001)\n\nLoad this library twice in the same process and the two halves run past\neach other in silence. isSignal() from copy B answers true for a signal\nfrom copy A, yet nothing propagates across the line -- and B''s\ndestroySignal() on A''s signal drives getSignalsCount() to -1. Every\npiece of shared state lives in module scope, so there is no shared\nstate at all.\n\nA leaf module registers each copy under a Symbol.for key on globalThis.\nMore than one entry and the second load reports it through the channel\npackage 24 built: level error, source ''multiple-instances'', naming both\nload paths. A message, never a throw -- the situation is a packaging\nmistake to be fixed, not a reason to refuse to start.\n\nDeduplicating the state itself was the audit''s first suggestion and is\nnot what this does: it spans eleven modules and trades a clean warning\nfor an undocumented protocol between two versions that have never met.\n\nThe registration is wrapped, because a sentinel that breaks `import` is\nthe worst version of this. Three states were measured where the naive\nform throws instead of warning -- a squatter on the key, a frozen array,\na frozen globalThis under SES lockdown. All three now fail silently: the\nlibrary works identically without the register, and the only channel\navailable during module evaluation is a console.error nobody in a\nhardened realm can turn off.\n\nConsequence recorded rather than papered over: sideEffects: false is no\nlonger strictly true. Measured, Rollup and Vite keep the assignment, and\nthe only path that drops the sentinel takes no export that reaches the\nreporter -- 19 of 33, none of them load-bearing.\n\nExactly equivalent: same 8/23/1/6 uncovered units.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"272839b28c5b494bac70a810ceca205e83573e40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/272839b28c5b494bac70a810ceca205e83573e40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/69263694c851990915f278bf28adfc12ef5a5a46","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/69263694c851990915f278bf28adfc12ef5a5a46","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDY5MjYzNjk0Yzg1MTk5MDkxNWYyNzhiZjI4YWRmYzEyZWY1YTVhNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/fed3ef17ba516616f17d99aca79c67041911bbab","sha":"fed3ef17ba516616f17d99aca79c67041911bbab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/fed3ef17ba516616f17d99aca79c67041911bbab"}],"sha":"69263694c851990915f278bf28adfc12ef5a5a46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/69263694c851990915f278bf28adfc12ef5a5a46"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/fed3ef17ba516616f17d99aca79c67041911bbab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T16:41:32Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T16:41:32Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"refactor: let the value-import graph say what it is (ARCH-003)\n\nThirteen import statements across eight files pulled in names that only\never appear in type position. The bundler cannot know that, so the value\ngraph carried edges nobody meant to draw: one strongly connected\ncomponent of twelve modules with five direct two-cycles. Marked as\n`import type`, that component is gone -- zero cycles.\n\nNothing about this is visible at runtime, which is exactly the point:\nthe change is correct if and only if the emitted output does not move.\nIt does not. dist/ is byte-identical, and in lib/ only the eight .d.ts\nfiles differ (they now say `import type`) plus one source map, whose .js\ncompares equal byte for byte.\n\n`style/useImportType` goes from off to error so the next such import is\ncaught by the linter rather than by an audit two years from now. It was\noff by omission, not by intent -- unlike the five rules this project\ndisables on purpose.\n\nOne thing the audit got wrong is worth recording: it offers\nSignalGroup <-> types.ts as the example of a back-edge that would return\nthe cycle if it used a value import. Measured, it does not, and it\ncannot -- that back-edge imports interfaces with no runtime\nrepresentation at all. AGENTS.md now carries a pair that does\n(globalEffectStack <-> EffectImpl), with the error rollup actually\nprints.\n\nExactly equivalent: same 8/23/1/6 uncovered units, same 583 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"db1a36b3ce56ddfa5e8e0c1c421d729f00358278","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/db1a36b3ce56ddfa5e8e0c1c421d729f00358278"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/fed3ef17ba516616f17d99aca79c67041911bbab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/fed3ef17ba516616f17d99aca79c67041911bbab","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKGZlZDNlZjE3YmE1MTY2MTZmMTdkOTlhY2E3OWM2NzA0MTkxMWJiYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/81c37cfac37ce50bc90db9da4a674f7b77b605fd","sha":"81c37cfac37ce50bc90db9da4a674f7b77b605fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/81c37cfac37ce50bc90db9da4a674f7b77b605fd"}],"sha":"fed3ef17ba516616f17d99aca79c67041911bbab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/fed3ef17ba516616f17d99aca79c67041911bbab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/81c37cfac37ce50bc90db9da4a674f7b77b605fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T16:00:01Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T16:00:01Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"feat: give the errors nobody could catch a channel of their own (CONS-001)\n\nA failure had three ways out of this library: throw, onEffectError, or\nconsole.error. The third one is not a channel, it is a dead end -- and\nit carried nine call sites, among them the group and link finalizers,\na deprecation notice and the thousand-links warning. Nothing running in\na FinalizationRegistry callback could be routed anywhere at all.\n\nonSignalizeError(cb, priority?) is that route. It carries a payload\nnaming its level, its source and the original error, so a host can log\nteardown failures where it logs everything else.\n\nWith no handler registered nothing changes, and that is the promise the\npackage stands on: same console method, same arguments, same order,\nsame count. It was measured against the built lib/ rather than against\na test count -- a warn that quietly became an error, or two arguments\nthat became one, is a break no green suite would show. All 575 existing\ntests pass untouched.\n\nA handler that throws never rethrows: reportSignalizeError has one exit\nand swallows the emit, verified inside a real FinalizationRegistry\ncallback under --expose-gc. Its own failure goes to console.error, the\noriginal payload follows on the method its level names.\n\nEvery new test was checked by taking the channel back out again, and\none mutation earned its keep: shortening write(message, error) to\nwrite(message) turns eight tests red, five of them pre-existing.\n\nExactly equivalent: same 8/23/1/6 uncovered units.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"d9099a63e4a0f2b7f2125b22114f78d394bebadc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/d9099a63e4a0f2b7f2125b22114f78d394bebadc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/81c37cfac37ce50bc90db9da4a674f7b77b605fd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/81c37cfac37ce50bc90db9da4a674f7b77b605fd","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDgxYzM3Y2ZhYzM3Y2U1MGJjOTBkYjlkYTRhNjc0ZjdiNzdiNjA1ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/715c10cdaab23d288ad1d2ac247f8d8e8e0e1a85","sha":"715c10cdaab23d288ad1d2ac247f8d8e8e0e1a85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/715c10cdaab23d288ad1d2ac247f8d8e8e0e1a85"}],"sha":"81c37cfac37ce50bc90db9da4a674f7b77b605fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/81c37cfac37ce50bc90db9da4a674f7b77b605fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/715c10cdaab23d288ad1d2ac247f8d8e8e0e1a85/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T15:15:40Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T15:15:40Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"types: keep the signal and link surface narrow (API-006, API-007, API-008)\n\nindex.ts re-exported everything from types.ts with a star, which put\nISignalImpl -- the implementation view, symbol keys and all -- into the\npublished surface, and SignalLink.source handed a whole one out. source\nis a four-member LinkSource view now, and the star is an explicit list\nof eighteen names. $signal stays internal and the docs say so rather\nthan leaving it to be discovered. And destroyed, which EffectImpl and\nSignalLink have carried all along, is now on Signal and Effect too.\n\nNarrowing source has a side effect worth having: SignalLink<T> loses\nits contravariant position and becomes covariant, which takes back the\nbreak package 20 caused for `const l: SignalLink = link(s, cb)`. Both\ndirections are in one changelog entry.\n\nThe named list is the part with no safety net. A type left out of it\nsilently leaves the published surface and nothing in `pnpm world` says\na word -- the only witness is the @ts-expect-error in\ntypes.public-surface.spec.ts. The obvious alternative, @internal plus\nstripInternal, was measured and rejected: it emits a lib/ carrying\nTS2304 and TS2305, and no step of the gate reports that either.\nAGENTS.md now says why the list is a list.\n\nEach assertion was verified by reverting exactly one signature. Two of\nthe four reverts yield TS2551 rather than TS2578, and Effect#destroyed\nreported nothing at all until it got the two runtime tests it now has.\n\nExactly equivalent: same 8/23/1/6 uncovered units.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"61ad18f2b846d6f3356589105dec479be953fd6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/61ad18f2b846d6f3356589105dec479be953fd6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/715c10cdaab23d288ad1d2ac247f8d8e8e0e1a85","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/715c10cdaab23d288ad1d2ac247f8d8e8e0e1a85","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDcxNWMxMGNkYWFiMjNkMjg4YWQxZDJhYzI0N2Y4ZDhlOGUwZTFhODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/6681cbabcd6c4b6909caf3c159ea5627db6b16b4","sha":"6681cbabcd6c4b6909caf3c159ea5627db6b16b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/6681cbabcd6c4b6909caf3c159ea5627db6b16b4"}],"sha":"715c10cdaab23d288ad1d2ac247f8d8e8e0e1a85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/715c10cdaab23d288ad1d2ac247f8d8e8e0e1a85"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/6681cbabcd6c4b6909caf3c159ea5627db6b16b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T14:26:23Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T14:26:23Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"feat: make the effect surface usable from outside (API-001, API-002, API-003, API-004)\n\nFour things kept the effect API in-house. attachEffect() was typed on\nEffectImpl, so a consumer holding the public Effect wrapper got TS2740\nand every call site in this repo unwrapped through effect[$effect]\ninstead; it is generic in its argument now and unwraps internally. The\nonCreateEffect/onDestroyEffect subscribers took (...args: unknown[])\nbehind a @ts-ignore, handing the callback an implicit any; they now\nname their parameter and take priority second. The effect depth limit\nlived on EffectImpl, which is not exported, so nobody could raise it --\ngetMaxEffectDepth() and setMaxEffectDepth() do that without widening\nthe surface by a class. And five option types the overloads are built\nfrom were unexported, which made a wrapper around createEffect()\nunannotatable.\n\nattachEffect() also closes the hole package 14 left open: a destroyed\nEffect wrapper used to be accepted silently and stayed in the group.\nIt throws now, and memberCounts.effects goes back to 0. The destroyed\ngetter that would let callers ask the same question belongs to API-008\nand is not part of this.\n\nEffectOptions is exported and refused at the call site on purpose:\nnaming the wide shape is useful, passing it is not, because the runtime\npicks its branch from which key is present. The two narrow names are\nwhat a call site wants.\n\nNone of this is visible to the gate, as in the two packages before:\neverything compiles either way. The assertions in\ntypes.public-surface.spec.ts carry the proof, each verified by reverting\nexactly one signature -- including the one revert that yields no TS2578\nat all, but three errors at the positive assertions.\n\nExactly equivalent elsewhere: same 8/23/1/6 uncovered units.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"eed18d16a28c82bbfd1fb056346d75961e5e1099","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/eed18d16a28c82bbfd1fb056346d75961e5e1099"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/6681cbabcd6c4b6909caf3c159ea5627db6b16b4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/6681cbabcd6c4b6909caf3c159ea5627db6b16b4","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDY2ODFjYmFiY2Q2YzRiNjkwOWNhZjNjMTU5ZWE1NjI3ZGI2YjE2YjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/c600a00c8a27525c2647e5cac8b0455f62467f52","sha":"c600a00c8a27525c2647e5cac8b0455f62467f52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/c600a00c8a27525c2647e5cac8b0455f62467f52"}],"sha":"6681cbabcd6c4b6909caf3c159ea5627db6b16b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/6681cbabcd6c4b6909caf3c159ea5627db6b16b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/c600a00c8a27525c2647e5cac8b0455f62467f52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T13:39:10Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T13:39:10Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"types: close three signatures that promised what the code does not do (TYPE-002, TYPE-004, TYPE-005)\n\nset(fn) and createSignal(fn) accepted a function without {lazy: true},\nwhere the runtime stores it as the value rather than calling it. The\ntwo are now overloads discriminated on the value argument: a factory\nrequires params whose lazy is statically true, a plain value takes any\nparams. SignalAutoMap.update() took Map<any, unknown> and cast the key,\nand fromProps'' propKeys widened to (keyof P)[]; both are exact now. And\nthe @signal decorator declared its name as a property of the host while\ncasting five times internally to work around it -- the name is a plain\nstring | symbol, the casts are gone, and a function-valued accessor is\nstored rather than invoked.\n\nTwo of the three recommendations do not survive contact with the code.\nDiscriminating on the params alone breaks every call whose options are\na variable: SignalParams<T> carries lazy?: boolean, assignable to\nneither true nor false, so `const p: SignalParams<number> = {}` stopped\ncompiling in the plain value branch. Widening the guard to accept an\nunnarrowed boolean reopens the hole it was meant to close, because\nboolean extends boolean | undefined holds for every annotated variable.\nDiscriminating on the value argument does both jobs at once, measured\nagainst 15 forms that must be rejected and 23 that must not.\n\nBreaking: passing a factory with params held in a variable no longer\ncompiles, even when that variable holds {lazy: true}. Repair with an\ninline literal, `as const`, or an annotation carrying `& {lazy: true}` --\nspreading the params does not work, it keeps lazy?: boolean.\n\nNone of this is visible to the gate: after the change everything still\ncompiles, so the assertions in types.public-surface.spec.ts carry the\nproof. Each was verified by reverting exactly one signature and\nconfirming that exactly one directive reports TS2578.\n\nOne branch better covered than before: 8/23/1/6 uncovered units.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"d6c6e28fe8cc362818f81143e35fc814fa5a18ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/d6c6e28fe8cc362818f81143e35fc814fa5a18ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/c600a00c8a27525c2647e5cac8b0455f62467f52","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/c600a00c8a27525c2647e5cac8b0455f62467f52","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKGM2MDBhMDBjOGEyNzUyNWMyNjQ3ZTVjYWM4YjA0NTVmNjI0NjdmNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/0a5aa745e982ca21467b96744f2eb14fdaf40e57","sha":"0a5aa745e982ca21467b96744f2eb14fdaf40e57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/0a5aa745e982ca21467b96744f2eb14fdaf40e57"}],"sha":"c600a00c8a27525c2647e5cac8b0455f62467f52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/c600a00c8a27525c2647e5cac8b0455f62467f52"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/0a5aa745e982ca21467b96744f2eb14fdaf40e57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T12:28:24Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T12:28:24Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"types: default the published type parameters to unknown, and give back what was passed in (TYPE-001, TYPE-003)\n\nEvery published type parameter defaulted to any, so a bare SignalLike,\nSignalLink, ValueCallback or ISignalImpl silently opted its holder out\nof type checking. They default to unknown now. And attachSignal,\ndetachSignal, attachSignalByName, attachLink and detachLink threw the\ninput type away, handing back SignalLike<any> for a Signal<number>;\nthey are generic in their argument now and return it unchanged.\n\nThe audit''s recommendation does not build as written, measured twice:\nSignalLike<T> is invariant through compare?: CompareFunc<T>, so unknown\nat a parameter position rejects Signal<number> with TS2345, and the\nproposed constraint S extends SignalLike<unknown> rejects it too. The\ndefaults become unknown; the parameter positions stay explicitly <any>,\nwhich is now documented as the right spelling for callers as well.\n\nNone of this is visible to the gate: after the change every spec and\nevery benchmark still compiles clean -- the wrong variant is what tsc\ncatches, not the right one. src/types.public-surface.spec.ts is the\nwitness. Each of its assertions was verified by reverting exactly one\nsignature or default and confirming that exactly one directive reports\nTS2578, in both directions, so no assertion rides along on another.\n\nExactly equivalent at runtime: same 8/24/1/6 uncovered units before and\nafter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"6ab62cdd638f6d382b53b1b5a5cf19c62816d0ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/6ab62cdd638f6d382b53b1b5a5cf19c62816d0ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/0a5aa745e982ca21467b96744f2eb14fdaf40e57","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/0a5aa745e982ca21467b96744f2eb14fdaf40e57","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDBhNWFhNzQ1ZTk4MmNhMjE0NjdiOTY3NDRmMmViMTRmZGFmNDBlNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/9e76d8df3d5643671ef2d07ac3429ef97e9bbd00","sha":"9e76d8df3d5643671ef2d07ac3429ef97e9bbd00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/9e76d8df3d5643671ef2d07ac3429ef97e9bbd00"}],"sha":"0a5aa745e982ca21467b96744f2eb14fdaf40e57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/0a5aa745e982ca21467b96744f2eb14fdaf40e57"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/9e76d8df3d5643671ef2d07ac3429ef97e9bbd00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T11:48:59Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T11:49:23Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"perf: allocate the rarely used SignalGroup collections on first write (PERF-004)\n\nEvery group eagerly built eleven containers, nine of which stay empty in\nthe common case: a group that holds a handful of signals never touches\n#namedSignals, #otherSignals, #groups, #links or the four maps behind\nthem. The empty containers outweighed the group itself.\n\nNine fields now start out pointing at a shared, frozen stand-in and are\nreplaced by a real container on the first write, through one own* helper\nper kind. No read path changed — no optional chaining, no null checks,\nno `?? 0`. getGroupMemberCounts() still answers 0 rather than undefined,\nand the DESTROY hooks that run at Priority.Max, at the head of an\neventize delivery, can never touch a stand-in.\n\nMeasured against the compiled lib/, 100k retained instances, eight gc\npasses, median of three: an empty group 2513 -> 1081 bytes (-57%), a\ndecorator host 4414 -> 3822, an {attach} effect host 7222 -> 5790.\nCreating a fresh group gained 16% in the bench, within its own rme --\nthe package stands on the memory number, not that one.\n\nExactly equivalent: same 8/24/1/6 uncovered units before and after, plus\nfour new tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016d6gxyj1RJ6gLuJCKs9gdk","tree":{"sha":"8e592734ce66560f6ec69d700cac973718f37ad2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/8e592734ce66560f6ec69d700cac973718f37ad2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/9e76d8df3d5643671ef2d07ac3429ef97e9bbd00","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/9e76d8df3d5643671ef2d07ac3429ef97e9bbd00","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDllNzZkOGRmM2Q1NjQzNjcxZWYyZDA3YWMzNDI5ZWY5N2U5YmJkMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/7d262f3e501ed089a124d30f2ea123a1ba45f69a","sha":"7d262f3e501ed089a124d30f2ea123a1ba45f69a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/7d262f3e501ed089a124d30f2ea123a1ba45f69a"}],"sha":"9e76d8df3d5643671ef2d07ac3429ef97e9bbd00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/9e76d8df3d5643671ef2d07ac3429ef97e9bbd00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/7d262f3e501ed089a124d30f2ea123a1ba45f69a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T09:11:09Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T09:11:09Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"docs: bring the remediation plan up to date for handover\n\nAdds a handover section at the head: where the run stands after 25\ncommits, how to resume it, today''s baseline instead of the one from\nlauf-beginn, and the cross-package obligations that bind an open\npackage — the two counters package 18 has to serve, and the guard 13b\ndeliberately left for it.\n\nAlso records what this run found wrong with the audit itself: seven\nrecommendations that are refuted at the code, and two promises in the\nshipped docs that the code did not keep.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0118ZzF46Zk5ZqgFkvmm2vsw","tree":{"sha":"3678458cf04ad15b1dfbd7ee7ce8b4634cff218c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/3678458cf04ad15b1dfbd7ee7ce8b4634cff218c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/7d262f3e501ed089a124d30f2ea123a1ba45f69a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/7d262f3e501ed089a124d30f2ea123a1ba45f69a","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDdkMjYyZjNlNTAxZWQwODlhMTI0ZDMwZjJlYTEyM2ExYmE0NWY2OWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/f6d5b4d0ddcde88c76919d13926cc5462cb76c1c","sha":"f6d5b4d0ddcde88c76919d13926cc5462cb76c1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/f6d5b4d0ddcde88c76919d13926cc5462cb76c1c"}],"sha":"7d262f3e501ed089a124d30f2ea123a1ba45f69a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/7d262f3e501ed089a124d30f2ea123a1ba45f69a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/f6d5b4d0ddcde88c76919d13926cc5462cb76c1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T08:52:48Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T08:52:48Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"perf: three early returns on the hottest path (PERF-001, PERF-002, PERF-003)\n\ndestroyChildEffects() allocated an error array and called\nthrowCollectedErrors() on every rerun, including the overwhelming\nmajority that have no child effects at all. Batch#run() allocated a Set,\nan array and two catch-all subscriptions even when nothing was queued —\nthe normal case for a defensive batch(). And every effect run emitted\nits id on a queue whose only subscriber exists for the duration of a\nflush, so outside one the emit walked eventize''s delivery for zero\nlisteners.\n\nMeasured, interleaved A/B, median of five: write fanning out to ten\neffects 373,783 -> 510,935 ops/s, an empty batch() from 629 ns to 50 ns,\nand {batchWrites: true} without a dependent effect from a factor of\nthree down to within five per cent of the default.\n\nExactly equivalent: same 8/24/1/6 uncovered units before and after.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0118ZzF46Zk5ZqgFkvmm2vsw","tree":{"sha":"6565a0aedd6bd22cf50b23b0784a476211c39903","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/6565a0aedd6bd22cf50b23b0784a476211c39903"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/f6d5b4d0ddcde88c76919d13926cc5462cb76c1c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/f6d5b4d0ddcde88c76919d13926cc5462cb76c1c","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKGY2ZDViNGQwZGRjZGU4OGM3NjkxOWQxMzkyNmNjNTQ2MmNiNzZjMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/ec4a043738bd33857f66e63b8c55a8491691d238","sha":"ec4a043738bd33857f66e63b8c55a8491691d238","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/ec4a043738bd33857f66e63b8c55a8491691d238"}],"sha":"f6d5b4d0ddcde88c76919d13926cc5462cb76c1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/f6d5b4d0ddcde88c76919d13926cc5462cb76c1c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/ec4a043738bd33857f66e63b8c55a8491691d238/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T21:11:18Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T21:11:18Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"fix: make two API promises hold (API-014, CONS-007)\n\nSignalGroup.delete(group) only looked in the store, where a group made\nby findOrCreate(host) sits under host and not under itself — so the call\ndid nothing at all, while docs/architecture.md calls it the public\ndestructor. It now takes the group itself, like get() and findOrCreate()\nalready do. The deprecated destroy(group) is fixed by the same line.\n\ntouch({}) and value({}) threw the native spread error, which tells the\ncaller nothing. They now throw the same prefixed TypeError link() has\nthrown all along. An iterable non-signal used to fall through the spread\nand get undefined; it throws too.\n\nThe four silent no-ops stay silent, and getLinksCount() keeps answering\nzero — all five are written down in docs/api.md now, grouped by what\nthey actually do.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0118ZzF46Zk5ZqgFkvmm2vsw","tree":{"sha":"539e502a330d6e47a667ac5527600c62cb17ca24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/539e502a330d6e47a667ac5527600c62cb17ca24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/ec4a043738bd33857f66e63b8c55a8491691d238","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/ec4a043738bd33857f66e63b8c55a8491691d238","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKGVjNGEwNDM3MzhiZDMzODU3ZjY2ZTYzYjhjNTVhODQ5MTY5MWQyMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/69ec659db24f8b4150bda3c011ef33a9bba910f0","sha":"69ec659db24f8b4150bda3c011ef33a9bba910f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/69ec659db24f8b4150bda3c011ef33a9bba910f0"}],"sha":"ec4a043738bd33857f66e63b8c55a8491691d238","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/ec4a043738bd33857f66e63b8c55a8491691d238"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/69ec659db24f8b4150bda3c011ef33a9bba910f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T18:14:46Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T18:14:46Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"fix(batch): carry out an explicitly requested run, and read memos fresh (ASYNC-002, ASYNC-003)\n\neffect.run() on a {autorun: false} effect inside a batch was not\ndeferred, it was dropped: the flush emits RECALL, and [RECALL] only\ncalls run() if autorun. The effect now notes that it was asked, and\nthe note is consumed by the run, not by RECALL — otherwise it stays\narmed when the flush dedupes the RECALL away.\n\nA memo read inside a batch returned its pre-batch value, and one\ncreated inside a batch returned undefined. Its recompute now bypasses\nthe deferral, which is safe because the batch dedupes the write anyway.\n\nBoth have a boundary, and both are now documented and pinned: a memo\nstale only through another memo is not reached — reading the upstream\nfirst is the way out — and a memo that reads both a batched signal and\nanother memo recomputes twice instead of once.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0118ZzF46Zk5ZqgFkvmm2vsw","tree":{"sha":"b3905e29bf20f9f1a758b9561e0186a01aba124a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/b3905e29bf20f9f1a758b9561e0186a01aba124a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/69ec659db24f8b4150bda3c011ef33a9bba910f0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/69ec659db24f8b4150bda3c011ef33a9bba910f0","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDY5ZWM2NTlkYjI0ZjhiNDE1MGJkYTNjMDExZWYzM2E5YmJhOTEwZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/394dfc1c2eacf88872f48de29612f1a03a0a5ade","sha":"394dfc1c2eacf88872f48de29612f1a03a0a5ade","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/394dfc1c2eacf88872f48de29612f1a03a0a5ade"}],"sha":"69ec659db24f8b4150bda3c011ef33a9bba910f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/69ec659db24f8b4150bda3c011ef33a9bba910f0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/394dfc1c2eacf88872f48de29612f1a03a0a5ade/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T17:01:43Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T17:01:43Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"fix: armour the bookkeeping hooks against a throwing listener (MEM-009, MEM-010, MEM-011, CONS-006)\n\nattachEffect() and link() registered their bookkeeping hooks at normal\npriority, so an application listener with a higher one could throw and\nend the delivery before them. The group then kept a destroyed effect\nand its callback closure; the link registry kept a counter that never\ncame back down and handed the frozen, destroyed link to the next\nlink(source, sameTarget) — the one consequence a user actually sees.\nBoth hooks move to Priority.Max, like the one in attachLink().\n\nunlink(source) called destroy() unguarded, so one throwing listener left\nevery link it had not reached yet fully subscribed. It collects now.\n\nAnd attachEffect() rejects an already destroyed effect, the way its two\nsibling methods have all along.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0118ZzF46Zk5ZqgFkvmm2vsw","tree":{"sha":"dae3adc4d52c52ad03f5c1abd5db8a73ead3bf60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/dae3adc4d52c52ad03f5c1abd5db8a73ead3bf60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/394dfc1c2eacf88872f48de29612f1a03a0a5ade","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/394dfc1c2eacf88872f48de29612f1a03a0a5ade","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDM5NGRmYzFjMmVhY2Y4ODg3MmY0OGRlMjk2MTJmMWEwM2EwYTVhZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/3e7fd9c0e68b968f6acf5b3aeb9957ebbe9ca5d4","sha":"3e7fd9c0e68b968f6acf5b3aeb9957ebbe9ca5d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/3e7fd9c0e68b968f6acf5b3aeb9957ebbe9ca5d4"}],"sha":"394dfc1c2eacf88872f48de29612f1a03a0a5ade","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/394dfc1c2eacf88872f48de29612f1a03a0a5ade"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/3e7fd9c0e68b968f6acf5b3aeb9957ebbe9ca5d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T16:22:15Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T16:22:15Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"fix: take the creation back when the first run throws (P1, P2)\n\nNot from the audit — both surfaced while rewriting the effect specs in\npackage 7b, and were confirmed and measured at the code.\n\ncreateEffect() ran the first callback before the Effect wrapper escaped,\nso a throw left a counted EffectImpl, its globalEffectQueue subscription\nand two subscriptions per signal already read, with nobody holding any\nof it. The repo had known this for a while: effects.spec.ts carried a\nworkaround with a variable named `leaked`.\n\ncreateMemo() lost the memo signal on top, and its callback typically\nthrows before it reads anything, so the self-teardown never triggers.\n\nThe rollback is conditional: with {attach} a group holds the effect, so\nit survives and stays usable, as documented. Without it the creation is\ntaken back — collecting the teardown error rather than letting it\nreplace the one that caused all this.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0118ZzF46Zk5ZqgFkvmm2vsw","tree":{"sha":"301fb1104b125bd6616a837fc55d9bde31d6a075","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/301fb1104b125bd6616a837fc55d9bde31d6a075"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/3e7fd9c0e68b968f6acf5b3aeb9957ebbe9ca5d4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/3e7fd9c0e68b968f6acf5b3aeb9957ebbe9ca5d4","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDNlN2ZkOWMwZTY4Yjk2OGY2YWNmNWIzYWViOTk1N2ViYmU5Y2E1ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/0f8626edd3f3bbf12f4ee3077c1380ea8735af8b","sha":"0f8626edd3f3bbf12f4ee3077c1380ea8735af8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/0f8626edd3f3bbf12f4ee3077c1380ea8735af8b"}],"sha":"3e7fd9c0e68b968f6acf5b3aeb9957ebbe9ca5d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/3e7fd9c0e68b968f6acf5b3aeb9957ebbe9ca5d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/0f8626edd3f3bbf12f4ee3077c1380ea8735af8b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T14:57:21Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T14:57:21Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"fix: isolate the destroy delivery and guard every teardown step on its own (BUG-011, MEM-008)\n\ndestroySignal() emitted bare, so an effect whose cleanup threw ended the\ndelivery: every subscriber behind it was skipped, leaving a SignalLink\nattached to the dead source, a SignalGroup holding the dead SignalImpl\nand a SignalAutoMap entry standing.\n\nThe audit''s recommendation — open an isolation frame — fixes nothing on\nits own, measured: the frame collects, it does not catch, and on the\ndestroy path no listener had a catch. Both halves are needed, and either\none alone leaves the same two tests red.\n\nEffectImpl.destroy() ran four teardown steps in one try, so a throwing\nonDestroyEffect() handler cost the application its cleanup callback.\nEach step now collects on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0118ZzF46Zk5ZqgFkvmm2vsw","tree":{"sha":"7f228c8037fcbe4270ef0b9f5f1dc08b67c84450","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/7f228c8037fcbe4270ef0b9f5f1dc08b67c84450"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/0f8626edd3f3bbf12f4ee3077c1380ea8735af8b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/0f8626edd3f3bbf12f4ee3077c1380ea8735af8b","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDBmODYyNmVkZDNmM2JiZjEyZjRlZTMwNzdjMTM4MGVhODczNWFmOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/54be99ad6b01a457b54227ed3d34de94ae3e8de4","sha":"54be99ad6b01a457b54227ed3d34de94ae3e8de4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/54be99ad6b01a457b54227ed3d34de94ae3e8de4"}],"sha":"0f8626edd3f3bbf12f4ee3077c1380ea8735af8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/0f8626edd3f3bbf12f4ee3077c1380ea8735af8b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/54be99ad6b01a457b54227ed3d34de94ae3e8de4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T14:21:12Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T14:21:12Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"refactor: fold the error-collecting idiom into a helper (READ-001)\n\ntry { … } catch (err) { errors.push(err) } stood fifteen times word for\nword, eleven of them in SignalGroup#clear() and #off(), where the actual\nteardown order disappeared between the boilerplate. Each repetition was\na place where a forgotten catch quietly reinstalls an abort.\n\nFourteen sites now read collect(errors, () => step()). Two stay: the\nfour-statement try in EffectImpl.destroy() is finding MEM-008 and gets\ntaken apart in the next package, and batch.ts allocates its array lazily.\n\nNo behaviour change — the suite reports the same 509 tests and the same\n465/489 branches. Removing the catch from the helper turns 23 tests red.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0118ZzF46Zk5ZqgFkvmm2vsw","tree":{"sha":"d927276d7dd819142186d18e661963a231e7a8b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/d927276d7dd819142186d18e661963a231e7a8b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/54be99ad6b01a457b54227ed3d34de94ae3e8de4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/54be99ad6b01a457b54227ed3d34de94ae3e8de4","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDU0YmU5OWFkNmIwMWE0NTdiNTQyMjdlZDNkMzRkZTk0YWUzZThkZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/54cfb8779701d189e8c741293160c183de56c2e3","sha":"54cfb8779701d189e8c741293160c183de56c2e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/54cfb8779701d189e8c741293160c183de56c2e3"}],"sha":"54be99ad6b01a457b54227ed3d34de94ae3e8de4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/54be99ad6b01a457b54227ed3d34de94ae3e8de4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/54cfb8779701d189e8c741293160c183de56c2e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T13:39:39Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T13:39:39Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"fix: restore both frames that must survive a throwing callback (ASYNC-001, BUG-012)\n\nhibernate() flushed the saved batch before the try, so a throwing effect\nskipped all three restore calls in the finally. Batch and effect stack\nhappened to repair themselves; the beQuiet counter did not — it ended at\n-1, and every silent read stayed silent for nothing for the rest of the\nprocess. The flush moves into the try.\n\nbatch() let the flush error replace the callback error outright, the\ndocumented TypeError guard against thenable callbacks included. Both now\narrive as an AggregateError, callback first. A batch where only one side\nfails rethrows that error unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0118ZzF46Zk5ZqgFkvmm2vsw","tree":{"sha":"81049ab961135d4a87501dfc55bfdea10ecbef01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/81049ab961135d4a87501dfc55bfdea10ecbef01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/54cfb8779701d189e8c741293160c183de56c2e3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/54cfb8779701d189e8c741293160c183de56c2e3","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDU0Y2ZiODc3OTcwMWQxODllOGM3NDEyOTMxNjBjMTgzZGU1NmMyZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/8aa267d9c983c02578bb098a9ea7695d6dedc8ad","sha":"8aa267d9c983c02578bb098a9ea7695d6dedc8ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/8aa267d9c983c02578bb098a9ea7695d6dedc8ad"}],"sha":"54cfb8779701d189e8c741293160c183de56c2e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/54cfb8779701d189e8c741293160c183de56c2e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/8aa267d9c983c02578bb098a9ea7695d6dedc8ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T13:00:44Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T13:00:44Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"fix(link): stop asyncValues() from replaying the retained value at itself (ASYNC-005, READ-002, TEST-022)\n\neventize replays a retained value synchronously when a listener\nsubscribes, and does not clear the slot doing so. Every nextValue()\ntherefore resolved at once with the same value: a microtask hot loop\nthat yielded one value half a million times and never let a macrotask\nthrough. Both existing specs masked it, because both write from inside\nthe loop body.\n\nThe link now carries the generation of its last emit and a per-read\ncursor, so a replay the reader has already seen is ignored instead of\ndelivered. Measured: 500000 iterations and no timer, down to one\niteration and a timer that fires.\n\nClosing the iterator works again while a read is pending — asyncValues()\nreturns a facade whose return/throw cancel that read. That also fixes\nthe case that never worked, closing before the first value ever arrived.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0118ZzF46Zk5ZqgFkvmm2vsw","tree":{"sha":"3b7ce5d9665ac4fbdf88162238a6e054799da127","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/3b7ce5d9665ac4fbdf88162238a6e054799da127"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/8aa267d9c983c02578bb098a9ea7695d6dedc8ad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/8aa267d9c983c02578bb098a9ea7695d6dedc8ad","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDhhYTI2N2Q5Yzk4M2MwMjU3OGJiMDk4YTllYTc2OTVkNmRlZGM4YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/87dc940381ef91f3b452610d80acca08629d09a8","sha":"87dc940381ef91f3b452610d80acca08629d09a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/87dc940381ef91f3b452610d80acca08629d09a8"}],"sha":"8aa267d9c983c02578bb098a9ea7695d6dedc8ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/8aa267d9c983c02578bb098a9ea7695d6dedc8ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/87dc940381ef91f3b452610d80acca08629d09a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T11:52:23Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T11:52:23Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"test: widen every spec''s counter guards to all three resource kinds (part 2 of 2)\n\nA file that only asserted the effect count never noticed a leaked\nsignal or link. Twelve files gain signals and links, eleven gain links.\n\nFive stay short of the full set for a documented reason, now written\ndown at each describe head and codified in AGENTS.md: two whose whole\nsubject is a GC-timed counter, one that must leave a resource dangling\nto prove its point, one that creates nothing a counter could see, and\nthe one that tests the guards themselves — where wiring a guard in\nwould let a defect in the assertion hide itself.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0118ZzF46Zk5ZqgFkvmm2vsw","tree":{"sha":"02560601eec9054182ddbecb349c2800bea6aaae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/02560601eec9054182ddbecb349c2800bea6aaae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/87dc940381ef91f3b452610d80acca08629d09a8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/87dc940381ef91f3b452610d80acca08629d09a8","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDg3ZGM5NDAzODFlZjkxZjNiNDUyNjEwZDgwYWNjYTA4NjI5ZDA5YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/204e4304a56750f909d54f33416a4dfcfcec0c27","sha":"204e4304a56750f909d54f33416a4dfcfcec0c27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/204e4304a56750f909d54f33416a4dfcfcec0c27"}],"sha":"87dc940381ef91f3b452610d80acca08629d09a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/87dc940381ef91f3b452610d80acca08629d09a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/204e4304a56750f909d54f33416a4dfcfcec0c27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T11:18:33Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T11:18:33Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"test: bring the five guard-less specs under the net (part 1 of 2)\n\nThese five files carried no counter guard at all, and ten of their\ntests were leaking eight effects and eighteen signals without anyone\nnoticing. They were also never part of the TEST-017 sweep, so adding\nguards alone would have restored the collateral damage that sweep\nremoved — measured: createMemo.spec.ts at radius 16 with 43 offenders.\n\nSo both, in order: 34 new finally blocks first, then the guards. The\nprobe that counts leaked signals, effects and links per test now\nreports zero across the whole suite.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0118ZzF46Zk5ZqgFkvmm2vsw","tree":{"sha":"293697fc02294bd9714c555aa39583a3b067bc33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/293697fc02294bd9714c555aa39583a3b067bc33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/204e4304a56750f909d54f33416a4dfcfcec0c27","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/204e4304a56750f909d54f33416a4dfcfcec0c27","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDIwNGU0MzA0YTU2NzUwZjkwOWQ1NGYzMzQxNmE0ZGZjZmNlYzBjMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/55d7fb6f2c15cb1105a2b206a90db6df0ebdc042","sha":"55d7fb6f2c15cb1105a2b206a90db6df0ebdc042","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/55d7fb6f2c15cb1105a2b206a90db6df0ebdc042"}],"sha":"204e4304a56750f909d54f33416a4dfcfcec0c27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/204e4304a56750f909d54f33416a4dfcfcec0c27"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/55d7fb6f2c15cb1105a2b206a90db6df0ebdc042/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T09:47:04Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T09:47:04Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"test: cover the untested half of the core logic (TEST-020, TEST-023, TEST-024, TEST-025)\n\nTen mutations survived the suite until now. Eight are pinned by eight\nnew tests: three finalizer bookkeeping spots, the position of the\neffect generation bump, the three unguarded branches of createSignal(),\nand the name fallback in detachSignal() — each fails exactly one test\nat a body assertion, with no collateral.\n\nTwo are left untested on purpose. The wrapper delete in the resource\nfinalizer and the self-keyed-group registration skip have no observable\neffect of their own, and a test for either would be a flaky GC test,\nwhich is worse than none.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0118ZzF46Zk5ZqgFkvmm2vsw","tree":{"sha":"824da1be4dae48a23bcd72569440bf456b7c5336","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/824da1be4dae48a23bcd72569440bf456b7c5336"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/55d7fb6f2c15cb1105a2b206a90db6df0ebdc042","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/55d7fb6f2c15cb1105a2b206a90db6df0ebdc042","node_id":"C_kwDOGEOuPNoAKDU1ZDdmYjZmMmMxNWNiMTEwNWEyYjIwNmE5MGRiNmRmMGViZGMwNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf/signalize/commit/bc38958c25257dab7227f0d32c4fd7d9e61515dc","sha":"bc38958c25257dab7227f0d32c4fd7d9e61515dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/bc38958c25257dab7227f0d32c4fd7d9e61515dc"}],"sha":"55d7fb6f2c15cb1105a2b206a90db6df0ebdc042","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/55d7fb6f2c15cb1105a2b206a90db6df0ebdc042"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spearwolf","id":12805,"login":"spearwolf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spearwolf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/commits/bc38958c25257dab7227f0d32c4fd7d9e61515dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T08:46:39Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T08:46:39Z","email":"wolfger@spearwolf.de","name":"Wolfger Schramm"},"message":"test: pin down the SignalGroup re-entrancy guards and its teardown order (TEST-018, TEST-019)\n\nThree of the five BUSY_* bits and all three deliberately ordered\nteardown steps could be removed or swapped without a single test going\nred. Seven tests now observe the sequence rather than the end state: a\nDESTROY listener reads memberCounts at emit time, an effect cleanup\ncounts the signals still alive, and off() logs the order it walks.\n\nAlso restores a leak detector the finally sweep had absorbed:\nattachEffect() returns the effect asserts the effect count after\nclear() instead of relying on the afterEach guard, so the effect loop\nin SignalGroup#clear() has four real detectors again instead of two.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0118ZzF46Zk5ZqgFkvmm2vsw","tree":{"sha":"142476aaf378ce532a6146727e4050cc987db4ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/trees/142476aaf378ce532a6146727e4050cc987db4ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spearwolf/signalize/git/commits/bc38958c25257dab7227f0d32c4fd7d9e61515dc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committe