d","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-ora-grading/commits/7b2406908980ce9fcc935d6784143fbd80a6247e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T06:43:33Z","email":"waleed.mujahid@arbisoft.com","name":"waleed.mujahid"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:21:38Z","email":"waleed.mujahid@arbisoft.com","name":"waleed.mujahid"},"message":"fix(ReviewModal): remove obsolete \"Grading Demo\" title suffix\n\nThe review modal appended \"Grading Demo\" to the ORA name whenever\nisEnabled was true, which is inverted: isEnabled means the Enhanced\nStaff Grader waffle flag (openresponseassessment.enhanced_staff_grader)\nis on for the course, i.e. real grading. Every other consumer of the\nflag branches on !isEnabled (DemoWarning banner in App.jsx, submit\nblocking in Rubric/hooks.js).\n\nThe label dates from the 2022 ESG opt-in rollout, when the ORA staff\narea exposed a separate \"Demo the new Grading Experience\" link into a\nread-only MFE. That period ended and this MFE is now the default\ngrading experience, so the suffix and its message are removed rather\nthan flipped. Dropped the resulting dead isEnabled selector and intl\nplumbing, and replaced the test that codified the inverted behaviour.","tree":{"sha":"71bb693ac2e1b04e12aa12eae64060109dd17df6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-ora-grading/git/trees/71bb693ac2e1b04e12aa12eae64060109dd17df6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-ora-grading/git/commits/7b2406908980ce9fcc935d6784143fbd80a6247e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81019006?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Waleed-Mujahid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Waleed-Mujahid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Waleed-Mujahid/following{/other_u