979a9b5f4e0ff9cce1a32a364af03fba140","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/9e95e979a9b5f4e0ff9cce1a32a364af03fba140"}],"sha":"3e176767eff17a214eef66c0f5c42754b7508692","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/3e176767eff17a214eef66c0f5c42754b7508692"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1331872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mearman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mearman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mearman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mearman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Mearman","id":1331872,"login":"Mearman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMzE4NzI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mearman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mearman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mearman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mearman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mearman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mearman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/9e95e979a9b5f4e0ff9cce1a32a364af03fba140/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T14:18:55Z","email":"joseph@mearman.co.uk","name":"Joseph Mearman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T14:18:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: Upgrade Ghostty for Zig 0.17 (#14419)\n\n### Description\n\nZig 0.15.2 cannot link the Ghostty build runner against the macOS 26\nSDK. This retains the original PR''s macOS libc-symbol protection and\nupgrades the compiler, native library, and Rust bindings together to Zig\n0.17.\n\nZig 0.16 resolved the macOS SDK linking failure, but its native Windows\nARM64 compiler crashed with an access violation. Running the x64\ncompiler under emulation to produce ARM64 output then hit a\nstandard-library pointer-alignment compile error. This is why the\nupgrade moves to Zig 0.17 instead of stopping at 0.16.\n\n- Pin Zig to `0.17.0` and Ghostty to\n`5147c0a503cdeed7615cce245cdd815ed7a6b692`, from [Ghostty''s Zig 0.17\nmigration](https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty/pull/14519).\n- Pin the compatible Rust wrapper to\n`3c7766d4e5d6ce93870ad666a14c0b5a0e957360`, from [libghostty-rs\n#84](https://github.com/Uzaaft/libghostty-rs/pull/84), and update the\nlocal FFI bindings, signed enums, and binding generator.\n- Adapt terminal construction and scrollback configuration while\npreserving zero-scrollback behavior and the default byte cap for\npositive line limits.\n- Keep baseline CPU targeting and aligned macOS deployment targets.\nExplicitly pass Windows targets so compiler architecture and output\narchitecture need not match.\n- Localize libc symbols across archive members and fail if the guarded\nsymbols remain exported. Apply protection to build-owned output archives\nso `GHOSTTY_SOURCE_DIR` checkouts do not need to be rewritten.\n- Update CI, devcontainer, and factory Zig pins together. Remove\n`terminal-control` and use a focused test-only adapter around the\nexisting `portable-pty` and Ghostty dependencies for the black-box TUI\ntests. No vendored library, personal fork, or alternate terminal parser\nis required.\n\n```text\nZig 0.17.0\n  └─ Ghostty libghostty-vt @ 5147c0a5\n       └─ Local FFI bindings + Rust wrapper @ 3c7766d4\n            ├─ Turborepo TUI\n            └─ TUI tests: existing portable-pty + Ghostty\n```\n\nThe test-only adapter in `crates/turborepo/tests/common/tui.rs` handles\nonly the PTY lifecycle, Ghostty screen capture, terminal-query\nresponses, raw output, input, and resizing needed by these tests. All\nseven existing TUI scenarios retain their assertions, input actions, and\ndeadlines; only harness imports and plumbing change. Focused regressions\ncover color/escape parsing, query responses and final output, and\ntimeout/drop cleanup. Removing the library and its unused CLI, MCP, and\nimage-rendering dependency tree eliminates 52 lockfile packages.\nProduction and tests continue to use the same Ghostty wrapper and native\nlibrary. Most of the remaining added source is generated C bindings.\n\nBoth upstream dependency revisions are currently unmerged PR commits.\nThey are pinned by full commit ID rather than floating branches.\n\n### Manual verification\n\nA native ARM64 Windows executable was exercised in a Windows 11\nParallels VM through a real ConPTY session. Startup, task output,\ninteractive input, return to navigation, resizing, Ctrl-C shutdown, and\nalternate-screen restoration all worked.\n\nThe macOS source-override path was exercised with a fresh Ghostty\ncheckout. The build completed without changing its tracked source files.\n\nThe local Windows x64 Zig build-runner experiment under Windows-on-ARM\nemulation stalled and was stopped at the maintainer''s request; that\nexperiment is not presented as passing manual verification.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Anthony Shew <anthonyshew@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com>","tree":{"sha":"54547e11449a71bc83a3b0711bfd580771ba90bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/54547e11449a71bc83a3b0711bfd580771ba90bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/9e95e979a9b5f4e0ff9cce1a32a364af03fba140","verification":{"payload":"tree 54547e11449a71bc83a3b0711bfd580771ba90bc\nparent 828e0ffd57b53edfb40ed6543abb1939e7f45660\nauthor Joseph Mearman <joseph@mearman.co.uk> 1791469135 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791469135 -0600\n\nchore: Upgrade Ghostty for Zig 0.17 (#14419)\n\n### Description\n\nZig 0.15.2 cannot link the Ghostty build runner against the macOS 26\nSDK. This retains the original PR''s macOS libc-symbol protection and\nupgrades the compiler, native library, and Rust bindings together to Zig\n0.17.\n\nZig 0.16 resolved the macOS SDK linking failure, but its native Windows\nARM64 compiler crashed with an access violation. Running the x64\ncompiler under emulation to produce ARM64 output then hit a\nstandard-library pointer-alignment compile error. This is why the\nupgrade moves to Zig 0.17 instead of stopping at 0.16.\n\n- Pin Zig to `0.17.0` and Ghostty to\n`5147c0a503cdeed7615cce245cdd815ed7a6b692`, from [Ghostty''s Zig 0.17\nmigration](https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty/pull/14519).\n- Pin the compatible Rust wrapper to\n`3c7766d4e5d6ce93870ad666a14c0b5a0e957360`, from [libghostty-rs\n#84](https://github.com/Uzaaft/libghostty-rs/pull/84), and update the\nlocal FFI bindings, signed enums, and binding generator.\n- Adapt terminal construction and scrollback configuration while\npreserving zero-scrollback behavior and the default byte cap for\npositive line limits.\n- Keep baseline CPU targeting and aligned macOS deployment targets.\nExplicitly pass Windows targets so compiler architecture and output\narchitecture need not match.\n- Localize libc symbols across archive members and fail if the guarded\nsymbols remain exported. Apply protection to build-owned output archives\nso `GHOSTTY_SOURCE_DIR` checkouts do not need to be rewritten.\n- Update CI, devcontainer, and factory Zig pins together. Remove\n`terminal-control` and use a focused test-only adapter around the\nexisting `portable-pty` and Ghostty dependencies for the black-box TUI\ntests. No vendored library, personal fork, or alternate terminal parser\nis required.\n\n```text\nZig 0.17.0\n  └─ Ghostty libghostty-vt @ 5147c0a5\n       └─ Local FFI bindings + Rust wrapper @ 3c7766d4\n            ├─ Turborepo TUI\n            └─ TUI tests: existing portable-pty + Ghostty\n```\n\nThe test-only adapter in `crates/turborepo/tests/common/tui.rs` handles\nonly the PTY lifecycle, Ghostty screen capture, terminal-query\nresponses, raw output, input, and resizing needed by these tests. All\nseven existing TUI scenarios retain their assertions, input actions, and\ndeadlines; only harness imports and plumbing change. Focused regressions\ncover color/escape parsing, query responses and final output, and\ntimeout/drop cleanup. Removing the library and its unused CLI, MCP, and\nimage-rendering dependency tree eliminates 52 lockfile packages.\nProduction and tests continue to use the same Ghostty wrapper and native\nlibrary. Most of the remaining added source is generated C bindings.\n\nBoth upstream dependency revisions are currently unmerged PR commits.\nThey are pinned by full commit ID rather than floating branches.\n\n### Manual verification\n\nA native ARM64 Windows executable was exercised in a Windows 11\nParallels VM through a real ConPTY session. Startup, task output,\ninteractive input, return to navigation, resizing, Ctrl-C shutdown, and\nalternate-screen restoration all worked.\n\nThe macOS source-override path was exercised with a fresh Ghostty\ncheckout. The build completed without changing its tracked source files.\n\nThe local Windows x64 Zig build-runner experiment under Windows-on-ARM\nemulation stalled and was stopped at the maintainer''s request; that\nexperiment is not presented as passing manual verification.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Anthony Shew <anthonyshew@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx6ZPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcjMQAAMvu5x3vs80fGy3EltMJrri\nKHMsZYcPI0OI3oFH/YaBvihX7dFChs7zd0+Ohd8uQSV6K1GIcApYNl29RauOY8mm\nsMJA88qzV9RITw1LaAz9DjEGWSqlEsbaQs3H5nKtkZ8n+vqbfjk2IxNDh7lkIYgm\nDdU7evTzzZr3lnT7pjD5GvRhiFirPcQmUtaiyUuByZmS6LCq+36yoHFlvV1CSjsB\nr170yImNF6ZY0/Y2tvkq6pzNin8qMhe6RcyU108z+Uh7KZuSQPk0byqK+P/2akkz\nBr5+mYQypw5Rikrntli1Sy1FwF7xHp3qxAR+H7GVP4SeOYZj9yHS1lg3t48GFjfX\ntruN1obt/vlAAyculbGlCApPRfyOk4CHpGf8TTnNnS0Ty1frwRkcMx/H9gto0Wcx\nBQHCcwTqthXuj1OR3XYDLzWvipn5mEcgSa+yRrFIjRTpDgbe1vuV0O6w7jJIHtLr\nnV55T9MkN6P5KEIolxXgFlmJxw1jUv07MIfHxJ2QWx1Ppy1OxUpQc+h4FkqH085W\n9yfyWzVkHyYOKSHm7yFLcxGT1jfibLF5DLfeL3m/2saS9Qrw7QI6UsMRpwl+1kw8\ntdW4aN5GA06hctRVuap/GDpAB71wDWP3xC12VnzW7NDXlYXejhSeNO0xbYjWcW+m\nfkhlSqjlP8ztzv+rDTh4\n=dh26\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T14:18:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/9e95e979a9b5f4e0ff9cce1a32a364af03fba140","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDllOTVlOTc5YTliNWY0ZTBmZjljY2UxYTMyYTM2NGFmMDNmYmExNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/828e0ffd57b53edfb40ed6543abb1939e7f45660","sha":"828e0ffd57b53edfb40ed6543abb1939e7f45660","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/828e0ffd57b53edfb40ed6543abb1939e7f45660"}],"sha":"9e95e979a9b5f4e0ff9cce1a32a364af03fba140","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/9e95e979a9b5f4e0ff9cce1a32a364af03fba140"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/828e0ffd57b53edfb40ed6543abb1939e7f45660/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:03:53Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:03:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: Capture setup discovery context for revalidation (#14439)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdvance [TURBO-6324](https://linear.app/vercel/issue/TURBO-6324), the\ndiscovery-context prerequisite for frozen inventory publication.\n\n- Capture immutable invocation selectors, inferred root/config identity,\nfuture flags, and flag-gated toolchain eligibility.\n- Preserve the existing `setup root: <canonical root>` diagnostic\nthrough the captured discovery object, without changing inference or\nintegration assertions.\n- Re-run the same inference to detect nested config/workspace/Git\nboundary changes, identity drift, and changed eligibility while\npreserving root diagnostics.\n- Reject custom configuration paths outside snapshot coverage; keep\ndebug output redacted.\n\n```text\noriginal invocation selectors\n  -> captured Discovery\n  -> provisioning preparation\n  -> revalidate the same selectors before storage/publication\n  -> reject root, flag, or eligibility drift\n```\n\nProduction setup now captures Discovery but still returns\n`NotImplemented`; publication revalidation is an API for the subsequent\nguarded executor, not active installation wiring. Full CLI qualification\nis required; extracted parser/root evidence is provisional. No tool\nprobes, network, mutation, feature docs, or capability advertisement.","tree":{"sha":"cbbdf022ed7cf1e425f31dd40ed1b9b80e42fc1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/cbbdf022ed7cf1e425f31dd40ed1b9b80e42fc1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/828e0ffd57b53edfb40ed6543abb1939e7f45660","verification":{"payload":"tree cbbdf022ed7cf1e425f31dd40ed1b9b80e42fc1f\nparent c31b2f9ee4efe286bf700c69d794ce8b24b9bf22\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791464633 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791464633 -0600\n\nfix: Capture setup discovery context for revalidation (#14439)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdvance [TURBO-6324](https://linear.app/vercel/issue/TURBO-6324), the\ndiscovery-context prerequisite for frozen inventory publication.\n\n- Capture immutable invocation selectors, inferred root/config identity,\nfuture flags, and flag-gated toolchain eligibility.\n- Preserve the existing `setup root: <canonical root>` diagnostic\nthrough the captured discovery object, without changing inference or\nintegration assertions.\n- Re-run the same inference to detect nested config/workspace/Git\nboundary changes, identity drift, and changed eligibility while\npreserving root diagnostics.\n- Reject custom configuration paths outside snapshot coverage; keep\ndebug output redacted.\n\n```text\noriginal invocation selectors\n  -> captured Discovery\n  -> provisioning preparation\n  -> revalidate the same selectors before storage/publication\n  -> reject root, flag, or eligibility drift\n```\n\nProduction setup now captures Discovery but still returns\n`NotImplemented`; publication revalidation is an API for the subsequent\nguarded executor, not active installation wiring. Full CLI qualification\nis required; extracted parser/root evidence is provisional. No tool\nprobes, network, mutation, feature docs, or capability advertisement.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx5S5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAx3UQADZGST5tYJQPJ4L3Wpq+aVPy\nsa8tKs/5EULBQZY70k1T8QWV1QBq6x+u9tsne1mR7zPDx1H95QylZQhLchwCkb45\nkPwl368sQmrfQQ9aw85Q22UqDAAIhjQtVTjZap6YkC97Wf00q8DrPhPyYzbAeJ27\nHuZ/VeFZtUggAaV3lXmaTqH9EfRAsPxTsA/jPpltkSbZm4h5N6QhpftbfktXpm8s\nonRtzZQLATPh2CtHeBbp8I07L3MwRReeYPXKfXMba8TH7uiq+KtWPGfqvmrBNlAF\nc26oQVEPBk9uS5Bgqu5ad7PFHlcBhsc6EXCJnkbbDJAV28pH3EibqvWQaTKnKWJJ\nvD9H+Sezcgaq1kKGEiG3OH/ixzNe851dXFKBT6+T8/k96xJGu8nnxQWLRo1uSN7q\nRkU6yUoclW0rFgFZ987U3dVFhe+W6ndSMnQ/V3ASW12RE3Bj1kkDbMZgvjheBA7m\nMzZr2C/ZikfAnssIfbVUmPamrQcoiygSFo31OvztMEju0vAKReZvI9Z3cP0JH991\nyoJ9JzvDm2RldRnta8dzXAMVYrhMImg3DlVPcWPpm/Mz4lsbnfuj7R1Le47YKwR1\nAFWRYzKkKzez1wRkXW1o/NLb8kcNNNVA+nXIk+u1m+LL139BWyESeML1HlWDG4ku\nCFSk2zkYNkHItUmFOA70\n=2u3A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T13:03:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/828e0ffd57b53edfb40ed6543abb1939e7f45660","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDgyOGUwZmZkNTdiNTNlZGZiNDBlZDY1NDNhYmIxOTM5ZTdmNDU2NjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/c31b2f9ee4efe286bf700c69d794ce8b24b9bf22","sha":"c31b2f9ee4efe286bf700c69d794ce8b24b9bf22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/c31b2f9ee4efe286bf700c69d794ce8b24b9bf22"}],"sha":"828e0ffd57b53edfb40ed6543abb1939e7f45660","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/828e0ffd57b53edfb40ed6543abb1939e7f45660"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/c31b2f9ee4efe286bf700c69d794ce8b24b9bf22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:03:40Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:03:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Provision independently pinned npm with managed Node (#14437)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdvance [TURBO-6325](https://linear.app/vercel/issue/TURBO-6325), the\ndiffering-pin portion of TURBO-6278.\n\n- Factor the concrete pnpm registry preparation/staging core and retain\npnpm''s public API and existing behavior.\n- Provision independently pinned npm with exact package/version/bin\nvalidation, mandatory SHA-512 and locked SHA-256 verification, and full\nresource preservation.\n- Bind npm/npx launchers to selected managed Node in the same complete\ninstallation generation, including fresh preparation, healthy reuse, and\nstale-shim repair.\n\n```text\nindependent npm lock + selected Node\n  -> shared verified registry core\n  -> complete npm resource tree and bound launchers\n  -> caller reconciles the full cohort once\n```\n\nNo hooks, dependency installation, probes, or global Node/Corepack\nlookup. Node must not concurrently own npm/npx. Matching Node-bundled\nnpm remains TURBO-6326; Windows/musl promotion, real npm execution\ncompatibility, and CLI wiring remain unqualified. TURBO-6278 is not\ncomplete.","tree":{"sha":"ca704bc71298b78d83d82c701b3ec792a929dbbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/ca704bc71298b78d83d82c701b3ec792a929dbbe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/c31b2f9ee4efe286bf700c69d794ce8b24b9bf22","verification":{"payload":"tree ca704bc71298b78d83d82c701b3ec792a929dbbe\nparent 1bf8e4cd0be613fa5fbc0752f4b490b28f909145\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791464620 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791464620 -0600\n\nfeat: Provision independently pinned npm with managed Node (#14437)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdvance [TURBO-6325](https://linear.app/vercel/issue/TURBO-6325), the\ndiffering-pin portion of TURBO-6278.\n\n- Factor the concrete pnpm registry preparation/staging core and retain\npnpm''s public API and existing behavior.\n- Provision independently pinned npm with exact package/version/bin\nvalidation, mandatory SHA-512 and locked SHA-256 verification, and full\nresource preservation.\n- Bind npm/npx launchers to selected managed Node in the same complete\ninstallation generation, including fresh preparation, healthy reuse, and\nstale-shim repair.\n\n```text\nindependent npm lock + selected Node\n  -> shared verified registry core\n  -> complete npm resource tree and bound launchers\n  -> caller reconciles the full cohort once\n```\n\nNo hooks, dependency installation, probes, or global Node/Corepack\nlookup. Node must not concurrently own npm/npx. Matching Node-bundled\nnpm remains TURBO-6326; Windows/musl promotion, real npm execution\ncompatibility, and CLI wiring remain unqualified. TURBO-6278 is not\ncomplete.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx5SsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACRwQAJrkkDA066QjRVgYB9rItSoJ\nG15T5YM9FlR2dSfkFth7rcw0L5LSvID3TVhzix8BoXJs0WCHF0pANJe9Y7s6R2kx\ni/tKANSH+2p7Ok1HNJqaFSdBKDhHoT/arx96vfh+W8P6mcpcksL+hm0NawEUycE4\nUs8dEayhKIvyBMiONp5+sI6jWiUsIGBC0C4rK0X9XajZh88itiTWM5PpxIefZC+r\nkL1104Mi94kUHqAzC1jtbVMJxJZBQ7OjCPVKhLSU7LHtf0Y71BDWAUPMfbLZS//x\ndnWLXdYOS1ryGhZVkV2bOVgGIiT0lJth9ZvL+6ELs2j5OeBF+bYCQmvRQnCo7a0H\nDF56V6uQeAFcMtl9yCtj03K64bIsAMFXks5kq7qF5SYH8mVu7tLdVq8bVxPDEMqr\ni2a94ltmf23GtmylyjMkbmj9srADZqP/VubUpOh/ybod+hySvItq+ndDzNzEWp6b\nFPfIGnqOUkvQY7dq5b0F/YdlEGEyVXINKvnjcWnTUpmIkvEJP9XkTZQqOB5AWinE\nBgB0ZTETW3FLjnw5fRpFnVZH9J577I9+fJwMLWONhA/Lu6t8l2FvmQzSr2gKBCvH\nrYwYPlHD//03fHeULywhcz7ua+vPhOpBhdiiqW33xKEfwI0keVU4KdNoXWZEEbzf\nWy3x2q6yhMXX/XpfD2Lq\n=ma/h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T13:03:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/c31b2f9ee4efe286bf700c69d794ce8b24b9bf22","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKGMzMWIyZjllZTRlZmUyODZiZjcwMGM2OWQ3OTRjZThiMjRiOWJmMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/1bf8e4cd0be613fa5fbc0752f4b490b28f909145","sha":"1bf8e4cd0be613fa5fbc0752f4b490b28f909145","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/1bf8e4cd0be613fa5fbc0752f4b490b28f909145"}],"sha":"c31b2f9ee4efe286bf700c69d794ce8b24b9bf22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/c31b2f9ee4efe286bf700c69d794ce8b24b9bf22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/1bf8e4cd0be613fa5fbc0752f4b490b28f909145/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:50:18Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:50:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: Cover pnpm release-age exclusions during prune (#14440)\n\n### Description\n\nAdd regression coverage for `minimumReleaseAgeExcludePrune`, following\n[the suggestion on\n#14372](https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/issues/14372#issuecomment-5999354131).\n\nUnlike catalogs, pnpm cleans up release-age exclusions after\ninstallation; they do not participate in frozen-lockfile validation.\n`turbo prune` should preserve this policy even when it removes\nreferenced package versions.\n\n```text\nprune(app-a)\n├─ Keep app-a and its transitive dependencies\n├─ Remove app-b and its exclusive package version\n└─ Preserve release-age policy in every workspace YAML copy\n```\n\n### Testing Instructions\n\nThe regression test covers the setting omitted, disabled, and enabled,\neach with normal and Docker output. It asserts preservation of\nbare-name, exact-version, version-union, scoped, and wildcard\nexclusions, verifies Docker lockfile copies, and checks that source\nfiles remain unchanged. The fixture does not require pnpm installation\nor network access.","tree":{"sha":"3905c0b8d44eb7184b4a917d43511d64ab5c900e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/3905c0b8d44eb7184b4a917d43511d64ab5c900e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/1bf8e4cd0be613fa5fbc0752f4b490b28f909145","verification":{"payload":"tree 3905c0b8d44eb7184b4a917d43511d64ab5c900e\nparent 9ee68b55e9254065449f074f70d0a7eba4ebb9a8\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791463818 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791463818 -0600\n\ntest: Cover pnpm release-age exclusions during prune (#14440)\n\n### Description\n\nAdd regression coverage for `minimumReleaseAgeExcludePrune`, following\n[the suggestion on\n#14372](https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/issues/14372#issuecomment-5999354131).\n\nUnlike catalogs, pnpm cleans up release-age exclusions after\ninstallation; they do not participate in frozen-lockfile validation.\n`turbo prune` should preserve this policy even when it removes\nreferenced package versions.\n\n```text\nprune(app-a)\n├─ Keep app-a and its transitive dependencies\n├─ Remove app-b and its exclusive package version\n└─ Preserve release-age policy in every workspace YAML copy\n```\n\n### Testing Instructions\n\nThe regression test covers the setting omitted, disabled, and enabled,\neach with normal and Docker output. It asserts preservation of\nbare-name, exact-version, version-union, scoped, and wildcard\nexclusions, verifies Docker lockfile copies, and checks that source\nfiles remain unchanged. The fixture does not require pnpm installation\nor network access.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx5GKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbWUQAGqlqajDS3mRWXN3/Bl++AkW\n9UhJaVMEaN300a++UBN93h6D+2BpxojlwnZqPzAYv0ATXdy5A5jhwLtGH3RKnOZk\nGVgQfjdlvzb1v75ac2SiAlVcF6CbS8jVbOVbZihsbgiOwHpL5oqlmSWc/VhYcycD\n/Ix6vgAqUDYV64mjT5ZMvL02XsqRifgiuGOo9FFwv+2dwK5MEW2aUlv9LbTu8dDV\ndfbtF1SfOtp08A+VPnk2U+DGDcW0dBcbxpEjNMP4xZqab0LicQm4gaoooFPrv1xz\nZCjUElr1gu9GviI1+5AJBLx7j/owWO5HFX18mu19Hq2OoXisKy++gcrNfqtyTqZl\naLqlCsSfWw/tfPGDix7W941ql911ApWzmmEgKLtPxCwtgOza9flTs4J3/qKa0jf1\nrdkNdctK7GjHV5c5J1pclC2SPkp/8MjI3H9JUVrrTCcVRYykT4dv1bKLBuS2b51s\nnXqf13ayk5gGtpwHGzZ2tgSFUgqKGTjcoSjXBPvTfg/S1Ks8MlEgpKW56xKL0C8E\nmZeK1xnRLRjsbU2L1GgVwDh+j6BMzfnJgxVQBKfZ2t/cX1Wxobd9bCEmY/EAkFsv\nrVdWzw2Ta/N7TJVJBEhtXdUrR2X4zRfQaB8csaIeplXf0X19ol9v+I17uZ/FxjfO\nu2MAoN/9LQnQz1NI676X\n=S9ES\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T12:50:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/1bf8e4cd0be613fa5fbc0752f4b490b28f909145","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDFiZjhlNGNkMGJlNjEzZmE1ZmJjMDc1MmY0YjQ5MGIyOGY5MDkxNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/9ee68b55e9254065449f074f70d0a7eba4ebb9a8","sha":"9ee68b55e9254065449f074f70d0a7eba4ebb9a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/9ee68b55e9254065449f074f70d0a7eba4ebb9a8"}],"sha":"1bf8e4cd0be613fa5fbc0752f4b490b28f909145","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/1bf8e4cd0be613fa5fbc0752f4b490b28f909145"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/9ee68b55e9254065449f074f70d0a7eba4ebb9a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:35:25Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:35:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: Avoid Windows CLI teardown deadlocks (#14435)\n\n## Summary\n\nFix the Windows CLI shutdown deadlock exposed by\n[`unfiltered_runs_keep_whole_repo_scan`](https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/actions/runs/37632124289/job/112828854812).\nThe scoping and hash assertions are unchanged.\n\nA captured native hang reached `process::exit`, then blocked in\n`thread_local::ThreadGuard::drop` acquiring its global thread-ID mutex.\n[Windows\nExitProcess](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/processthreadsapi/nf-processthreadsapi-exitprocess)\nterminates other threads before DLL/TLS teardown, so a destructor can\nwait forever on a lock held by a terminated worker.\n\n- Add a Windows-specific final exit boundary after existing application\ncleanup and heap-profile finalization.\n- Flush stdout/stderr explicitly, then self-terminate without the\nhazardous automatic DLL/TLS teardown. Preserve all 32 exit-status bits\nand use fast-fail if termination unexpectedly returns.\n- Route help/version exits through the same boundary. Leave Unix exit\nbehavior unchanged.\n- Add a deterministic TLS/mutex subprocess regression with a bounded\nowned-child watchdog, output tails, and seven DWORD exit statuses.\n\n```diff\n CLI command completes and application cleanup returns\n finish_heap_profile\n-  ExitProcess -> terminate workers -> DLL/TLS destructors -> possible orphaned mutex wait\n+  Flush stdout/stderr\n+  TerminateProcess with the requested DWORD status\n```\n\n## Manual native verification\n\nAt exact candidate `c866029848e2ee185bf957912bda2fc87b6474ce`:\n\n- Captured the baseline hang with a matched dump/PDB and 133 seconds of\nunchanged CPU/I/O counters; the CLI had one remaining thread in the\nteardown mutex wait.\n- A gate-controlled model reproduced the deadlock with both\n`process::exit` and normal main return, three times each.\n- Windows ARM64: all 11 unchanged scoping tests passed; the original\nunfiltered test passed 200/200 concurrent stress cases with zero budget\nexpirations.\n- The exact committed exit helper preserved seven full DWORD statuses\nand 1 MiB plus unflushed stdout/stderr tails on ARM64 and x64 emulation.\nBoth full CLIs produced complete dry-run/profile JSON and preserved a\nreal task''s exit 23 and output tails.\n\n## Qualification limits\n\nThis deliberately skips automatic Windows TLS destructors, CRT/atexit\nhandlers, and DLL process-detach callbacks. Required cleanup must finish\nexplicitly before this boundary; it is not a claim that normal automatic\nteardown is preserved.\n\nThe guest was Windows 11 ARM64; x64 ran under emulation, not Windows\nServer x64 CI. Extended signal/child/daemon checks, heap-profile runtime\nqualification, and x64 automated unit-regression execution were not\ncompleted. Internal Ctrl+C helper and LSP return paths are unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"285539b4d3f2d533defa1e470872b4e8ed6156dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/285539b4d3f2d533defa1e470872b4e8ed6156dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/9ee68b55e9254065449f074f70d0a7eba4ebb9a8","verification":{"payload":"tree 285539b4d3f2d533defa1e470872b4e8ed6156dc\nparent 7b470b6b86e40bb8cce7f5d86b9feb42d39c6195\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791462925 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791462925 +0000\n\ntest: Avoid Windows CLI teardown deadlocks (#14435)\n\n## Summary\n\nFix the Windows CLI shutdown deadlock exposed by\n[`unfiltered_runs_keep_whole_repo_scan`](https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/actions/runs/37632124289/job/112828854812).\nThe scoping and hash assertions are unchanged.\n\nA captured native hang reached `process::exit`, then blocked in\n`thread_local::ThreadGuard::drop` acquiring its global thread-ID mutex.\n[Windows\nExitProcess](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/processthreadsapi/nf-processthreadsapi-exitprocess)\nterminates other threads before DLL/TLS teardown, so a destructor can\nwait forever on a lock held by a terminated worker.\n\n- Add a Windows-specific final exit boundary after existing application\ncleanup and heap-profile finalization.\n- Flush stdout/stderr explicitly, then self-terminate without the\nhazardous automatic DLL/TLS teardown. Preserve all 32 exit-status bits\nand use fast-fail if termination unexpectedly returns.\n- Route help/version exits through the same boundary. Leave Unix exit\nbehavior unchanged.\n- Add a deterministic TLS/mutex subprocess regression with a bounded\nowned-child watchdog, output tails, and seven DWORD exit statuses.\n\n```diff\n CLI command completes and application cleanup returns\n finish_heap_profile\n-  ExitProcess -> terminate workers -> DLL/TLS destructors -> possible orphaned mutex wait\n+  Flush stdout/stderr\n+  TerminateProcess with the requested DWORD status\n```\n\n## Manual native verification\n\nAt exact candidate `c866029848e2ee185bf957912bda2fc87b6474ce`:\n\n- Captured the baseline hang with a matched dump/PDB and 133 seconds of\nunchanged CPU/I/O counters; the CLI had one remaining thread in the\nteardown mutex wait.\n- A gate-controlled model reproduced the deadlock with both\n`process::exit` and normal main return, three times each.\n- Windows ARM64: all 11 unchanged scoping tests passed; the original\nunfiltered test passed 200/200 concurrent stress cases with zero budget\nexpirations.\n- The exact committed exit helper preserved seven full DWORD statuses\nand 1 MiB plus unflushed stdout/stderr tails on ARM64 and x64 emulation.\nBoth full CLIs produced complete dry-run/profile JSON and preserved a\nreal task''s exit 23 and output tails.\n\n## Qualification limits\n\nThis deliberately skips automatic Windows TLS destructors, CRT/atexit\nhandlers, and DLL process-detach callbacks. Required cleanup must finish\nexplicitly before this boundary; it is not a claim that normal automatic\nteardown is preserved.\n\nThe guest was Windows 11 ARM64; x64 ran under emulation, not Windows\nServer x64 CI. Extended signal/child/daemon checks, heap-profile runtime\nqualification, and x64 automated unit-regression execution were not\ncompleted. Internal Ctrl+C helper and LSP return paths are unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx44NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+tcQAIgq7XbP8mLs0t5BfTkI54WW\nLzL+WbgCaMgk4A1+iETeAImpbEZDPjEvYdWqvN6zvbGKZmLtWNx5PtdplZ2g2F9W\nlH02AdFNyBVHfXXiIdy953fuz+ZnFWFTcuKEllXYjXz+lw+yebPFi3gUsnt2mH8W\nkCih3jzha/fCH+nKMajfqvMmGVMNgV+dKHwjpKVNvT4v6EcSc7QnaZDIYN1/lAB6\nQIUCcKAZw/faDiSmh3pSXWFs+Lj5Idl9zt/biQI7KHvbPH/msBEuCme/R86rdgQa\nIXEtAS1v4MhwBEJ9vUaOY/yBP/jey3VSKLA2dReWMEi/olJwC7tLw6T0uUf210D2\n6C5ZxdQZQziI8ac5KYN/o5RDsk0L4kRAHG3gVAa32BRtX4tB3LmFA9qBYKE0ADAU\nIHZwvrNzMV8Zmda/UU21b0dV7PoUoIh7Vtqc1j3daMM2RVlCEVTsPARW7yADu1yo\nmFMyVBPzDwz/RKZAs4Bv0J8CVUYn4PfKdrLvRnw9iXVhLCgiaX5MyE5MBqdqVH4n\nAEdXRTYgnEKNVqB2TRKxWE0/ao97IKjfdOOo9GSJ11ZuYOCpTmkRQ+r0yL7dO4sQ\nXPdr1bkbfFG2eoLdYlwLH65ynK1RS/54xNwi2kGkFoSJOn2wx32eKf3zobWVdr4s\nvweUbFlA4yL7Sdl3vcd2\n=BZrr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T12:35:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/9ee68b55e9254065449f074f70d0a7eba4ebb9a8","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDllZTY4YjU1ZTkyNTQwNjU0NDlmMDc0ZjcwZDBhN2ViYTRlYmI5YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/7b470b6b86e40bb8cce7f5d86b9feb42d39c6195","sha":"7b470b6b86e40bb8cce7f5d86b9feb42d39c6195","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/7b470b6b86e40bb8cce7f5d86b9feb42d39c6195"}],"sha":"9ee68b55e9254065449f074f70d0a7eba4ebb9a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/9ee68b55e9254065449f074f70d0a7eba4ebb9a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31102185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/withkarann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/withkarann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/withkarann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/withkarann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/withkarann","id":31102185,"login":"withkarann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMTAyMTg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/withkarann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/withkarann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/withkarann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/withkarann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/withkarann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/withkarann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/7b470b6b86e40bb8cce7f5d86b9feb42d39c6195/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:12:19Z","email":"31102185+withkarann@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Karan Rajeshbhai Mungara"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:12:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: Skip ignored directories when discovering nested .gitignore files (#14442)\n\n### Description\n\nFixes #14441.\n\nTo find nested `.gitignore` files, `Snapshot::load_matchers` walked the\nwhole tree with every ignore rule turned off, including `node_modules`\nand any other ignored directory. `turbo watch` waits for that walk\nbefore it starts any task.\n\nThis changes the walk to skip directories that are already ignored. Git\nnever reads a `.gitignore` inside an ignored directory, and\n`is_relevant` stops at the first ignored ancestor, so a matcher in there\nwas never used. The walk loads each directory''s `.gitignore` before it\nchecks that directory''s children. `.git/info/exclude` and the global\nexcludes file are now loaded before the walk, because `is_ignored` reads\nthem too.\n\nTime for `RepositoryIgnore::new` (release build, macOS, median of 5):\n\n| repo | before | after |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| repro from #14441 (1M ignored files in 125k directories) | 7705 ms |\n28 ms |\n| a pnpm monorepo with `node_modules` installed (235k paths) | 547 ms |\n44 ms |\n| a smaller pnpm monorepo (57k paths) | 172 ms | 33 ms |\n\nOn a repo without ignored directories the time is the same as before.\n\n### Testing Instructions\n\n- New test `does_not_load_ignore_files_below_ignored_directories`:\nignored directories, an `info/exclude` directory, and a `dir/*` +\n`!dir/keep/` case. It checks which matchers get loaded and the relevance\nof files inside them. It fails on `main` (matchers inside ignored\ndirectories are loaded) and passes here.\n- I also compared `path_is_ignored` from the old and the new snapshot\nfor every file and directory in 4 local repos (about 400k paths). There\nwere no differences.\n- `cargo test -p turborepo-filewatch` and `cargo clippy -p\nturborepo-filewatch --all-targets -- -D warnings` pass. Some\n`globwatcher` tests are flaky for me on `main` too.","tree":{"sha":"ac873cca0ea64f90117390f79719391a0f08258f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/ac873cca0ea64f90117390f79719391a0f08258f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/7b470b6b86e40bb8cce7f5d86b9feb42d39c6195","verification":{"payload":"tree ac873cca0ea64f90117390f79719391a0f08258f\nparent 1926e2e3d9097b7a8a345bde1c3bf8f7c0ee0fd7\nauthor Karan Rajeshbhai Mungara <31102185+withkarann@users.noreply.github.com> 1791414739 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791414739 -0600\n\nperf: Skip ignored directories when discovering nested .gitignore files (#14442)\n\n### Description\n\nFixes #14441.\n\nTo find nested `.gitignore` files, `Snapshot::load_matchers` walked the\nwhole tree with every ignore rule turned off, including `node_modules`\nand any other ignored directory. `turbo watch` waits for that walk\nbefore it starts any task.\n\nThis changes the walk to skip directories that are already ignored. Git\nnever reads a `.gitignore` inside an ignored directory, and\n`is_relevant` stops at the first ignored ancestor, so a matcher in there\nwas never used. The walk loads each directory''s `.gitignore` before it\nchecks that directory''s children. `.git/info/exclude` and the global\nexcludes file are now loaded before the walk, because `is_ignored` reads\nthem too.\n\nTime for `RepositoryIgnore::new` (release build, macOS, median of 5):\n\n| repo | before | after |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| repro from #14441 (1M ignored files in 125k directories) | 7705 ms |\n28 ms |\n| a pnpm monorepo with `node_modules` installed (235k paths) | 547 ms |\n44 ms |\n| a smaller pnpm monorepo (57k paths) | 172 ms | 33 ms |\n\nOn a repo without ignored directories the time is the same as before.\n\n### Testing Instructions\n\n- New test `does_not_load_ignore_files_below_ignored_directories`:\nignored directories, an `info/exclude` directory, and a `dir/*` +\n`!dir/keep/` case. It checks which matchers get loaded and the relevance\nof files inside them. It fails on `main` (matchers inside ignored\ndirectories are loaded) and passes here.\n- I also compared `path_is_ignored` from the old and the new snapshot\nfor every file and directory in 4 local repos (about 400k paths). There\nwere no differences.\n- `cargo test -p turborepo-filewatch` and `cargo clippy -p\nturborepo-filewatch --all-targets -- -D warnings` pass. Some\n`globwatcher` tests are flaky for me on `main` too.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxtHTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVv8QADWOR4jOV2jR3l1/40p8R5HU\nYD9PrqcEftSPoLHRmDxzEWNiIgdiGhQAadfVNC5pygB1OyBRx9rXbuaHK6iyE4nn\nJpImOubKkHocDyjKxlPq+wgbVtvdyWXfJ4ZntNO6IhHhKwth2keqU4dNVOfVjdez\nBni7glmwAZPfjhNVEG0w6ik7hf0YVdCUivOuaaJ9LUIcrxOkCVtcfrtQJiVd9Mzk\nW+ThLNvk7SkF/2Im3aY33OpfLAGFHlC/k1YRp6PlHW6cyuoiMENdelYQ9VKw0NiT\nuH+oE5xnSTkfQm3ERCOsK0Wz/DYIrQ81sSet/BGUqZv5L8LtYNtPAihrhCKHh8kO\no5BpAKZ+XOGpY27EJhGGq01V2Q7gatg97X435fPFT5VgfxgYlcfbGOcreW6av5Lz\nsxSbsHXkrNgFyH7i02lqTbojcazdeNZA+vBf58wz6Yo+rl1yvEeLQgfi/yMVT8eL\ndVM/LC9/rnt88KPKzeQhDGdxn0g/Bnu9Ft6r3tNxExmOeiZPQenXpF6Xbmfzcc9R\nJjLl3/JT1ZuunsLbdHnSDXA6hLxfwVBuZYzB1FjhN2NsFR1Q0Nz5hvGOpCwqGcXm\n68KEdMn4A9YODGH/alNWr/IE5VpA59y6bHLRvXv5LgwkKjJCUjJSdN7jUeP16QPU\nkQpRvqkGWMpUyP2nnVHE\n=wOTB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T23:12:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/7b470b6b86e40bb8cce7f5d86b9feb42d39c6195","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDdiNDcwYjZiODZlNDBiYjhjY2U3ZjVkODZiOWZlYjQyZDM5YzYxOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/1926e2e3d9097b7a8a345bde1c3bf8f7c0ee0fd7","sha":"1926e2e3d9097b7a8a345bde1c3bf8f7c0ee0fd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/1926e2e3d9097b7a8a345bde1c3bf8f7c0ee0fd7"}],"sha":"7b470b6b86e40bb8cce7f5d86b9feb42d39c6195","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/7b470b6b86e40bb8cce7f5d86b9feb42d39c6195"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/1926e2e3d9097b7a8a345bde1c3bf8f7c0ee0fd7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T16:09:26Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T16:09:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Project selected managed execution identity (#14430)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdvance [TURBO-6308](https://linear.app/vercel/issue/TURBO-6308) with a\npure, owned execution-selection and hash-projection API.\n\n- Select active built-in tool/artifact semantics from a validated lock\nusing explicit OS, architecture, libc ABI, target, and CPU variants.\n- Canonically encode selected versions, options, executable mappings,\nand composed artifact identities.\n- Exclude URLs, provenance, local paths, timestamps, and\ninactive-platform metadata. An `any` payload does not imply\nplatform-independent task-output compatibility.\n\n```text\nvalidated lock + explicit execution context + selected tools\n  -> owned execution selection\n  -> canonical identity\n  -> SHA-256 fingerprint\n```\n\nThis is not activation or task-hash/dry-run wiring. Adapter semantic\nvalidation and verify-system checks must precede execution;\nverify-system rows are requirements, not verification evidence. Current\ninventory cannot reconstruct complete lockless semantics. TURBO-6212\nremains incomplete, and no managed capability is advertised.","tree":{"sha":"85c8d7760e6f19b8cc92a14276c2acfa62190e36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/85c8d7760e6f19b8cc92a14276c2acfa62190e36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/1926e2e3d9097b7a8a345bde1c3bf8f7c0ee0fd7","verification":{"payload":"tree 85c8d7760e6f19b8cc92a14276c2acfa62190e36\nparent 5a14ffd1096d74035c4e58df24938014aa9bf9e1\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791389366 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791389366 +0000\n\nfeat: Project selected managed execution identity (#14430)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdvance [TURBO-6308](https://linear.app/vercel/issue/TURBO-6308) with a\npure, owned execution-selection and hash-projection API.\n\n- Select active built-in tool/artifact semantics from a validated lock\nusing explicit OS, architecture, libc ABI, target, and CPU variants.\n- Canonically encode selected versions, options, executable mappings,\nand composed artifact identities.\n- Exclude URLs, provenance, local paths, timestamps, and\ninactive-platform metadata. An `any` payload does not imply\nplatform-independent task-output compatibility.\n\n```text\nvalidated lock + explicit execution context + selected tools\n  -> owned execution selection\n  -> canonical identity\n  -> SHA-256 fingerprint\n```\n\nThis is not activation or task-hash/dry-run wiring. Adapter semantic\nvalidation and verify-system checks must precede execution;\nverify-system rows are requirements, not verification evidence. Current\ninventory cannot reconstruct complete lockless semantics. TURBO-6212\nremains incomplete, and no managed capability is advertised.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABC