vercel/turborepo/commit/5a14ffd1096d74035c4e58df24938014aa9bf9e1","sha":"5a14ffd1096d74035c4e58df24938014aa9bf9e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/5a14ffd1096d74035c4e58df24938014aa9bf9e1"}],"sha":"1926e2e3d9097b7a8a345bde1c3bf8f7c0ee0fd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/1926e2e3d9097b7a8a345bde1c3bf8f7c0ee0fd7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/3623469?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/vercel-gh-bot-3","id":282332853,"login":"vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDOENQOtQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/5a14ffd1096d74035c4e58df24938014aa9bf9e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:58:40Z","email":"282332853+vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:58:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: Support npm patches in pruned workspaces (#14434)\n\nFixes #14426.\n\nnpm 12 records patch paths and integrity on package-lock entries, but\nnpm did not expose those paths to prune and its manifest patch-pruning\nbranch was unreachable. Consequently, retained patches were not copied\nand declarations for removed packages survived.\n\n- Expose npm lockfile patch paths to the existing patch validation and\ncopying flow.\n- Filter root `patchedDependencies` to the patches referenced by the\npruned lockfile.\n- Add an npm-generated fixture and regression coverage for\nretained/removed patches in standard and Docker layouts, nested scoped\ndependencies, metadata preservation, and absolute-path rejection.\n\n### Manual verification\n\nUsing Node 24 and npm 12.2.0, reproduced `EPATCHNOTFOUND` for the\npatched workspace and `EPATCHUNUSED` for the unpatched workspace with\nthe original binary. With the fix, `npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit\n--no-fund` succeeds for both workspaces after both ordinary prune and\n`prune --docker`. Verified the patch''s marker is present in the\ninstalled dependency when retained, and its file/declaration are omitted\nwhen unused.\n\nNo remaining blockers.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: vercel-gh-bot-3[bot] <282332853+vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: vercel-gh-bot-5[bot] <312521305+vercel-gh-bot-5[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"26867bd0884b605623f08b9fb305e8ea09d9e55f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/26867bd0884b605623f08b9fb305e8ea09d9e55f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/5a14ffd1096d74035c4e58df24938014aa9bf9e1","verification":{"payload":"tree 26867bd0884b605623f08b9fb305e8ea09d9e55f\nparent c0e45d40d347f4f3b4868fd4d4c81cd900edd996\nauthor vercel-gh-bot-3[bot] <282332853+vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791388720 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791388720 -0600\n\nfix: Support npm patches in pruned workspaces (#14434)\n\nFixes #14426.\n\nnpm 12 records patch paths and integrity on package-lock entries, but\nnpm did not expose those paths to prune and its manifest patch-pruning\nbranch was unreachable. Consequently, retained patches were not copied\nand declarations for removed packages survived.\n\n- Expose npm lockfile patch paths to the existing patch validation and\ncopying flow.\n- Filter root `patchedDependencies` to the patches referenced by the\npruned lockfile.\n- Add an npm-generated fixture and regression coverage for\nretained/removed patches in standard and Docker layouts, nested scoped\ndependencies, metadata preservation, and absolute-path rejection.\n\n### Manual verification\n\nUsing Node 24 and npm 12.2.0, reproduced `EPATCHNOTFOUND` for the\npatched workspace and `EPATCHUNUSED` for the unpatched workspace with\nthe original binary. With the fix, `npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit\n--no-fund` succeeds for both workspaces after both ordinary prune and\n`prune --docker`. Verified the patch''s marker is present in the\ninstalled dependency when retained, and its file/declaration are omitted\nwhen unused.\n\nNo remaining blockers.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: vercel-gh-bot-3[bot] <282332853+vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: vercel-gh-bot-5[bot] <312521305+vercel-gh-bot-5[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxmwwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiMwQACCYQuNXZKbIpsDdKUiSHzOx\n/9TvMFQ3iq8qGdREYfEcC+BvDQ5pJLq29scMQM4SRQN39zH9U5cDo1EgjwOSna3U\noMjp8so7Sl7lf+aHQmfpgDwyLKjWSS3eabZ5bhPFW3BKE1NMqKo9BmLBec9FVeEc\niXXtKgcSxmhF4Vycn98bUn7D8WRERzmPDEqp30IyL/6J5obkMUm5sUfltly2N0ek\nqk6ON1QdtHUK2uGSQjjlTHJJ/35vjz43pc90/xkjkWNpdJtIEnO9C5cqLTqLkN5T\nyJ+fJ100+cK1nof6yBpnHoNCiGlfByzSf0SnJ0nls7OvB1DdNA9RrGFjjJaTgX4f\nPs8DWAlJ7RJdjyk7snibZTPcbQWSEaYundCmTQpHUtpsPr1VNXjhLd9/wj1oS0Uc\nwR00tRDJGq8ET4B0dv2chsK6YwFTSQv1awWRdeH4U4mviyw6Pa2akEx39nc2HMhD\nwcZh5WWb9wtwr3SPvf31JbaNPXFtKF/aWJma2eTyTl9EClz4CYLXALbkADVoXDwJ\nBm/RIlgU7Gxnxj/JnTyv2Lgs+okMS2Ls4FZgouq/ZCGzQCJ/HcJHOIfSdvjAugwL\nw2Rob0v5WG1OVgGKBz/6dEIPWtHp87DNN3k3oZvOcaj/HSyWBcZCF/GAxr6PPafy\nvP+FLO2D4JtJMObqhz0n\n=Fl4g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T15:58:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/5a14ffd1096d74035c4e58df24938014aa9bf9e1","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDVhMTRmZmQxMDk2ZDc0MDM1YzRlNThkZjI0OTM4MDE0YWE5YmY5ZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/c0e45d40d347f4f3b4868fd4d4c81cd900edd996","sha":"c0e45d40d347f4f3b4868fd4d4c81cd900edd996","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/c0e45d40d347f4f3b4868fd4d4c81cd900edd996"}],"sha":"5a14ffd1096d74035c4e58df24938014aa9bf9e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/5a14ffd1096d74035c4e58df24938014aa9bf9e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/c0e45d40d347f4f3b4868fd4d4c81cd900edd996/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:41:05Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:41:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: Reuse healthy Node.js across managed inventory changes (#14429)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdvance [TURBO-6311](https://linear.app/vercel/issue/TURBO-6311) using\nthe merged reusable-readiness and missing-generation repair APIs.\n\n- Reuse the identical selected Node when the whole selected generation\nis healthy, even if unrelated desired tools change.\n- Keep sibling additions, replacements, and removals from causing Node\ndownloads or staging.\n- Preserve repair behavior for missing generations, damaged\nresources/shims, and scoped npm resources. The complete desired\ninventory and Store guard remain caller-owned.\n\n```diff\n prepare locked Node\n-  Require equality with the entire desired tool set\n+  Require healthy selected generation and identical Node\n reconcile complete desired inventory\n```\n\nNo resolution fallback, activation, or setup dispatch is added.\nWindows/musl promotion remains explicitly unqualified.","tree":{"sha":"f48cef075bfdf6afbf9a764b9427d1984f618f63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/f48cef075bfdf6afbf9a764b9427d1984f618f63"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/c0e45d40d347f4f3b4868fd4d4c81cd900edd996","verification":{"payload":"tree f48cef075bfdf6afbf9a764b9427d1984f618f63\nparent fedba139017728660eac421af7fab7bf10fda3b5\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791384065 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791384065 -0600\n\nfix: Reuse healthy Node.js across managed inventory changes (#14429)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdvance [TURBO-6311](https://linear.app/vercel/issue/TURBO-6311) using\nthe merged reusable-readiness and missing-generation repair APIs.\n\n- Reuse the identical selected Node when the whole selected generation\nis healthy, even if unrelated desired tools change.\n- Keep sibling additions, replacements, and removals from causing Node\ndownloads or staging.\n- Preserve repair behavior for missing generations, damaged\nresources/shims, and scoped npm resources. The complete desired\ninventory and Store guard remain caller-owned.\n\n```diff\n prepare locked Node\n-  Require equality with the entire desired tool set\n+  Require healthy selected generation and identical Node\n reconcile complete desired inventory\n```\n\nNo resolution fallback, activation, or setup dispatch is added.\nWindows/musl promotion remains explicitly unqualified.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxloBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAG9kQABuHYCxtS5IsLQHKBy2qse4X\nob/lUNDgwWU0ij7I6O55yBN8U+GTi+kMHTXz5ih0Ere3PiF7bVKezVOn+XwWaV22\nVA1l+vesEtwqbdIPIe3ozKQlyVTT9ZjFJLyR8qYr7YLocNx3Z08qXcRpbEB098GY\nj3lhnDAMGBmrujq1rkNNDHVRK/P/OLH59t2DIaYkwrELuNApXKeqFmVOqo9maAyb\nFGdYI2LEh1Vq2xhEq9y+OYRYxMu5Qb4C8yJnAdfOhOTwj3L4IBB9fChjNCdA9Lkt\n+v5GkK8IJq0zwhHFt1Y6AT77hP0NS1u54vZVqsadZqMMZ5CCHN4ljs21qNIyt06x\nM5nY47LOfqSAKMl5HrR2g6DPpko5FmJeWi8LOYKmq9pcrDAxLQVfWaCWSoNjidud\nVaV1NBAFKcpPoz68MjQVTpGJtFUINW7G7Xkw0Wctdz6D0OurTqmVlqYqcjB+Q