ckfile\n\nCo-authored-by: vercel-gh-bot-2[bot] <282331341+vercel-gh-bot-2[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxWvTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH0oQAGvugwciR+nmwK8PSb68OyVN\nXVCCb9qYxDxpvk0pKGcseTGJQIbXKIA7lXH6DMfpKyIEBiKDAPQpPNgYOkVTVVcl\nZmlFDuFphyKX1wKwdeks2PHndJHoeJ4PnJILI8hX6/f/jiL7mietXUNq4OvKilQv\nAc+m+qakCRmLER7We33XZgqrzYShyV+Oaey8jKkh1whWhJPZQyYiJitW+jvtsDO7\nWh/6fZc8ClZ45X+3iiY45C8P7jrBCURnsU0L4ehHjAYh66Kn6L2n/HlmQn/4Vk79\n//2iycmlmI8eWypRlZ76WFoTQmoMP+yHdTDmX6qAAwlZwojrqkHoGNVuqNgIlvYE\ndIAtORSg57qJDAxUzltwtVwLJMTm/UEbtqxcpNu411eqwm+K3rlVJZCTqZEoyFBy\n4nylCyjbjLcpWqZAtb2nj3M7a+6andVObp++TLx6eizeEiDTAvq6HH7tp4nONPhn\ne7C+MxS9jQ3cU4s6nKcvraS3B4AtWJdWDnMHm0/7XbZOrkOlyjimgGeI01TpXvWQ\nGeFrb8wXRW6T6EB0PtFGnW8YmEpO2hjMmaXpbQQ+xd1cP+2LfgWErvNBK4pDfmVT\nFgHuJSiKZCQS3DEZ0bD9So3Snaq4U1rT1VzFMcfoV7tSh+ji7xw96MYebiH1lsnC\nhU7h9bM+/msxsM5n8KzB\n=MhdI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T21:44:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/d9464ccf1a872cb23a1dfaf512dd62010c58e807","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKGQ5NDY0Y2NmMWE4NzJjYjIzYTFkZmFmNTEyZGQ2MjAxMGM1OGU4MDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/0b13633a068e133424d7e2d70041d8678abad6af","sha":"0b13633a068e133424d7e2d70041d8678abad6af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/0b13633a068e133424d7e2d70041d8678abad6af"}],"sha":"d9464ccf1a872cb23a1dfaf512dd62010c58e807","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/d9464ccf1a872cb23a1dfaf512dd62010c58e807"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/0b13633a068e133424d7e2d70041d8678abad6af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T21:24:23Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T21:24:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Parse bounded npm registry release metadata (#14412)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes TURBO-6312. Pure exact-version npm/pnpm metadata prerequisite for\nprovisioning, independently based on `main`.\n\n```text\nBounded version document\n  Exact manager + published version\n    Literal canonical tarball URL\n      Mandatory canonical SHA-512 SRI\n        Existing Corepack integrity records\n        -> Still metadata, not verified bytes\n```\n\n- Require object-shaped release/dist records, reject duplicate\nsecurity-relevant fields and trailing content, and bound metadata to 256\nKiB.\n- Require `https://registry.npmjs.org/{name}/-/{name}-{version}.tgz`\nliterally; do not normalize credentials, alternate origins/ports,\nqueries, fragments, or path aliases into acceptance.\n- Decode one canonical padded SHA-512 SRI token into native\n128-character hex. Match an authored SHA-512 pin; retain an authored\nSHA-256 pin as an additional actual-byte requirement, never a weak-hash\nfallback.\n- Reuse the existing manager family, version validation, and\nCorepackIntegrity record. No downloader/client wrapper, installer,\nrange/tag resolution, schema dependency, run activation, or feature\ndocs.\n\nPublisher/source approval remains the caller''s responsibility. This\nhelper never returns artifact bytes or a SHA-256 lock identity. Actual\nbytes must pass mandatory SHA-512 and any additional SHA-256 pin through\nthe shared verification boundary before identity is used. The shared\nSHA-512 precursor is a separate main-based PR, not a compile-time\ndependency or stacked base here.\n\n## Manual boundary check\n\nA local cross-library probe using Python-generated npm/pnpm SRI fixtures\nverified this output with the shared SHA-512 precursor, derived SHA-256\nonly from verified bytes, and rejected altered payloads and\nadditional-pin mismatches. No transport or composition implementation\nwas added to this helper.","tree":{"sha":"fed8072fefc47ea3a54c3498984e004a63a1b442","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/fed8072fefc47ea3a54c3498984e004a63a1b442"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/0b13633a068e133424d7e2d70041d8678abad6af","verification":{"payload":"tree fed8072fefc47ea3a54c3498984e004a63a1b442\nparent 8d019da67ff7524627cd7f3579199dfbc659fc8c\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791321863 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791321863 +0000\n\nfeat: Parse bounded npm registry release metadata (#14412)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes TURBO-6312. Pure exact-version npm/pnpm metadata prerequisite for\nprovisioning, independently based on `main`.\n\n```text\nBounded version document\n  Exact manager + published version\n    Literal canonical tarball URL\n      Mandatory canonical SHA-512 SRI\n        Existing Corepack integrity records\n        -> Still metadata, not verified bytes\n```\n\n- Require object-shaped release/dist records, reject duplicate\nsecurity-relevant fields and trailing content, and bound metadata to 256\nKiB.\n- Require `https://registry.npmjs.org/{name}/-/{name}-{version}.tgz`\nliterally; do not normalize credentials, alternate origins/ports,\nqueries, fragments, or path aliases into acceptance.\n- Decode one canonical padded SHA-512 SRI token into native\n128-character hex. Match an authored SHA-512 pin; retain an authored\nSHA-256 pin as an additional actual-byte requirement, never a weak-hash\nfallback.\n- Reuse the existing manager family, version validation, and\nCorepackIntegrity record. No downloader/client wrapper, installer,\nrange/tag resolution, schema dependency, run activation, or feature\ndocs.\n\nPublisher/source approval remains the caller''s responsibility. This\nhelper never returns artifact bytes or a SHA-256 lock identity. Actual\nbytes must pass mandatory SHA-512 and any additional SHA-256 pin through\nthe shared verification boundary before identity is used. The shared\nSHA-512 precursor is a separate main-based PR, not a compile-time\ndependency or stacked base here.\n\n## Manual boundary check\n\nA local cross-library probe using Python-generated npm/pnpm SRI fixtures\nverified this output with the shared SHA-512 precursor, derived SHA-256\nonly from verified bytes, and rejected altered payloads and\nadditional-pin mismatches. No transport or composition implementation\nwas added to this helper.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxWcHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsc8QAKi/J73lI04F7x8pecllD3el\nC59ap1BOlf87EzDkGrgmyXRSB6rOPS97AjqYSiAX02vPLg9WxNVKA3CP9h1IVKDM\nUva7my7EbqSyQ0Rw/oln0rx7qrIb2uc/gOD9i3QidCn2W2p4Ba/WOnUE2hnz4GAA\nK91Ge0mwBK9kEuuTQRx97rimatP9ppm10LPVFTh54w/uwcuvhPbKYG0dV4chCzog\nUVnPAratWLqc0cyKHNvHWWIxNtuiv0tyOkik/9LwDeUP0hWNhwi15va3b7fyFPhl\nCQnpznh4riaLc3dSLMWMKVVPKW8QtZH3S0Hj8hZxSX/0VCHVJUuGGbBY9kjvNN+Z\n/Fjpmbd6dYNIDD3Fm60POCJoHbmAEuGVn+MpzSUvnlmh33BgvzrB3DeCxkLGjV0C\nrIMSgci/F3yCyxL6d/4TFvtXEacGtzryL0fLxYLkyzcTVeQDbFvxicNy/58guDCx\nImYxs+RMzNQPNo3fO/hBi5RVerAt3vmvQuF1vP7CtWDt3iDbchAdtH4q8FzLC3gJ\nY5sS6dSI18cfWg1gVR3Wvjw83aLE9uit+NgZm99yf6KflQNUGapuKFacOSAFqVDC\n0vrMX/dwQOHy8AeAVbfThxJ1PVlGwYfHtxpFW/1eqyvGTRYHehtHDCPeTG0MAGuC\n57N9bHoeDmDxulD87aOR\n=dfnP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T21:24:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/0b13633a068e133424d7e2d70041d8678abad6af","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDBiMTM2MzNhMDY4ZTEzMzQyNGQ3ZTJkNzAwNDFkODY3OGFiYWQ2YWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/8d019da67ff7524627cd7f3579199dfbc659fc8c","sha":"8d019da67ff7524627cd7f3579199dfbc659fc8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/8d019da67ff7524627cd7f3579199dfbc659fc8c"}],"sha":"0b13633a068e133424d7e2d70041d8678abad6af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/0b13633a068e133424d7e2d70041d8678abad6af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/8d019da67ff7524627cd7f3579199dfbc659fc8c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:42:28Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:42:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Write setup locks atomically (#14399)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Serialize validated tool selections deterministically, including\ncanonical provenance sequences and system executable ordering.\n- Hold a persistent sidecar OS lock across comparison, same-filesystem\nstaging, and atomic replacement. Leave identical locks untouched and\npreserve the previous lock on failure.\n- Add bounded, read-only native declaration probing and comparison\nwithout release resolution. Preserve file/field/request presence,\nadvisory alternatives, integrity, and failure policy; reject unsafe\ninput paths.\n\n```text\nwrite(validated selections)\n  canonicalize bytes\n  acquire persistent writer lock\n  identical? → unchanged\n  stage beside turbo.lock → flush → atomic replacement\n\nordinary native comparison\n  bounded source snapshot → complete declaration map → compare locked provenance\n  no release resolution or installation\n```\n\nStacked on `shew/setup-lock-schema` at `d2d4e72963`. Retarget to `main`\nafter the schema lands. This diff does not duplicate the schema and adds\nno installer or documentation changes.\n\n## Outstanding accepted-review fixes\n\n- Replace root bookkeeping with secure ignored storage and recover owned\ncrash staging under the persistent writer lock. The main-based precursor\nis #14407; consume it rather than duplicating its implementation in this\nPR''s review budget.\n- Preserve or reject Node runtime `onFail` rather than silently missing\npolicy drift. The main-based native-discovery fix is #14406; its\nprovenance must be incorporated into this writer''s ancestry.\n- Require lock/source snapshot CAS before resolver wiring; tracked in\nTURBO-6309. The current unconditional writer must not be used to publish\na precomputed resolver candidate.\n\nReferences TURBO-6203. Do not merge this writer implementation before\nthe accepted storage and provenance fixes are incorporated; the issue\nremains In Progress.","tree":{"sha":"71efaa4b1c7ed5108f09a6f433f9ddb9ac17d45c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/71efaa4b1c7ed5108f09a6f433f9ddb9ac17d45c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/8d019da67ff7524627cd7f3579199dfbc659fc8c","verification":{"payload":"tree 71efaa4b1c7ed5108f09a6f433f9ddb9ac17d45c\nparent ccd998c96bb142eb4a0a68e3b67c47a3cb7aed09\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791319348 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791319348 +0000\n\nfeat: Write setup locks atomically (#14399)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Serialize validated tool selections deterministically, including\ncanonical provenance sequences and system executable ordering.\n- Hold a persistent sidecar OS lock across comparison, same-filesystem\nstaging, and atomic replacement. Leave identical locks untouched and\npreserve the previous lock on failure.\n- Add bounded, read-only native declaration probing and comparison\nwithout release resolution. Preserve file/field/request presence,\nadvisory alternatives, integrity, and failure policy; reject unsafe\ninput paths.\n\n```text\nwrite(validated selections)\n  canonicalize bytes\n  acquire persistent writer lock\n  identical? → unchanged\n  stage beside turbo.lock → flush → atomic replacement\n\nordinary native comparison\n  bounded source snapshot → complete declaration map → compare locked provenance\n  no release resolution or installation\n```\n\nStacked on `shew/setup-lock-schema` at `d2d4e72963`. Retarget to `main`\nafter the schema lands. This diff does not duplicate the schema and adds\nno installer or documentation changes.\n\n## Outstanding accepted-review fixes\n\n- Replace root bookkeeping with secure ignored storage and recover owned\ncrash staging under the persistent writer lock. The main-based precursor\nis #14407; consume it rather than duplicating its implementation in this\nPR''s review budget.\n- Preserve or reject Node runtime `onFail` rather than silently missing\npolicy drift. The main-based native-discovery fix is #14406; its\nprovenance must be incorporated into this writer''s ancestry.\n- Require lock/source snapshot CAS before resolver wiring; tracked in\nTURBO-6309. The current unconditional writer must not be used to publish\na precomputed resolver candidate.\n\nReferences TURBO-6203. Do not merge this writer implementation before\nthe accepted storage and provenance fixes are incorporated; the issue\nremains In Progress.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxV00CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYowQAFQMLXbOlUS5mKaDwyzpEBcE\nDZKgPQlr8RFspxIECOn30+TN+tXVdetn8oNfw5UEMYzB5T1M317U63wQkTgubY5G\n/XFeV/GcBcEFaj70H5VSrHeHaXo8W6oN0wWznr0ZI7XFc6lBH6ApgfbyQoyYfl9+\n/DA7PmBHSbu09Gdz57iXlpYQYh1MC+/0gRmygQRA9+HWXCaFN2XNVlXtM4ZFIf+/\nTzF6TcnkpXweH7xMR6anON6WObIgQO2XXzFt2lJC8yTxHzuWlpWWJmpk2uY3QCUR\nuTH/EyBIP9jg/jNZuE+v/mq45iiaG20nC6T7flk2378l/eb4Fx7IVosOR/m3T1nZ\nOtpBzsN8/feCwY7/7E7rcZjlMCXX/YpiaHoz7WGU0UOfiThrXI7Lv6JKBbDzV6Mx\n85HOyXbR9IfGkqWZkH56MXPy1rr8UhFZ7HagXZL7eTJLJxnK6j4VCi3Kek3ahHAy\nHr5iOavVwsA/ylkT804mbPU70LpDAOw+0qSbgtsm7A33OcmnKV3t4xWo/q1rF1EJ\nWOOuhsX3WTcuXWSMo4fLrxQDW8XXyUWRXLaNPfL108PdN6w9akvaEab5N8o8WOI1\nPheBzH/yMaeCc79dTQPm7li/cWDRcmX/dVBhv+kgU6vFlt8OwgMOFdiNrPAhlic7\nzjsQymh3BEsIPzDVn31y\n=mreI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T20:42:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/8d019da67ff7524627cd7f3579199dfbc659fc8c","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDhkMDE5ZGE2N2ZmNzUyNDYyN2NkN2YzNTc5MTk5ZGZiYzY1OWZjOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/ccd998c96bb142eb4a0a68e3b67c47a3cb7aed09","sha":"ccd998c96bb142eb4a0a68e3b67c47a3cb7aed09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/ccd998c96bb142eb4a0a68e3b67c47a3cb7aed09"}],"sha":"8d019da67ff7524627cd7f3579199dfbc659fc8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/8d019da67ff7524627cd7f3579199dfbc659fc8c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/ccd998c96bb142eb4a0a68e3b67c47a3cb7aed09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:25:14Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:25:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Parse bounded Node release metadata (#14410)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd a pure, bounded adapter for the official Node JSON release index and\nSHA-256 checksum manifests. This is a precursor to lock creation, not\nsetup orchestration or installation.\n\n```text\napproved-source metadata\n  → release index + exact checksum filename map\n    → one selected release\n      → advertised target + exact artifact digest\n```\n\n- Reuse native request resolution and standard Node artifact names\nwithout selecting different releases per platform.\n- Retain bundled npm identity and normalized LTS metadata; tolerate\nunrelated upstream enrichment while rejecting duplicate JSON keys,\nreleases, and file labels.\n- Bind advertised targets to mandatory exact filename checksums, with\nbounded input and deterministic local fixtures.\n- Keep publisher trust, required-platform coverage, runtime\ncompatibility, transport, and installation with their callers. No\nfeature documentation is added.\n\nFixes TURBO-6310","tree":{"sha":"13b9a49f34c59021cbd45167272d9c4ce122beee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/13b9a49f34c59021cbd45167272d9c4ce122beee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/ccd998c96bb142eb4a0a68e3b67c47a3cb7aed09","verification":{"payload":"tree 13b9a49f34c59021cbd45167272d9c4ce122beee\nparent 98f488474cfefb4015da8a420a4d1dd1543734d7\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791318314 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791318314 +0000\n\nfeat: Parse bounded Node release metadata (#14410)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd a pure, bounded adapter for the official Node JSON release index and\nSHA-256 checksum manifests. This is a precursor to lock creation, not\nsetup orchestration or installation.\n\n```text\napproved-source metadata\n  → release index + exact checksum filename map\n    → one selected release\n      → advertised target + exact artifact digest\n```\n\n- Reuse native request resolution and standard Node artifact names\nwithout selecting different releases per platform.\n- Retain bundled npm identity and normalized LTS metadata; tolerate\nunrelated upstream enrichment while rejecting duplicate JSON keys,\nreleases, and file labels.\n- Bind advertised targets to mandatory exact filename checksums, with\nbounded input and deterministic local fixtures.\n- Keep publisher trust, required-platform coverage, runtime\ncompatibility, transport, and installation with their callers. No\nfeature documentation is added.\n\nFixes TURBO-6310","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxVkqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWa4QADrSbeUQmHkhOpaNOO/yALVq\nN0I5j9Fr9Apqmpc//g9IzczgqtveU+/DxROfrj0i/KBGQDZgAJzgSFq3eFLCuDjg\nEkF3pt+qcpSSazCH6Tq2S3ku+S/3lXHuEctIt2TQDJTddbNOehkTLW5koLNaw4/c\nrFt4EH3zJJJZZ4f/DVKv8vPNu9FaQ1W5z8HaVEpATjx4jolhKRo07TFJBcGDZ625\nkQGbEirKK4dQ52FIOqAjMG3hu8CGwIzqgnvP89KXBiulxGHXEsUa8sGrSf+34a6w\nGTBKIB10+ZP3jnVMSJ/Cw5YOeqgDYd3Dexw/jZ3TfX/bTEj/kqF2otP62/74XwgW\n+ByKRf+qfOANXoBAIy7tx9ndIF31+N0M0HjwRWkGBeU0sqMRPv0rR5BNCv/5VsXh\nWcMw5DsCuU9HLYwbqgDF+w3bbdKEh6toXALu4o1P0B/l8rrVDdmBb9Xqp1NjtqZ7\nhM1OORjGbDPkfFlY4Uw/p3to3VJtB68VC3JPkVFfXpUhBOZ02hpkJybF9FMTtRcR\nJPU/GPBKj0UCvRkqsu+RVtqmnWRg6Dmu7WupMSVTooiMUPNvYiOtDgURnYTlMDnv\nMeAFUBAkgauEO4EJakF8gP+GCE+ZrxC76eZWEUmOtOHmzV1qzJ1xhukZy57aVAe8\naGje7UwzWyH3ySm5heLF\n=h9NG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T20:25:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/ccd998c96bb142eb4a0a68e3b67c47a3cb7aed09","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKGNjZDk5OGM5NmJiMTQyZWI0YTBhNjhlM2I2N2M0N2EzY2I3YWVkMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/98f488474cfefb4015da8a420a4d1dd1543734d7","sha":"98f488474cfefb4015da8a420a4d1dd1543734d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/98f488474cfefb4015da8a420a4d1dd1543734d7"}],"sha":"ccd998c96bb142eb4a0a68e3b67c47a3cb7aed09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/ccd998c96bb142eb4a0a68e3b67c47a3cb7aed09"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/98f488474cfefb4015da8a420a4d1dd1543734d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:23:41Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:23:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Add secure ignored setup writer storage (#14407)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add a schema-independent writer-storage primitive for the accepted\nbookkeeping findings in #14399.\n- Keep the persistent writer inode and owned crash staging in Git-proven\nignored `.turbo/setup-lock` storage. Report missing ignore coverage\nbefore writing; do not silently edit `.gitignore`.\n- Pin safe directory components, reject links/reparse points and\nnon-regular state, and require same-filesystem staging.\n- Serialize Unix writers on the stable root-directory inode before the\ncache sidecar, so replacing `.turbo` cannot split active transactions.\nPin Windows directories against deletion.\n- Recover only the owned stale stage under the exclusive guard and\npreserve the previous lock on failed promotion.\n\n```text\nwriter acquire\n  pin root → stable transaction guard → verify ignore coverage\n  pin .turbo/setup-lock → persistent writer lock → recover owned stage\n  compare lock/source snapshot → stage → flush → atomic promotion\n\n.turbo/setup-lock/\n├── writer   (Persistent; never unlinked)\n└── staged   (Owned crash staging; recovered under the writer guard)\n```\n\nReaders and ordinary plan checks must not acquire writer storage. This\nPR adds no installer, resolver, schema duplication, user documentation,\nor current-writer integration.\n\nReferences TURBO-6203. This is a main-based precursor for #14399, not\ncompletion of that issue. Lock/source snapshot CAS before resolver\nwiring is tracked in TURBO-6309.","tree":{"sha":"579d3a1667f1db0574984a002f9c3fea704300d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/579d3a1667f1db0574984a002f9c3fea704300d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/98f488474cfefb4015da8a420a4d1dd1543734d7","verification":{"payload":"tree 579d3a1667f1db0574984a002f9c3fea704300d1\nparent 78442d4286941a78aa8ec20301160b0cb03eecdb\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791318221 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791318221 +0000\n\nfeat: Add secure ignored setup writer storage (#14407)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add a schema-independent writer-storage primitive for the accepted\nbookkeeping findings in #14399.\n- Keep the persistent writer inode and owned crash staging in Git-proven\nignored `.turbo/setup-lock` storage. Report missing ignore coverage\nbefore writing; do not silently edit `.gitignore`.\n- Pin safe directory components, reject links/reparse points and\nnon-regular state, and require same-filesystem staging.\n- Serialize Unix writers on the stable root-directory inode before the\ncache sidecar, so replacing `.turbo` cannot split active transactions.\nPin Windows directories against deletion.\n- Recover only the owned stale stage under the exclusive guard and\npreserve the previous lock on failed promotion.\n\n```text\nwriter acquire\n  pin root → stable transaction guard → verify ignore coverage\n  pin .turbo/setup-lock → persistent writer lock → recover owned stage\n  compare lock/source snapshot → stage → flush → atomic promotion\n\n.turbo/setup-lock/\n├── writer   (Persistent; never unlinked)\n└── staged   (Owned crash staging; recovered under the writer guard)\n```\n\nReaders and ordinary plan checks must not acquire writer storage. This\nPR adds no installer, resolver, schema duplication, user documentation,\nor current-writer integration.\n\nReferences TURBO-6203. This is a main-based precursor for #14399, not\ncompletion of that issue. Lock/source snapshot CAS before resolver\nwiring is tracked in TURBO-6309.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxVjNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/gIQAIXuCyFEDV5GAflZ2OBp2Z2Q\nH/Whw0nSlMfMTgm0jj0kOf4+bg254NHLSb/1Akh7OWZFDVeGruFvyolYjUp9ImiM\nZSt0GYHeV1zdLU/xuelwAq/zddU+TMQb3FoSMuIayB8s45yAaDWJQljvmf4inoEG\n6gA6FkaRuweN67u0MKqrBX/4dtdvMFNblxaFPfXVe55iESu2X2eX3ec+jpZV77ni\nLEvpgf7RBfN66pmPYGY+fWIMx0iN2e9x+9doaBNcvz1luYH3Um0B+/hnAAP9w/Kt\nQieWW9/PdOpr5qT7aVYCzjuvTxxZ13I2mqF2A9LZYRvroNUPBJYttCSpoXVzglQB\nmzVDWs0r3a45vH1se4AIBLhURSMvvKkYJVG7K3psBqqAfVg60SbFG1KWwhJ9hu9/\n3AsHP6EK6Mo9weOe07Nym/UmhQIQSByVWAz/YWy0ZmsswSxjtAgpTD43X48C5nUw\ngopZzlKYmwONRVXErRhltqNVgwh+ytg8SNWq2HMWF6gEKWPg5jrsVxBtMv07MToo\n0qoxqdBaNfzRMu5+6RLZoEhh1av1SkpTtkptZho6yG6Axpzu4AFIGAZqq1wroF2L\nnSIDQIsXZZ1w3PHQ5acZy98NLjvgQBahVt8YlY9nEvwDbbBnileCEu1qZDykmoZo\nJiAK8w0+6KvC09Q0lFqG\n=shzF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T20:23:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/98f488474cfefb4015da8a420a4d1dd1543734d7","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDk4ZjQ4ODQ3NGNmZWZiNDAxNWRhOGE0MjBhNGQxZGQxNTQzNzM0ZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/78442d4286941a78aa8ec20301160b0cb03eecdb","sha":"78442d4286941a78aa8ec20301160b0cb03eecdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/78442d4286941a78aa8ec20301160b0cb03eecdb"}],"sha":"98f488474cfefb4015da8a420a4d1dd1543734d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/98f488474cfefb4015da8a420a4d1dd1543734d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/78442d4286941a78aa8ec20301160b0cb03eecdb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:21:13Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:21:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: Repair missing install generations and share tool readiness (#14404)\n\nFixes TURBO-6306\n\nAdds shared readiness APIs for the Node provisioning precursor and lets\nsetup repair a deleted selected generation without replacing a valid\nmanifest with partial state.\n\n```text\nValidate manifest and selected-generation path\n├─ Malformed or unsafe → error\n├─ Generation missing → absent installation; rebuild desired set\n└─ Generation exists → check the entire generation\n   ├─ Healthy → is_current(desired): exact complete set\n   │            can_reuse(tool): exact installed member\n   └─ Damaged → no reuse; prepare and stage the complete desired set\n```\n\n- Provides the complete-set `Store::is_current` API currently carried by\nthe Node PR, alongside `Store::can_reuse(&Tool)`.\n- Shares whole-generation health and exact tool membership with\nreconciliation. Adding or removing another tool can reuse an unchanged\nNode tree; a damaged sibling tree or shim invalidates every tool''s\nreuse.\n- Keeps malformed metadata and unsafe selected paths fail-closed,\npropagates unrelated I/O errors, and classifies regular-file/directory\nshim replacements as repairable installation damage.\n- Preserves clone-local locking, serialized callbacks, private staging\nand atomic publication.\n\nThis is main-based and does not modify the Node branch. The scoped\nartifact-path and owner-executable fixes remain separate in #14403; the\nNode owner can remove its duplicate API diff and consume `can_reuse`\nwhen integrating the approved precursor base. No feature documentation\nis added.","tree":{"sha":"83b8d357774bdcf8a172469f3e0012fe13bc8839","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/83b8d357774bdcf8a172469f3e0012fe13bc8839"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/78442d4286941a78aa8ec20301160b0cb03eecdb","verification":{"payload":"tree 83b8d357774bdcf8a172469f3e0012fe13bc8839\nparent 4f4ff2e9ecc0986174c6d31440e109a4a2357118\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791318073 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791318073 +0000\n\nfix: Repair missing install generations and share tool readiness (#14404)\n\nFixes TURBO-6306\n\nAdds shared readiness APIs for the Node provisioning precursor and lets\nsetup repair a deleted selected generation without replacing a valid\nmanifest with partial state.\n\n```text\nValidate manifest and selected-generation path\n├─ Malformed or unsafe → error\n├─ Generation missing → absent installation; rebuild desired set\n└─ Generation exists → check the entire generation\n   ├─ Healthy → is_current(desired): exact complete set\n   │            can_reuse(tool): exact installed member\n   └─ Damaged → no reuse; prepare and stage the complete desired set\n```\n\n- Provides the complete-set `Store::is_current` API currently carried by\nthe Node PR, alongside `Store::can_reuse(&Tool)`.\n- Shares whole-generation health and exact tool membership with\nreconciliation. Adding or removing another tool can reuse an unchanged\nNode tree; a damaged sibling tree or shim invalidates every tool''s\nreuse.\n- Keeps malformed metadata and unsafe selected paths fail-closed,\npropagates unrelated I/O errors, and classifies regular-file/directory\nshim replacements as repairable installation damage.\n- Preserves clone-local locking, serialized callbacks, private staging\nand atomic publication.\n\nThis is main-based and does not modify the Node branch. The scoped\nartifact-path and owner-executable fixes remain separate in #14403; the\nNode owner can remove its duplicate API diff and consume `can_reuse`\nwhen integrating the approved precursor base. No feature documentation\nis added.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxVg5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKRsQADuil+xAyHVjhfD4znX5/GN5\n31yPWP7upY1m0luChfG0GjBlaEyAdriVtmdi1t8mQP9guIP6o3FxN4kUUowuXdMX\nsg+U+DotV07yCseGoDA+nq8xQENjilTPSdkxobuLb1U9oVOX74nxqsTKZlgYikn1\nbxNRAyox207HzikuFYdluuHF0oC6oW7vrlMb2+7IPqOH73ua/FKs6l9ZbfYQrCyV\nFl2k9ObCqi0/5oZ1701Plf0mOkx0oR8cNRwxLiMiR5tXvc9vNGK/tOZhapbGYE3i\nm97I+i7QhoOli+S63ZpchFXmwUDq7WNAvJUT5ApeRGWkE1Ov2k6ZSR37ftE54hjr\n8QVp447/gcl9CN3Jt+y23Vu/3KsSsra0o8LellGyPn9kKxufyImD4uR1DnXY9iLW\naHzTldVrtTBqsoKiFKGZ7LclbdLzvDViP+dIJfErdqvF1BioU3kqi5N2hBL9GqI6\ncBNbYzq09ZVQwXf5wLNKfBVi/F56L1NUlzb+3iL/eEDGOg3Ov2mtrBbsUeF0XGdG\n+s6Gq7KPujAoe3r0XlCTPWMGXHRIwDL1i3zRMwV4iyTQefbI3Mvbt8y9Hl6NnsFt\n5aQ5z99pEbKZhRtDqXZfLIIjZ/GnTsLwALs3tdM0M7aITqtxZTgFOpWJk5zH071X\nP8MPZ1IJVP/da0uUsBJY\n=qJ4+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T20:21:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/78442d4286941a78aa8ec20301160b0cb03eecdb","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDc4NDQyZDQyODY5NDFhNzhhYThlYzIwMzAxMTYwYjBjYjAzZWVjZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/4f4ff2e9ecc0986174c6d31440e109a4a2357118","sha":"4f4ff2e9ecc0986174c6d31440e109a4a2357118","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/4f4ff2e9ecc0986174c6d31440e109a4a2357118"}],"sha":"78442d4286941a78aa8ec20301160b0cb03eecdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/78442d4286941a78aa8ec20301160b0cb03eecdb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/4f4ff2e9ecc0986174c6d31440e109a4a2357118/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:07:41Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:07:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: Stabilize lockfile closure parity coverage (#14420)\n\n## Summary\n\nFix the shared Rust CI failure caused by requiring the live repository\nlockfile to always use the closure DP fast path.\n\nThe dependency update in #14416 introduced a legitimate\nworkspace-sensitive `@jest/globals@30.3.0` edge: a workspace importer\nselects a peer-suffixed snapshot while another resolves the plain\nsnapshot. Production correctly falls back to the workspace-scoped walk;\nthe test incorrectly labels this lockfile uniform.\n\n```text\nStable pnpm v9 fixture → Require DP → Legacy parity + sorting + shared Arcs\nLive repository lock  → Public API → Legacy parity + sorting + uniqueness\nDivergent fixture     → Require fallback → Legacy parity\n```\n\n- Keep mandatory fast-path assertions on deterministic fixtures,\nincluding a shared two-node dependency cycle and three reused package\nidentities.\n- Compare every live-repository closure with independent\nsingle-workspace legacy walks, regardless of which production path is\nvalid.\n- Preserve the existing divergent-edge regression.\n- Change only the test module. Production resolution, dependency\nversions, and CI gates are unchanged.\n\nThis addresses the common lockfile assertion blocking main and the\nqueued setup PRs.","tree":{"sha":"deae8ea9af82208061e247fbab12783b54ecc7e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/deae8ea9af82208061e247fbab12783b54ecc7e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/4f4ff2e9ecc0986174c6d31440e109a4a2357118","verification":{"payload":"tree deae8ea9af82208061e247fbab12783b54ecc7e5\nparent c661f636f2b352db759536f37058af2a3972192a\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791317261 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791317261 -0600\n\ntest: Stabilize lockfile closure parity coverage (#14420)\n\n## Summary\n\nFix the shared Rust CI failure caused by requiring the live repository\nlockfile to always use the closure DP fast path.\n\nThe dependency update in #14416 introduced a legitimate\nworkspace-sensitive `@jest/globals@30.3.0` edge: a workspace importer\nselects a peer-suffixed snapshot while another resolves the plain\nsnapshot. Production correctly falls back to the workspace-scoped walk;\nthe test incorrectly labels this lockfile uniform.\n\n```text\nStable pnpm v9 fixture → Require DP → Legacy parity + sorting + shared Arcs\nLive repository lock  → Public API → Legacy parity + sorting + uniqueness\nDivergent fixture     → Require fallback → Legacy parity\n```\n\n- Keep mandatory fast-path assertions on deterministic fixtures,\nincluding a shared two-node dependency cycle and three reused package\nidentities.\n- Compare every live-repository closure with independent\nsingle-workspace legacy walks, regardless of which production path is\nvalid.\n- Preserve the existing divergent-edge regression.\n- Change only the test module. Production resolution, dependency\nversions, and CI gates are unchanged.\n\nThis addresses the common lockfile assertion blocking main and the\nqueued setup PRs.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxVUNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFgUQAJe9ymk+9j1ZrTsbLcewIMX0\njvyHej4E+x8XQBWB27fNCXCdV9dmVulJIKx234QTqJdGuyBT7bMsbgvmJwoqkqrH\nXP6ThndL19+Xjz/a/zPlaPLpCdWxc4hgTHyykt00ROjLRPSrB13wNNvb13cskk8j\nYr8uGsSaZGs+eDP/93dEfapIQCB3Fn/JrsmjdWP3IVE7PbYzhP+mH+WLrDUsFsfp\n7DW7uIUT3sUCshIN/1m+POmsf4sgmPCvJVQ6YI3w+JFifdZKErps4bxkYGdTPg94\nRnrbZmxrr8wg6iTtqXKVwwY1Zm42ULXPK4I5yMdLb2nRnjzVXEXuLuSrvsz5YDYr\nw0uJxWA+YlIKxjrS421qBsZDtd0L8Xs+EnG0+eUypq4EchDEVjGGTfHgtWexZXq9\nkMdRsaTyIwIJGOO9OwJlLRzz27SRRxHMwToeisaV/sqhVieICHYeXyyYRLKufWbU\nHlKZWKMsM6eQRh5u8IDnfXE9jen2reQ5soCujWJ+zwvyMr8nq7YGndom0EgyQ8So\nutYWk5qta8UAh9m0L2bn/iQFmqgWlqF+HX85iYVJt0r+MEaNgyP7Yt2tqj7ryQpu\nBR7cmlXTw7bmhL90YiDRi/VtMJm3fq9sLiZg5UrKGBI0JdIYU+r24BDgkfT8UW52\nCaujckfHmgwL+reE7hay\n=JgOm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T20:07:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/4f4ff2e9ecc0986174c6d31440e109a4a2357118","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDRmNGZmMmU5ZWNjMDk4NjE3NGM2ZDMxNDQwZTEwOWE0YTIzNTcxMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/c661f636f2b352db759536f37058af2a3972192a","sha":"c661f636f2b352db759536f37058af2a3972192a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/c661f636f2b352db759536f37058af2a3972192a"}],"sha":"4f4ff2e9ecc0986174c6d31440e109a4a2357118","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/4f4ff2e9ecc0986174c6d31440e109a4a2357118"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/c661f636f2b352db759536f37058af2a3972192a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:12:45Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:12:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Verify bounded SHA-512 tool artifacts (#14411)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes TURBO-6313. Shared-download precursor for npm/pnpm integrity\nhandling, independently based on `main`.\n\n```text\nBounded artifact bytes\n  Mandatory SHA-512 pin matches\n    Optional additional SHA-256 pin matches\n      Existing VerifiedArtifact\n        SHA-256 artifact identity\n```\n\n- Extend the existing local-byte and DownloadClient APIs with an exact\n128-character hex ExpectedSha512. Keep the SHA-256 APIs and one shared\ntransport path.\n- Do not derive or compare SHA-256 until mandatory SHA-512 verification\nsucceeds. Return the existing verified-byte type only after all supplied\npins match.\n- Preserve approved origins, credential rejection, redirect denial,\nverified TLS/proxy behavior, identity encoding, byte/total-time bounds,\nand opaque errors. Metadata reads remain unverified.\n\nNo registry resolution, wrapper client, installer, CLI/run wiring,\nschema dependency, or feature docs. Callers still choose bounds for\nlocal bytes and obtain expected digests from a pinned or otherwise\ntrusted source; a digest parsed from untrusted adjacent metadata does\nnot establish publisher authenticity.\n\n## Manual boundary check\n\nComposed this library with the separately based registry helper using\nlocal npm/pnpm documents generated by Python hashlib/base64. Canonical\nSRI became native SHA-512 expectations, correct artifact bytes produced\nthe expected SHA-256 identity, and altered bytes or an additional\nSHA-256 mismatch produced no verified artifact. This probe added no\ndependency or composition code to either PR.","tree":{"sha":"c269ed64f5c349d174df4c2fcddb56cef9ef1556","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/c269ed64f5c349d174df4c2fcddb56cef9ef1556"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/c661f636f2b352db759536f37058af2a3972192a","verification":{"payload":"tree c269ed64f5c349d174df4c2fcddb56cef9ef1556\nparent 3ad1a4313e0b1c6fc6bb6c7b686087b10a30c87a\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791313965 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791313965 -0600\n\nfeat: Verify bounded SHA-512 tool artifacts (#14411)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes TURBO-6313. Shared-download precursor for npm/pnpm integrity\nhandling, independently based on `main`.\n\n```text\nBounded artifact bytes\n  Mandatory SHA-512 pin matches\n    Optional additional SHA-256 pin matches\n      Existing VerifiedArtifact\n        SHA-256 artifact identity\n```\n\n- Extend the existing local-byte and DownloadClient APIs with an exact\n128-character hex ExpectedSha512. Keep the SHA-256 APIs and one shared\ntransport path.\n- Do not derive or compare SHA-256 until mandatory SHA-512 verification\nsucceeds. Return the existing verified-byte type only after all supplied\npins match.\n- Preserve approved origins, credential rejection, redirect denial,\nverified TLS/proxy behavior, identity encoding, byte/total-time bounds,\nand opaque errors. Metadata reads remain unverified.\n\nNo registry resolution, wrapper client, installer, CLI/run wiring,\nschema dependency, or feature docs. Callers still choose bounds for\nlocal bytes and obtain expected digests from a pinned or otherwise\ntrusted source; a digest parsed from untrusted adjacent metadata does\nnot establish publisher authenticity.\n\n## Manual boundary check\n\nComposed this library with the separately based registry helper using\nlocal npm/pnpm documents generated by Python hashlib/base64. Canonical\nSRI became native SHA-512 expectations, correct artifact bytes produced\nthe expected SHA-256 identity, and altered bytes or an additional\nSHA-256 mismatch produced no verified artifact. This probe added no\ndependency or composition code to either PR.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxUgtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuDoQAIKw/do3NNf3/e/20Mr+Orxo\nJ3eJIllOLmHVBhfJ0wEsXkVkox1F3wpXMTs7Z3CxHYML9GBOKyW9UOUB7E/zKmWn\n35vUCkSD+X4i+nRjOTSpF/O1n3VTCtXwEVJjTseA5CU7/rvrZrdWLn7giLDvjHqm\ntwHCBrfCiFlg55DTugrGNjoLoHJQlMuYIdJwFQ2S01CA5f3z6wihmSrItBGo20eB\nrijEyZS/kvwDO2ubhDAS6e5XNdOvvITdTWgISXTd+ROsgMjw+M4X6RHHnvlqC3WO\nl5I4MekPCnLkfEorOgyjcYVIXI2mTjv9VIWtAgIWShZhFy8DyqnV2MMM4H2H60uu\n0r+JsIIJ3qomHg+gpwIvHUNCidp8nqBFlzcaKyF16sEwEIXzGbgERXGNWYv0mHWG\ncYDVON4juTVPPVmNvTcASrrRlzhnlRO2B8WRmzYK5lEsU4hfNY+gTUvdzW2u69L6\nZy8ckxE0B/mKRdIlBV44U9Wgs+LSw1GLbRJddHvV9kgEoCzdgUYtsT9PImFVrEgy\nQ3Ose5OqNU3+CSl3OMequw3pjZXwvvtegfYfBl6H3nN3zTJ94HTLTSwo8+WiMnYQ\nFBVtAPgaNuC90hzR1SOzx1Q8vShW+QnCf9jrZqk6uOHqE3z6u56O8q2QxuTJquFQ\n4fnIentJVp5uZQyY+V5Z\n=+AV4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T19:12:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/c661f636f2b352db759536f37058af2a3972192a","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKGM2NjFmNjM2ZjJiMzUyZGI3NTk1MzZmMzcwNThhZjJhMzk3MjE5MmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/3ad1a4313e0b1c6fc6bb6c7b686087b10a30c87a","sha":"3ad1a4313e0b1c6fc6bb6c7b686087b10a30c87a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/3ad1a4313e0b1c6fc6bb6c7b686087b10a30c87a"}],"sha":"c661f636f2b352db759536f37058af2a3972192a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/c661f636f2b352db759536f37058af2a3972192a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/3ad1a4313e0b1c6fc6bb6c7b686087b10a30c87a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:12:37Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:12:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Add an internal managed-run capability query (#14408)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add the exact native `--__internal-managed-run-capabilities` query\nbefore normal CLI/shim initialization. It does not read repository\nconfiguration, infer or spawn a local CLI, start telemetry/profiles,\nwrite guidance, or change descriptor limits.\n- Define a versioned JSON ABI bounded to 4 KiB, with a validated decoder\nthat rejects unknown ABI versions, malformed/duplicate/unknown fields,\nand invalid metadata. CLI versions are diagnostic only; compatibility is\nexplicit lock-schema membership.\n- Keep the production `managedRunSchemas` list empty. Lock parsing and\npartial setup delivery do not establish the complete activation,\ndrift-validation, strict/loose task-environment, and hashing contract.\n- Cover malformed roots, missing JavaScript tools, local pins, ambient\noverrides, profile arguments, and closed output streams. No feature\ndocumentation is added.\n\n```text\nnative CLI entry\n  → exact capability query\n    → bounded JSON, managedRunSchemas: []\n  → otherwise: existing initialization and shim routing\n```\n\nThis is the approved ABI-foundation split of TURBO-6202. Metadata\ngating, bounded local probing, and handoff enforcement remain a separate\nPR after this foundation and schema PR #14400 are both on main. The\nparent issue is not completed by this change.\n\nCloses TURBO-6307.","tree":{"sha":"f2d9476d808438144ebdc331bc70c0c80250967e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/f2d9476d808438144ebdc331bc70c0c80250967e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/3ad1a4313e0b1c6fc6bb6c7b686087b10a30c87a","verification":{"payload":"tree f2d9476d808438144ebdc331bc70c0c80250967e\nparent e2695034994973a690436d793c0517334e5d2b49\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791313957 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791313957 -0600\n\nfeat: Add an internal managed-run capability query (#14408)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add the exact native `--__internal-managed-run-capabilities` query\nbefore normal CLI/shim initialization. It does not read repository\nconfiguration, infer or spawn a local CLI, start telemetry/profiles,\nwrite guidance, or change descriptor limits.\n- Define a versioned JSON ABI bounded to 4 KiB, with a validated decoder\nthat rejects unknown ABI versions, malformed/duplicate/unknown fields,\nand invalid metadata. CLI versions are diagnostic only; compatibility is\nexplicit lock-schema membership.\n- Keep the production `managedRunSchemas` list empty. Lock parsing and\npartial setup delivery do not establish the complete activation,\ndrift-validation, strict/loose task-environment, and hashing contract.\n- Cover malformed roots, missing JavaScript tools, local pins, ambient\noverrides, profile arguments, and closed output streams. No feature\ndocumentation is added.\n\n```text\nnative CLI entry\n  → exact capability query\n    → bounded JSON, managedRunSchemas: []\n  → otherwise: existing initialization and shim routing\n```\n\nThis is the approved ABI-foundation split of TURBO-6202. Metadata\ngating, bounded local probing, and handoff enforcement remain a separate\nPR after this foundation and schema PR #14400 are both on main. The\nparent issue is not completed by this change.\n\nCloses TURBO-6307.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxUglCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAy5EQADMI/nvysy6yJhJ07KuBqCMj\nIIfcL/UQXUndJ3NyTWLYv7w3vOEDN78CEY19SCk9aCW0jaVbVLswC7I8lYfaMn4P\nVniGfJ+5hiQI/1aTJaecywYFIXVLCt8QDuXruYK/KdN1qyXU6qXFEalUGgITfs8Y\nJ9xQ+efBjUq9iW0FZQ87C7MKISvIlsJIlDheinrv/lw2pJwBW3Vxy8U4xo1xtDsq\nDR9PxykfJtLNLrhci7bdON/ywGKfyZBsUomopgM9s8rrk+ZjtUdQpVmlYpk1dZH0\nPmfXsNqHonoyxS3KNSC1VPS2m99MMwSXzUP8Ps9swSbGdFjCRHe+o55rzN6jyWHj\nFl+PykqkLUJ0QCal4jNP+56THTjaNqu28LqknI83lzV7JXoHLgZpaLbdh7a2o/Gm\noSALQqNEXW7wTDU0Eudxcg5oU8BABAN4+QWtQIbesEzTs4F+6O9OxEmXcSAT30ik\nAiqwIdPaROA87w3J1FYEgY8sWxIefsM6MfSmhtqvykyVerQ6AUkhtYumBnj4oMPv\nUDyqLdvOg3Qla6uwNU0uEEKUIv9pXApr4OBOaVJAvStowXWxu121QD2vCWbEkqi+\nsFq5SgaXSs7W5iRpfNPI4vqWTKNB5dQgrqwMmYFpS2esXSMEKj63o63luHe9CvHf\nkB6If4LnbRa7UlisTICs\n=FheH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T19:12:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/3ad1a4313e0b1c6fc6bb6c7b686087b10a30c87a","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDNhZDFhNDMxM2UwYjFjNmZjNmJiNmM3YjY4NjA4N2IxMGEzMGM4N2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/e2695034994973a690436d793c0517334e5d2b49","sha":"e2695034994973a690436d793c0517334e5d2b49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/e2695034994973a690436d793c0517334e5d2b49"}],"sha":"3ad1a4313e0b1c6fc6bb6c7b686087b10a30c87a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/3ad1a4313e0b1c6fc6bb6c7b686087b10a30c87a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/e2695034994973a690436d793c0517334e5d2b49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:12:29Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:12:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: Preserve Node runtime failure policy provenance (#14406)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Preserve explicitly authored Node runtime `onFail: \"error\"` as source\nprovenance, including object/array locations and name-only declarations.\n- Diagnose advisory `warn`/`ignore` policies as unsupported until setup\nimplements their semantics. Reject malformed policies instead of\nsilently falling back to another source.\n- Keep policy provenance out of the version-alternative set so it cannot\nadmit an unconstrained release.\n\n```text\nNode runtime declaration\n├── Version request → constrained resolver alternative\n├── Explicit onFail: error → provenance-only source\n└── Advisory or invalid onFail → focused discovery error\n```\n\nOnce incorporated into the writer''s ancestry, its existing native probe\nconsumes all discovery sources, so authored policy additions/removals\nbecome visible to declaration comparison without release resolution.\nThis main-based fix adds no installer, user documentation, or\nwriter/schema code.\n\nReferences TURBO-6203 and the accepted native-drift finding in #14399.\nThe writer issue remains incomplete until its storage and provenance\nfixes are incorporated.","tree":{"sha":"f7eee03061571678f64bcbfe42d399464a914472","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/f7eee03061571678f64bcbfe42d399464a914472"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/e2695034994973a690436d793c0517334e5d2b49","verification":{"payload":"tree f7eee03061571678f64bcbfe42d399464a914472\nparent 8aa9a8a4bcfa3d5a8792337ddc4fa75ea044b8da\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791313949 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791313949 -0600\n\nfix: Preserve Node runtime failure policy provenance (#14406)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Preserve explicitly authored Node runtime `onFail: \"error\"` as source\nprovenance, including object/array locations and name-only declarations.\n- Diagnose advisory `warn`/`ignore` policies as unsupported until setup\nimplements their semantics. Reject malformed policies instead of\nsilently falling back to another source.\n- Keep policy provenance out of the version-alternative set so it cannot\nadmit an unconstrained release.\n\n```text\nNode runtime declaration\n├── Version request → constrained resolver alternative\n├── Explicit onFail: error → provenance-only source\n└── Advisory or invalid onFail → focused discovery error\n```\n\nOnce incorporated into the writer''s ancestry, its existing native probe\nconsumes all discovery sources, so authored policy additions/removals\nbecome visible to declaration comparison without release resolution.\nThis main-based fix adds no installer, user documentation, or\nwriter/schema code.\n\nReferences TURBO-6203 and the accepted native-drift finding in #14399.\nThe writer issue remains incomplete until its storage and provenance\nfixes are incorporated.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxUgdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbs4QAB7qwySOG5lL0D9oCFRyxof5\nTaca+17mKHkqRD2K1QiuRm8gT6neLdSsOCIdQeo5yvPmnxgGbybBjw0DNbSd9WrF\nuaCOmHrdeorHp0LoJG2rxNPa/NGub/lTdEqqhiAhwGYbmll8pqF