s/8aa9a8a4bcfa3d5a8792337ddc4fa75ea044b8da"}],"sha":"e2695034994973a690436d793c0517334e5d2b49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/e2695034994973a690436d793c0517334e5d2b49"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/8aa9a8a4bcfa3d5a8792337ddc4fa75ea044b8da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:10:11Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:10:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: Preserve scoped tool paths and owner-executable exports (#14403)\n\n## Summary\n\nFollow-up to merged #14398, independently based on `main`.\n\n```text\nTool IDs / shim names -> Strict bookkeeping validation\nArtifact paths       -> Safe scoped / case-preserving validation\nResolved export      -> In-tree regular file + owner execute\nHealthy inventory    -> No-op\nInvalid staged tree  -> Prior generation stays selected\n```\n\n- Accept safe scoped directories, dotfiles, and exact-case executable\npaths without loosening tool IDs or owned shim names. Keep traversal,\nseparators, Windows device/ADS hazards, trailing dots/spaces, and\nnonportable bytes rejected.\n- Require owner execute on resolved direct and symlink exports.\nPreviously accepted group/other-only modes no longer establish readiness\nor a healthy no-op.\n- Preserve symlink containment, full-resource reuse, shim ownership, and\natomic publication. No Node adapter, `is_current` API, schema,\ndependencies, cleanup, or feature docs are included.\n\n## Boundaries\n\nRepository/temp parents and installer-owned staging are trusted; hostile\nsame-user concurrent mutation remains outside the threat model. The\nclone-local inventory remains bookkeeping, not activation authorization.\nNative Windows qualification is unchanged.\n\nThe focused inventory patch applies cleanly to #14402''s current library\nand preserves its separate `Store::is_current` addition. That PR still\nneeds to integrate this fix; it is not part of this branch.","tree":{"sha":"b66298011ee4ce9e90690a3f91662de4673e2ce2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/b66298011ee4ce9e90690a3f91662de4673e2ce2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/8aa9a8a4bcfa3d5a8792337ddc4fa75ea044b8da","verification":{"payload":"tree b66298011ee4ce9e90690a3f91662de4673e2ce2\nparent 56a0826e7201ae6dc924531d0049d6256f54a6d0\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791313811 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791313811 -0600\n\nfix: Preserve scoped tool paths and owner-executable exports (#14403)\n\n## Summary\n\nFollow-up to merged #14398, independently based on `main`.\n\n```text\nTool IDs / shim names -> Strict bookkeeping validation\nArtifact paths       -> Safe scoped / case-preserving validation\nResolved export      -> In-tree regular file + owner execute\nHealthy inventory    -> No-op\nInvalid staged tree  -> Prior generation stays selected\n```\n\n- Accept safe scoped directories, dotfiles, and exact-case executable\npaths without loosening tool IDs or owned shim names. Keep traversal,\nseparators, Windows device/ADS hazards, trailing dots/spaces, and\nnonportable bytes rejected.\n- Require owner execute on resolved direct and symlink exports.\nPreviously accepted group/other-only modes no longer establish readiness\nor a healthy no-op.\n- Preserve symlink containment, full-resource reuse, shim ownership, and\natomic publication. No Node adapter, `is_current` API, schema,\ndependencies, cleanup, or feature docs are included.\n\n## Boundaries\n\nRepository/temp parents and installer-owned staging are trusted; hostile\nsame-user concurrent mutation remains outside the threat model. The\nclone-local inventory remains bookkeeping, not activation authorization.\nNative Windows qualification is unchanged.\n\nThe focused inventory patch applies cleanly to #14402''s current library\nand preserves its separate `Store::is_current` addition. That PR still\nneeds to integrate this fix; it is not part of this branch.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxUeTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA/MQAGPk6RkAUA2YKubef+6eb+f+\nApifOFZ4diYJjlJdn860tNbZu3SNHSacWu0s9ud2ftmLr2qN6DTGZmhq8b0eP2Vr\n8Nuz04UbHY4ddDVSlyV/XrqmVAlj2Ug6x+FWxnsspMO+iK5F/c8kw+iAjRaZE7Zz\ntmyuJycXOGmGpkbSOwwpUDOYDLnMT8iqEwZOvUSocKRp9wBcZHzY2nCQz5z2XQZN\nXQmRPA6ZfSbvRUkzD4odrqezBUz6nwsrAc9B3CdeXbrQVMhF3d9KG5uuYX6ciQi7\nv9aHu0JEMINaH9nchMgyPNvuWtgIfn7NJUm0EEGpRbhjUvVM7/WJEDsAo2+HW3Sj\n2y6w9C/hT699hDCIuimXJmqrIl3ll5O6Fa96dPRtOx9F4sI11crtNOVEOMwJraQq\nuUVdkp7RB52f2M8fysvYhWGQb58b4yqAYhwzbqsOhfFjB+8L0euUJpKUILaE+2ns\n2s+KbjtK59Kvj6IZq7EicC7mxVSPUZeyiMyfdgPEVkTZV/+KAdRv5YEonyS3JJSv\n2TbfPNGvZls4i1aQIRRrtj8nxHUHnStnMETZ/NkZcfrtTYAgLRF9FM9XjYhHlaSS\nVAFqFV+qzIVOvmHt/FhXEBSrHI6vfmnIfB1Pfgk2i7i9PROJXextpxCJo5y1ZJ5F\nCUNOnNwGmp/wI33Bzu2U\n=hHYO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T19:10:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/8aa9a8a4bcfa3d5a8792337ddc4fa75ea044b8da","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDhhYTlhOGE0YmNmYTNkNWE4NzkyMzM3ZGRjNGZhNzVlYTA0NGI4ZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/56a0826e7201ae6dc924531d0049d6256f54a6d0","sha":"56a0826e7201ae6dc924531d0049d6256f54a6d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/56a0826e7201ae6dc924531d0049d6256f54a6d0"}],"sha":"8aa9a8a4bcfa3d5a8792337ddc4fa75ea044b8da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/8aa9a8a4bcfa3d5a8792337ddc4fa75ea044b8da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/56a0826e7201ae6dc924531d0049d6256f54a6d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:07:37Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:07:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Validate portable setup tool resolutions (#14400)\n\n## Summary\n\nDefine the prelaunch `turbo.lock` tool-resolution schema and a bounded,\nvalidated read-only API. This does not write locks, install tools,\nactivate executables, or resolve versions.\n\n```text\nnative declarations\n  → schemaVersion 0 + exact tool identity\n    → managed platform artifact sets OR verified-system executable requirements\n      → validated immutable lock\n```\n\n- Reject duplicate JSON keys, unknown structural fields, unsupported\nschema versions, unsafe paths, credential-bearing transport metadata,\nand co-active executable collisions.\n- Keep tool and adapter IDs open. Adapter-owned exact identities\naccommodate non-npm releases; current Node/npm/pnpm identities require\ncanonical exact versions.\n- Preserve portable provenance, composed artifact destinations,\nresource-only components, executable mappings, and canonical semantic\noption sets.\n- Keep `any` artifact selection separate from execution-platform/cache\ncompatibility. Treat archive-content validation and adapter execution\nsupport as consumer responsibilities.\n- Exclude dependency graphs and local installation state. No feature\ndocumentation is added.\n\nFixes TURBO-6196","tree":{"sha":"24b5b1ff0248da8aa885273bcff34dc9810b8b28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/24b5b1ff0248da8aa885273bcff34dc9810b8b28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/56a0826e7201ae6dc924531d0049d6256f54a6d0","verification":{"payload":"tree 24b5b1ff0248da8aa885273bcff34dc9810b8b28\nparent 0c1db56e20fdc06085cce3874b330cbe06c1dc75\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791313657 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791313657 -0600\n\nfeat: Validate portable setup tool resolutions (#14400)\n\n## Summary\n\nDefine the prelaunch `turbo.lock` tool-resolution schema and a bounded,\nvalidated read-only API. This does not write locks, install tools,\nactivate executables, or resolve versions.\n\n```text\nnative declarations\n  → schemaVersion 0 + exact tool identity\n    → managed platform artifact sets OR verified-system executable requirements\n      → validated immutable lock\n```\n\n- Reject duplicate JSON keys, unknown structural fields, unsupported\nschema versions, unsafe paths, credential-bearing transport metadata,\nand co-active executable collisions.\n- Keep tool and adapter IDs open. Adapter-owned exact identities\naccommodate non-npm releases; current Node/npm/pnpm identities require\ncanonical exact versions.\n- Preserve portable provenance, composed artifact destinations,\nresource-only components, executable mappings, and canonical semantic\noption sets.\n- Keep `any` artifact selection separate from execution-platform/cache\ncompatibility. Treat archive-content validation and adapter execution\nsupport as consumer responsibilities.\n- Exclude dependency graphs and local installation state. No feature\ndocumentation is added.\n\nFixes TURBO-6196","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxUb6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8vIQAGGY5MoU3R0PET8iyZRVmNq3\n5CQ2ncisRCeXilTWUUUKJ