31401c3851b077dce72c01b8c931a357bd9d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/e0931401c3851b077dce72c01b8c931a357bd9d0"}],"sha":"ebf78f69d96bc213bd38a99754e782027f8d40bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/ebf78f69d96bc213bd38a99754e782027f8d40bb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/e0931401c3851b077dce72c01b8c931a357bd9d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T16:27:18Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T16:27:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: Avoid duplicate code CI on pull request reviews (#14414)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Keep code checks on PR updates and pushes to `main`, but skip code\njobs and cache cleanup on review events.\n- Separate review and code concurrency groups so reviews cannot cancel\nin-progress code checks.\n- Preserve the required `CI Summary` check: reviews reuse a successful\n`Code checks` aggregate for the latest matching PR revision and run\nattempt, then evaluate the current review policy using the trusted\ndefault-branch validator.\n\n```text\nPR update\n  Code jobs → Code checks → Current review policy → CI Summary\n\nPR review\n  Wait for matching Code checks → Current review policy → CI Summary\n```\n\nThe review validator rejects mismatched PRs, revisions, bases,\nworkflows, failed aggregates, and stale run attempts. It polls when a\ncode run or aggregate is not yet visible, and does not wait for\nunrelated cleanup once code checks succeed.\n\n## Rollout\n\nExisting PRs need a fresh PR-event run under the new workflow to produce\nthe labelled `Code checks` aggregate. Legacy `CI Summary` results are\nintentionally not accepted as code evidence. Review events still create\na lightweight summary run; they no longer rerun the code suite.","tree":{"sha":"01159d976831ea82851b6fa452a01669f947e35b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/01159d976831ea82851b6fa452a01669f947e35b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/e0931401c3851b077dce72c01b8c931a357bd9d0","verification":{"payload":"tree 01159d976831ea82851b6fa452a01669f947e35b\nparent 7dba02edee4ebe63b68cfbcad0d5fde8e85da24f\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791304038 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791304038 -0600\n\nfix: Avoid duplicate code CI on pull request reviews (#14414)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Keep code checks on PR updates and pushes to `main`, but skip code\njobs and cache cleanup on review events.\n- Separate review and code concurrency groups so reviews cannot cancel\nin-progress code checks.\n- Preserve the required `CI Summary` check: reviews reuse a successful\n`Code checks` aggregate for the latest matching PR revision and run\nattempt, then evaluate the current review policy using the trusted\ndefault-branch validator.\n\n```text\nPR update\n  Code jobs → Code checks → Current review policy → CI Summary\n\nPR review\n  Wait for matching Code checks → Current review policy → CI Summary\n```\n\nThe review validator rejects mismatched PRs, revisions, bases,\nworkflows, failed aggregates, and stale run attempts. It polls when a\ncode run or aggregate is not yet visible, and does not wait for\nunrelated cleanup once code checks succeed.\n\n## Rollout\n\nExisting PRs need a fresh PR-event run under the new workflow to produce\nthe labelled `Code checks` aggregate. Legacy `CI Summary` results are\nintentionally not accepted as code evidence. Review events still create\na lightweight summary run; they no longer rerun the code suite.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxSFmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0X4QACN/DJTW+Ulm1d3Y5bz4OgYb\nkAaY4zcxm79rLoDZA8gVPk7wJpefKHa8EqKlLMe8yOhd1Tg1XuHHtLXjDcZdVYTm\nx6ucT9L75JmgocQ3sRLuVVsVBPT4kNl7l9/VkbkYqtv0k3uCVsrHW8XW93fQwpaQ\npSt66bvSgoyKkvnOfs0o0/5okf9tu6s51JhSKE1XrWfbsBtZXQxw3pUzmQ9gZobp\nWK4T+a6MkpNOPmf9pkzC22Ny7RMKyDoCYTqNoHjo+eOsscV2/jsFgV3zFStxOXnH\nNEx4KPa0D8Bidp5C00ErJvYM3jI07mn0/duQXQCX2r5zyMILnwcHp9/S7lQN6r8H\nRRTl/KSFT8SvjS0Gaqeeh8OZ3OfB4FtxCDZtOqdOW+FcyoC7rjgcl5hBbZD4Qm3F\n5aoZ1xZp6Ivp0/tzLLlu8dXeAtvDmut0gbE+eVSkv7bqcG2GexxExlpQ7ITdljMj\nQPvnc0/uVbaHSJeF/lqcCDKfTBqQ3T5p6pA2eavPznqtY7UF4ompw9JUAf3rB3lh\ntqTbycuIuwQtXtvUqcyq4OgzBccb0XJPcicUzJlegAIcfEdsuW1hCKNNKpTnMZXZ\ntOTA1vfRZlF4Ks0x2Buuh+olT5Tpjfz+byL3qzt2vO8YQglySnP2CRktrtwT/Hli\nZX5vaK6FsOb2erKHrOm2\n=4Rzp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T16:27:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MD