ommit/52bea749ff98079d89ee968657d2a3859cd77c07","sha":"52bea749ff98079d89ee968657d2a3859cd77c07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/52bea749ff98079d89ee968657d2a3859cd77c07"}],"sha":"bca05164dbf5f9eadf46d7e39e0c4f348d1995ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/bca05164dbf5f9eadf46d7e39e0c4f348d1995ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/52bea749ff98079d89ee968657d2a3859cd77c07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:17:44Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:17:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Add atomic managed tool installation inventory (#14398)\n\nFixes TURBO-6200\n\nAdds a clone/worktree-local managed installation primitive. It owns\n`.turbo/tools/manifest.json`, stages full tool trees with adjacent\nresources and owned shims, and publishes the desired inventory through\none atomic manifest replacement.\n\n```text\nPrevious generation stays intact\n            │\n            ▼\nStage desired tools + owned bin\n            │\n            ▼\nValidate identities, paths, tree hashes and executables\n            │\n            ▼\nSync staged state → atomically replace manifest.json\n                              │\n                              └─ Selected bin contains only desired tools\n```\n\n- Reuses unchanged verified local trees and makes an unchanged desired\ninventory a no-op.\n- Keeps failed/interrupted staging from replacing the prior valid\ngeneration. Old generations remain inactive for the separate cleanup\nmilestone.\n- Rejects unsafe bookkeeping paths, escaping symlinks, executable\ncollisions, special files and hard-linked tool files.\n- Keeps exact tool/platform/artifact identities independent of the\nseparate `turbo.lock` schema work.\n\nNo downloads, installers, tool-specific adapters, CLI provisioning or\nactivation are added. This local inventory is not a trust record: later\nactivation must authorize setup-recorded tools using user state outside\nthe repository. Windows installation is explicitly unsupported pending\nnative qualification.","tree":{"sha":"b2ba7d66abd9a3e0de488ed86ee518f55412d1f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/b2ba7d66abd9a3e0de488ed86ee518f55412d1f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/52bea749ff98079d89ee968657d2a3859cd77c07","verification":{"payload":"tree b2ba7d66abd9a3e0de488ed86ee518f55412d1f1\nparent 0f5f850dad6deefaee66b288a3466e81484dd70d\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791292664 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791292664 -0600\n\nfeat: Add atomic managed tool installation inventory (#14398)\n\nFixes TURBO-6200\n\nAdds a clone/worktree-local managed installation primitive. It owns\n`.turbo/tools/manifest.json`, stages full tool trees with adjacent\nresources and owned shims, and publishes the desired inventory through\none atomic manifest replacement.\n\n```text\nPrevious generation stays intact\n            │\n            ▼\nStage desired tools + owned bin\n            │\n            ▼\nValidate identities, paths, tree hashes and executables\n            │\n            ▼\nSync staged state → atomically replace manifest.json\n                              │\n                              └─ Selected bin contains only desired tools\n```\n\n- Reuses unchanged verified local trees and makes an unchanged desired\ninventory a no-op.\n- Keeps failed/interrupted staging from replacing the prior valid\ngeneration. Old generations remain inactive for the separate cleanup\nmilestone.\n- Rejects unsafe bookkeeping paths, escaping symlinks, executable\ncollisions, special files and hard-linked tool files.\n- Keeps exact tool/platform/artifact identities independent of the\nseparate `turbo.lock` schema work.\n\nNo downloads, installers, tool-specific adapters, CLI provisioning or\nactivation are added. This local inventory is not a trust record: later\nactivation must authorize setup-recorded tools using user state outside\nthe repository. Windows installation is explicitly unsupported pending\nnative qualification.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxPT4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHAoQAJADSVt01BJU1x1fsk1BcBlV\nOIvUZd2VI0AoLykMQM2dQTzJ6PM9kwItoGiUZJc2yUsse4v203lhKBNPsowOErzo\n81wVJytncnaMZmS+IpDBxGbemQXSH1dJnz/NogXq1TtMGAiNhLmbICVIiVYgkuix\n+gmtsCGn3ZfWgwW4EGBszm9mjOfTSPQQ3H0HHgGRIOmIrVB82C+ws1ct1oh/OsBg\n3gVdw41a3qe6fUE/4TYxRU8QNX4fclHP/GcUN/rJYGyJI/xBe5I3lUtvHLizPKa5\nkfAdW3RqnhS9bOVVD90OIxG7yNOa/NAF9OecWgxruUn6jQ7fmJwac4mH80GKhNDG\nM1g9VV9HSVRSKuB1+uRvkclR86B019the/d3XG2FHdMvZsVBjuRcmDGqfWPpeFl+\niPF4u5gcIYHIBoUlhve6TiQpmRQZJLerhwG8geVUKRtJj4Jn/4REoJZqPM/XpKNg\nf1qz20LkeFDlB/VvPjYHe44vzAtMx59cK2oYaIOM3fM4NtSY3RZmuN8MqRkZdzTE\nmH4qUCdu2l0ekGXPUxvrhkNzrQYQhoDfGNUPIkNg/DrTePaWC+H3XEMRHGPfgXKF\nlSKXh0YKA9n5v84QqIjS50ToHszRqCDB11EaOC3eHiL/q9nmvcQsXj4BlyTATZfy\n8bIe29Lr+LcTpi/2o7B7\n=9Z84\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T13:17:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/52bea749ff98079d89ee968657d2a3859cd77c07","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDUyYmVhNzQ5ZmY5ODA3OWQ4OWVlOTY4NjU3ZDJhMzg1OWNkNzdjMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/0f5f850dad6deefaee66b288a3466e81484dd70d","sha":"0f5f850dad6deefaee66b288a3466e81484dd70d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/0f5f850dad6deefaee66b288a3466e81484dd70d"}],"sha":"52bea749ff98079d89ee968657d2a3859cd77c07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/52bea749ff98079d89ee968657d2a3859cd77c07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/0f5f850dad6deefaee66b288a3466e81484dd70d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:55:43Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:55:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Infer setup roots without package managers (#14395)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes TURBO-6201.\n\n- Infer setup roots from nested directories and `--cwd` without Node.js,\na package manager, or language-tool probes, including pure Cargo,\nuv/Python, and Go repositories.\n- Distinguish package configurations from root configurations, enforce\nGit clone/worktree boundaries, and name ambiguous or secondary workspace\nroots with actionable `--cwd` guidance.\n- Ignore native root markers when their corresponding experimental\nworkspace flag is off, matching the product spec''s discovery and\nprovisioning decision.\n\n## Discovery flow\n\n```text\nturbo setup [--cwd=<directory>]\n  Native shim bypasses JS inference and local-binary handoff\n  Canonicalize the starting directory\n  Find root configuration within the Git boundary\n    Package configuration → Continue to its root\n    Multiple roots → Diagnose paths; require an explicit root\n  Read root future flags\n  Check intervening JS and enabled native workspace markers\n    Secondary root → Diagnose marker and selected root\n  Require experimentalSetup\n  Pass through to the existing not-implemented executor\n```\n\nThis is a read-only discovery slice. Provisioning, planning, checking,\nlock changes, and compatible local CLI handoff remain separate work;\nsetup still never schedules Turborepo tasks.","tree":{"sha":"2a63de01b99cefdbddb21021f2faee6f3c6efeb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/2a63de01b99cefdbddb21021f2faee6f3c6efeb9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/0f5f850dad6deefaee66b288a3466e81484dd70d","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a63de01b99cefdbddb21021f2faee6f3c6efeb9\nparent 132b0a233605297f7972e69416cde5b52ad9fa9b\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791291343 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791291343 -0600\n\nfeat: Infer setup roots without package managers (#14395)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes TURBO-6201.\n\n- Infer setup roots from nested directories and `--cwd` without Node.js,\na package manager, or language-tool probes, including pure Cargo,\nuv/Python, and Go repositories.\n- Distinguish package configurations from root configurations, enforce\nGit clone/worktree boundaries, and name ambiguous or secondary workspace\nroots with actionable `--cwd` guidance.\n- Ignore native root markers when their corresponding experimental\nworkspace flag is off, matching the product spec''s discovery and\nprovisioning decision.\n\n## Discovery flow\n\n```text\nturbo setup [--cwd=<directory>]\n  Native shim bypasses JS inference and local-binary handoff\n  Canonicalize the starting directory\n  Find root configuration within the Git boundary\n    Package configuration → Continue to its root\n    Multiple roots → Diagnose paths; require an explicit root\n  Read root future flags\n  Check intervening JS and enabled native workspace markers\n    Secondary root → Diagnose marker and selected root\n  Require experimentalSetup\n  Pass through to the existing not-implemented executor\n```\n\nThis is a read-only discovery slice. Provisioning, planning, checking,\nlock changes, and compatible local CLI handoff remain separate work;\nsetup still never schedules Turborepo tasks.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxO/QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX5oQABz5tDrdmRLb/QW1sDHSdqJb\njAjcTdSB+YbGWjWgKEFJPbVLO3ia/JUqK1RUhAHOyei4xnyi1ZKoh3oVyxy+gqkl\nUg1ZyLoEZ7Wj87bhX+PQ6i7u5WBGmWK5bhQOa/i1AfJ75aZe+clLMeUf7dxxd3/w\n+Fp30XseljU4ybqAEXFrVdGS37oTC2cSLJwBWzbC9lvTcb1JfcuRUN12qFRxvI+Z\nmkVP0yXu0lcPI/K2Si29QPCWBKHgdoEjprbm3T5vdU2YO7HPoJZWsL/oJ7yuxVLK\nyuOfwNoWxJURfhFpbb9zs2OlFj+mEPkOU+gfMiTIl6G+yC057ij2wIGbnjsmpM55\nvrz4kd5OI6g+O/PC5xLG9TF1kkmb+bfOe52aS3QkmSjW4GDP841HDd7Y6StFlU2s\ns5wtV0El/6ktlxG/mOwu14zjWKfd6m4K+FPWWVc/s8uD+g21FFQHvpPVp/gZEYXe\nLbulYXLIZMlKXt7jS97zjDdXhgp75JTCmWN1vHqx9acAA6W87vKo4XFYYc1MEpoo\n7Fk32Zv3cIQevo8HUtdLoSlhIEpI+QmYQTIysYg32fpaLKmLlnHKfY4oDCk1n2jS\npCd2SAOq/mV5PGsAKCN/bsXW/XMNGcOQ2qPAMMNPBAn8sZasELavqiIUB4YhsXy6\nWFWuTbbhHsbmhJA+PJjW\n=kXjg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T12:55:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/0f5f850dad6deefaee66b288a3466e81484dd70d","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDBmNWY4NTBkYWQ2ZGVlZmFlZTY2YjI4OGEzNDY2ZTgxNDg0ZGQ3MGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/132b0a233605297f7972e69416cde5b52ad9fa9b","sha":"132b0a233605297f7972e69416cde5b52ad9fa9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/132b0a233605297f7972e69416cde5b52ad9fa9b"}],"sha":"0f5f850dad6deefaee66b288a3466e81484dd70d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/0f5f850dad6deefaee66b288a3466e81484dd70d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/132b0a233605297f7972e69416cde5b52ad9fa9b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:37:36Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:37:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Extract safe Node TAR symlinks (#14393)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes TURBO-6301.\n\nSupport the relative npm/npx/corepack symlinks used by Node TAR\ndistributions at the verified extraction boundary from #14384.\n\n```text\nVerified TAR bytes\n  Extract regular files + reserve link paths\n  Validate in-root targets + acyclic filesystem graph\n  Create Unix symlinks last\n  Failure or drop → Remove owned staging\n```\n\n- Preserve the complete installation tree, including runtime resources,\nheaders, manuals, and licenses.\n- Reject absolute/escaping targets, dangling or aliased targets, file\nand directory cycles, collisions, and writes through links. Intermediate\ntarget components must be real directories; terminal link chains are\nsupported.\n- Keep link paths and targets bounded. Required layout files remain\nregular files. Hard links and GNU long-link metadata remain unsupported.\n- Keep this TAR-only and independent of ZIP work, HTTP, CLI wiring, and\ninstallation/promotion.\n\n## Native qualification\n\nRan generated local extraction fixtures on native macOS arm64 under\n`umask 0700`, including npm/npx target reads, link chains, directory\nlinks, and cleanup after partial symlink creation. This exposed and\nfixed macOS symlink permission masking using a no-follow permission\nupdate that leaves target modes unchanged.\n\nThis qualifies fixture extraction only, not a complete Node\ninstaller/runtime or Linux/Windows support. Non-Unix symlink extraction\nfails explicitly. The OS temp parent and same-user processes remain\ntrusted, as in the precursor.","tree":{"sha":"aa5ed6ccfbcc25e5c8f19d6427b5db4b7bdb7c6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/aa5ed6ccfbcc25e5c8f19d6427b5db4b7bdb7c6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/132b0a233605297f7972e69416cde5b52ad9fa9b","verification":{"payload":"tree aa5ed6ccfbcc25e5c8f19d6427b5db4b7bdb7c6d\nparent 46064de17f9f85755963ef146e0cc289f5298fbd\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791290256 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791290256 -0600\n\nfeat: Extract safe Node TAR symlinks (#14393)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes TURBO-6301.\n\nSupport the relative npm/npx/corepack symlinks used by Node TAR\ndistributions at the verified extraction boundary from #14384.\n\n```text\nVerified TAR bytes\n  Extract regular files + reserve link paths\n  Validate in-root targets + acyclic filesystem graph\n  Create Unix symlinks last\n  Failure or drop → Remove owned staging\n```\n\n- Preserve the complete installation tree, including runtime resources,\nheaders, manuals, and licenses.\n- Reject absolute/escaping targets, dangling or aliased targets, file\nand directory cycles, collisions, and writes through links. Intermediate\ntarget components must be real directories; terminal link chains are\nsupported.\n- Keep link paths and targets bounded. Required layout files remain\nregular files. Hard links and GNU long-link metadata remain unsupported.\n- Keep this TAR-only and independent of ZIP work, HTTP, CLI wiring, and\ninstallation/promotion.\n\n## Native qualification\n\nRan generated local extraction fixtures on native macOS arm64 under\n`umask 0700`, including npm/npx target reads, link chains, directory\nlinks, and cleanup after partial symlink creation. This exposed and\nfixed macOS symlink permission masking using a no-follow permission\nupdate that leaves target modes unchanged.\n\nThis qualifies fixture extraction only, not a complete Node\ninstaller/runtime or Linux/Windows support. Non-Unix symlink extraction\nfails explicitly. The OS temp parent and same-user processes remain\ntrusted, as in the precursor.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxOuQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6QIQAK9a4vvSr+dR21qn8W3SG5V5\nLrTtBuVtbBOrnUVGHAIrRB7kPLPWoOwNvrpTaA3k+cEl3Hn3sJuu++AskERs+m6Q\n7xWOkmWY/K62ffT8YNZmijHU92gUt1K4I4ZUMzztBa0fyLL8gsRTSUJTdp7xLK1O\nxF3k5MHOwGq3Hjaky/8e7fzlIGxX8yya7DGfKYz+/a+5kiv5L/CZp+/lN6p