https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/489d5e02cd4bb908ade90f50edeb4382202074d5"}],"sha":"2872e914a1fc4a548a3f1a07c44712c7fcec5b06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/2872e914a1fc4a548a3f1a07c44712c7fcec5b06"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/489d5e02cd4bb908ade90f50edeb4382202074d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T03:15:03Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T03:15:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Add experimental setup command surface (#14385)\n\n### Summary\n\nCloses TURBO-6195.\n\nIntroduce the experimental standalone setup command surface without\nrequiring Node.js, a package manager, or a built repository-local CLI.\n\n```text\nGlobal setup routing\n  Native parsing/help             No JS inference or local bootstrap\n  Execution                       Root experimentalSetup gate\n  Typed normalized request        Honest not-implemented diagnostic\n```\n\n- Add the settled plan/check, force, frozen/no-frozen, offline,\ntools-only, no-lock, and update-lock controls with conflict and\nCI-default normalization.\n- Keep setup on the global command path while preserving ordinary\nrun/handoff behavior.\n- Suppress profile creation before setup parsing, including help and\nmalformed task-only tails, so plan/check cannot write through profiling\nstartup.\n- Align help, configuration documentation, and the future-flag schema\ndescriptions with the command surface.\n\nProvisioning, plan/check execution, automatic root inference,\nmanaged-run compatibility, and lock handling remain separate work. The\nempty backend never reports prepared success, including for\n`--__test-run`, and runs no tasks or installers.\n\n### Manual verification\n\nBuilt the `heap-dhat` variant and exercised setup help/gates,\nplan/check, heap/Chrome profiling options, and malformed tails with an\nexisting profile file, an empty `PATH`, and a loopback HTTP monitor. The\nfixture retained its complete filesystem snapshot and recorded no HTTP\nconnection.","tree":{"sha":"4e384b73efa547595a3426998ef03cd075ea61d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/4e384b73efa547595a3426998ef03cd075ea61d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/489d5e02cd4bb908ade90f50edeb4382202074d5","verification":{"payload":"tree 4e384b73efa547595a3426998ef03cd075ea61d4\nparent 84c5860b9efefde996363331e7345191da2d403b\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791256503 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791256503 -0600\n\nfeat: Add experimental setup command surface (#14385)\n\n### Summary\n\nCloses TURBO-6195.\n\nIntroduce the experimental standalone setup command surface without\nrequiring Node.js, a package manager, or a built repository-local CLI.\n\n```text\nGlobal setup routing\n  Native parsing/help             No JS inference or local bootstrap\n  Execution                       Root experimentalSetup gate\n  Typed normalized request        Honest not-implemented diagnostic\n```\n\n- Add the settled plan/check, force, frozen/no-frozen, offline,\ntools-only, no-lock, and update-lock controls with conflict and\nCI-default normalization.\n- Keep setup on the global command path while preserving ordinary\nrun/handoff behavior.\n- Suppress profile creation before setup parsing, including help and\nmalformed task-only tails, so plan/check cannot write through profiling\nstartup.\n- Align help, configuration documentation, and the future-flag schema\ndescriptions with the command surface.\n\nProvisioning, plan/check execution, automatic root inference,\nmanaged-run compatibility, and lock handling remain separate work. The\nempty backend never reports prepared success, including for\n`--__test-run`, and runs no tasks or installers.\n\n### Manual verification\n\nBuilt the `heap-dhat` variant and exercised setup help/gates,\nplan/check, heap/Chrome profiling options, and malformed tails with an\nexisting profile file, an empty `PATH`, and a loopback HTTP monitor. The\nfixture retained its complete filesystem snapshot and recorded no HTTP\nconnection.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxGe3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKZIQAJcDcj83JhAwJfelVDxpnH0Y\nxdd7bx2crzrLgpDNElxZAp8gljQ3JAgDJJpid9DVZ97vPcfZ/UDGRiJl9gwjXB4J\n6m8AFOhA5UEzJKki0z8DPdJMBRHVx4UDgXMzPcM4Q7IZzONd5U7yosbRRN/NDyN6\n6noWJA25jcE6xRHweymXayclGIr/3AE3fV9qifc96UxB9Y9UgTPNExXWwqGR99/U\nXBCfy3Ki2VqvohERNjDMtOUaIzaMNcA0JweSkYTTrh42Boa+lcPoSMvkIwqEz+vF\nD+zMx0PeSwrqDsQiQWDaWKG65Q/LFbSmP3Yp/x00k67pgXrlrs59AvLf8b2qP2XV\nqDMYI1Dg6dmENY0pMeZWlWjjeUPV4FwevnjGHJXEpM7N7yiOPbp+8Gu7t4BWNj9I\no1wiZrQ/MnXwuM5Cbxlf+z3upnKeZJDuSjDou8vnQuKJgUq28ABrxS4WK1uVFv0K\nRDG7tSpkWadF+vH7lLzj9cVQw91iKreHNaCZW+AlF8IcY87mye4QespKJNqSbZcR\nx2crLyskpL/UfvNMS7mVFW7f1/RZd6Cnae1sPX2J9SVAYMpRcRF2FNsCvAdTGGxQ\nMcpHdSzPi3mDcEKkeM6VMQieOuYL1v+hqxKSdOUFSCgtuyLwuB4KHyaDJldpLN/Y\nyWQ4l8d0hUtIjzj8xblr\n=UAXe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T03:15:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/489d5e02cd4bb908ade90f50edeb4382202074d5","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDQ4OWQ1ZTAyY2Q0YmI5MDhhZGU5MGY1MGVkZWI0MzgyMjAyMDc0ZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/84c5860b9efefde996363331e7345191da2d403b","sha":"84c5860b9efefde996363331e7345191da2d403b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/84c5860b9efefde996363331e7345191da2d403b"}],"sha":"489d5e02cd4bb908ade90f50edeb4382202074d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/489d5e02cd4bb908ade90f50edeb4382202074d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/84c5860b9efefde996363331e7345191da2d403b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T03:14:51Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T03:14:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Extract verified TAR archives into private staging (#14384)\n\n### Summary\n\nCloses TURBO-6300. Builds on #14383''s independently tested local-byte\nverification boundary.\n\n```text\nVerifiedArtifact\n  Decode within caller-selected limits\n  Validate paths, entry kinds, and expected layout\n  Write freshly owned private staging\n  Failure or drop -> Remove staging\n```\n\n- Bound compressed/decompressed bytes, raw entries, created nodes, and\npath length/depth.\n- Enforce conservative portable paths and reject traversal, aliases,\ncollisions, links, and unsupported special/PAX/sparse entries.\n- Support bounded GNU long names, preserve safe Unix executable bits,\nand restore cleanup-safe private directory modes.\n- Keep extraction separate from HTTP, ZIP, installation/promotion, and\nCLI wiring.\n\nAll links are explicitly rejected, including valid Node TAR symlinks.\nSafe Node symlinks remain TURBO-6301; this is not full Node distribution\ncompatibility. The OS temp parent and same-user processes are trusted.\nNative macOS/Windows qualification remains outstanding; no\nplatform-support claim is made.\n\n### Manual verification\n\nRan the extraction/mode/owned-cleanup fixture under `umask 0700`.\nStaging and extracted directories remained `0700`, executable modes were\npreserved with special bits stripped, and owned staging was removed on\ndrop.","tree":{"sha":"dbc0a6e365f3416078b1c6043eac12d87001ecc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/dbc0a6e365f3416078b1c6043eac12d87001ecc6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/84c5860b9efefde996363331e7345191da2d403b","verification":{"payload":"tree dbc0a6e365f3416078b1c6043eac12d87001ecc6\nparent 7b237ef7bcf8d176bff3f0b92de97e00f7cdf683\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791256491 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791256491 -0600\n\nfeat: Extract verified TAR archives into private staging (#14384)\n\n### Summary\n\nCloses TURBO-6300. Builds on #14383''s independently tested local-byte\nverification boundary.\n\n```text\nVerifiedArtifact\n  Decode within caller-selected limits\n  Validate paths, entry kinds, and expected layout\n  Write freshly owned private staging\n  Failure or drop -> Remove staging\n```\n\n- Bound compressed/decompressed bytes, raw entries, created nodes, and\npath length/depth.\n- Enforce conservative portable paths and reject traversal, aliases,\ncollisions, links, and unsupported special/PAX/sparse entries.\n- Support bounded GNU long names, preserve safe Unix executable bits,\nand restore cleanup-safe private directory modes.\n- Keep extraction separate from HTTP, ZIP, installation/promotion, and\nCLI wiring.\n\nAll links are explicitly rejected, including valid Node TAR symlinks.\nSafe Node symlinks remain TURBO-6301; this is not full Node distribution\ncompatibility. The OS temp parent and same-user processes are trusted.\nNative macOS/Windows qualification remains outstanding; no\nplatform-support claim is made.\n\n### Manual verification\n\nRan the extraction/mode/owned-cleanup fixture under `umask 0700`.\nStaging and extracted directories remained `0700`, executable modes were\npreserved with special bits stripped, and owned staging was removed on\ndrop.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxGerCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOegQABKikw0IA8jWGFVIWIB5usiC\nEo9ZOI1bQuXFdAvNsQK0GzmVhOAmZVmXfH/OByKfodi8lztbQXi16qUj2gWGBvv+\nGFNea2jCJ7fO34q/1J26+BilXcG06khb/oqarqULSOckttdaHs7e1RnK8uV343rD\n+hswvEsvsMqn8K95TqPXPk+K8IM7jkutfmTr4OOq/jHrUxe/Lqih3VWGCqK+NqZs\nyplG2WeEqsBQh5MBsrSMpmVZ9QwEZZpJfYrTfZsFnaaiv5Z8/8JWLYxJXMq2BWcj\nY32H5bNdfwVM8JVeijqMLpkdrUMJsvb3yLCE3itEglACc1TXd/LJmOwjq0zM7neu\nMiHW2kf8WiATexvKHtATdhFwa73a9His5bHHIAaFbUeR+0QBLAdwh5gyGYPEHMKJ\njBdQSEhc8iPUT6Oe7jx+yJ9R7fJJK3bPhRw0tPboFokmseMDzUsUlBT/+l+RcsMu\n3hiZuoWD2Rzy5YehfMx++GIBIYzHXXQF7QQ3SuR0fwRk0XnytNssNbozf1Ypp1yr\nQEyBa1M0VlN+74CUoMUx7098xFVMgEwYuf/db9qtdXJrF9cKyT7KvZwhbh1Sbq1w\n1MOucXOR2IxN7piueocWN2enqC2M3D6INr6P6yC4SMnDbBC2OF8l+8AgLphBi5xi\nTsycztEqDIoFZlQJU4YT\n=xeBL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T03:14:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/