hub.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/5913324d69ddea29bac18f9338f2fd846b00c415/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T03:00:44Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T03:00:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Verify local artifact bytes without HTTP (#14383)\n\n### Summary\n\nCloses TURBO-6304. Prepares the separately reviewed TAR staging work in\nTURBO-6300.\n\n```text\nLocal bytes + mandatory trusted SHA-256\n  Verify the complete byte vector\n  Match     VerifiedArtifact\n  Mismatch  Redacted DigestMismatch; no bytes released\n```\n\n- Add synchronous local-byte verification without constructing an HTTP\nclient or performing filesystem/cache I/O.\n- Retain the existing verified-artifact type and mandatory digest\nboundary for archive and future cache consumers.\n- Cover known and empty artifacts, altered bytes, wrong digests, and\nredacted mismatch diagnostics.\n\nThe caller must bound input size. This helper adds no time budget,\ntransport, installer, or publisher-authenticity guarantee; a matching\ndigest pins bytes only.","tree":{"sha":"c6845ffb8bad5d30eb598849c3327247d974651c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/c6845ffb8bad5d30eb598849c3327247d974651c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/5913324d69ddea29bac18f9338f2fd846b00c415","verification":{"payload":"tree c6845ffb8bad5d30eb598849c3327247d974651c\nparent 5b409397c0d02f648269be84308b78a941d39d34\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791255644 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791255644 -0600\n\nfeat: Verify local artifact bytes without HTTP (#14383)\n\n### Summary\n\nCloses TURBO-6304. Prepares the separately reviewed TAR staging work in\nTURBO-6300.\n\n```text\nLocal bytes + mandatory trusted SHA-256\n  Verify the complete byte vector\n  Match     VerifiedArtifact\n  Mismatch  Redacted DigestMismatch; no bytes released\n```\n\n- Add synchronous local-byte verification without constructing an HTTP\nclient or performing filesystem/cache I/O.\n- Retain the existing verified-artifact type and mandatory digest\nboundary for archive and future cache consumers.\n- Cover known and empty artifacts, altered bytes, wrong digests, and\nredacted mismatch diagnostics.\n\nThe caller must bound input size. This helper adds no time budget,\ntransport, installer, or publisher-authenticity guarantee; a matching\ndigest pins bytes only.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxGRcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAIUQAKGze2UKJ+AhT8sV1Bx7J9wX\nQwLwUepE5OQwuXG3IoiPF7YPw01Jq0jXXtPvJH4ct/CVWvZ8aXWZcn4YS7hoN3m+\nQ5Uo1+zSw/x/CR/UgjaPyQxwXDGsp2A0kwO9hf6a8TOkmsw0Ph1hSb3d2Gr9sVSu\n6h6oX51YdHlN4tftFvY50xEqe0WQXh8tnlIXoaDVXsoSSIACdIvlnfFt2vzEyTmg\nrbQXSox62rsro0M0tItoOTkCIMdeI4LMQ21T+ZhFmBvZJOpKXhypnzXqK5hKe9xe\n99LDMy9JZWzcov02ev485w1rvLfPoIHXPb5jOqzhSeD5mUhvtxHxTTx5TDwcpn2o\n5agIBnBSGZkM2Ocn8CYpSo/u29+aa68rCKJjs3qlANdmef6PDw3ZT1JueUwMY176\nQ2kv5YDFW8hgLh9iijd/REgb8YoIdn2PscvnMxLCl+5iGYQTfUez9pVOs5UwKJ1+\nabfkACYQJawq7sYdyjIci198Fs0pKfMYRn10jNOuw/QSDDvmqbx1UY6trqNMxnl3\neQC3MTd/xEF8e6H4uMl1w2kdSm5x2T73mNO/eJwV9J+kN8GXweLAfbOoCH5bOPxV\nlVFJVqWKHvz1Dff0+FnYjIQ6xqrSsJeBkyMAm01HTa27pdyM8Et2e6wWcGXqmLOe\nMWGTlx/fISji/zrjRWb3\n=RhDK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T03:00:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/5913324d69ddea29bac18f9338f2fd846b00c415","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDU5MTMzMjRkNjlkZGVhMjliYWMxOGY5MzM4ZjJmZDg0NmIwMGM0MTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/5b409397c0d02f648269be84308b78a941d39d34","sha":"5b409397c0d02f648269be84308b78a941d39d34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/5b409397c0d02f648269be84308b78a941d39d34"}],"sha":"5913324d69ddea29bac18f9338f2fd846b00c415","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/5913324d69ddea29bac18f9338f2fd846b00c415"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/5b409397c0d02f648269be84308b78a941d39d34/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T02:49:35Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T02:49:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Discover setup JavaScript package-manager declarations (#14382)\n\n### Summary\n\nCloses TURBO-6198.\n\nBuilds on #14381 and incorporates the shared parsing refactor from\n#14386. Discover root npm/pnpm declarations for setup and `turbo.lock`,\npreserving package-graph detection behavior and performing no registry\nor installation work.\n\n```text\nRoot package.json\n  turborepo-package-manager\n    Family: npm, pnpm, Yarn, Bun, nub, aube\n    Borrowed packageManager / devEngines entries\n      turborepo-repository    Existing graph and lockfile policy\n      turborepo-setup         npm/pnpm capability gate\n                             Constraints + integrity + OR/onFail + source pointers\n```\n\n- Share package-manager family identity and declaration structure\nbetween repository detection and setup, replacing setup''s separate\nnpm/pnpm-only identity model without expanding its supported managers.\n- Keep version grammar, bounds, integrity interpretation, failure\npolicy, and diagnostics in each consumer. Preserve repository validation\nordering, messages, source spans, URL handling, and the numeric-version\nfast path.\n- Preserve exact/ranged requests, build-sensitive top-level pins, and\nname-only declarations without replacing absent constraints with `*`.\n- Retain Corepack algorithm/digest metadata and reject malformed,\nrepeated, or misplaced checksum suffixes.\n- Respect native alternative ordering and error/warn/ignore policy while\nreporting known conflicts with declaration provenance.\n- Reject unsupported URLs/managers and malformed fields without falling\nback; keep diagnostics opaque and raw-field preprocessing bounded.\n\nThe shared core has no filesystem, network, executable discovery, or\nruntime invocation. This is library-only declaration discovery; artifact\nverification, catalog resolution, installers, CLI wiring, and lock\nserialization remain separate work.\n\n### Manual verification\n\nRan the compiled shared-parser, setup package-manager, and repository\npackage-manager test binaries with an empty `PATH`. All 5 shared-parser\ntests, 12 setup tests, and 157 repository package-manager tests passed\nwithout Node.js or a package-manager executable available.","tree":{"sha":"6edd656320391d24dce6709415907e704b56c2cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/6edd656320391d24dce6709415907e704b56c2cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/5b409397c0d02f648269be84308b78a941d39d34","verification":{"payload":"tree 6edd656320391d24dce6709415907e704b56c2cc\nparent 75999d01b4a037acaf610d91d2325131151d4b1a\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791254975 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791254975 -0600\n\nfeat: Discover setup JavaScript package-manager declarations (#14382)\n\n### Summary\n\nCloses TURBO-6198.\n\nBuilds on #14381 and incorporates the shared parsing refactor from\n#14386. Discover root npm/pnpm declarations for setup and `turbo.lock`,\npreserving package-graph detection behavior and performing no registry\nor installation work.\n\n```text\nRoot package.json\n  turborepo-package-manager\n    Family: npm, pnpm, Yarn, Bun, nub, aube\n    Borrowed packageManager / devEngines entries\n      turborepo-repository    Existing graph and lockfile policy\n      turborepo-setup         npm/pnpm capability gate\n                             Constraints + integrity + OR/onFail + source pointers\n```\n\n- Share package-manager family identity and declaration structure\nbetween repository detection and setup, replacing setup''s separate\nnpm/pnpm-only identity model without expanding its supported managers.\n- Keep version grammar, bounds, integrity interpretation, failure\npolicy, and diagnostics in each consumer. Preserve repository validation\nordering, messages, source spans, URL handling, and the numeric-version\nfast path.\n- Preserve exact/ranged requests, build-sensitive top-level pins, and\nname-only declarations without replacing absent constraints with `*`.\n- Retain Corepack algorithm/digest metadata and reject malformed,\nrepeated, or misplaced checksum suffixes.\n- Respect native alternative ordering and error/warn/ignore policy while\nreporting known conflicts with declaration provenance.\n- Reject unsupported URLs/managers and malformed fields without falling\nback; keep diagnostics opaque and raw-field preprocessing bounded.\n\nThe shared core has no filesystem, network, executable discovery, or\nruntime invocation. This is library-only declaration discovery; artifact\nverification, catalog resolution, installers, CLI wiring, and lock\nserialization remain separate work.\n\n### Manual verification\n\nRan the compiled shared-parser, setup package-manager, and repository\npackage-manager test binaries with an empty `PATH`. All 5 shared-parser\ntests, 12 setup tests, and 157 repository package-manager tests passed\nwithout Node.js or a package-manager executable available.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAA