99832790f30e1e304723661f153314044e791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/77b99832790f30e1e304723661f153314044e791"}],"sha":"fbe90e9e7b0965caa0dcc4b5eb89f253e2643106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/fbe90e9e7b0965caa0dcc4b5eb89f253e2643106"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/77b99832790f30e1e304723661f153314044e791/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:08:50Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:08:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Resolve Node versions from native declarations (#14378)\n\n### Summary\n\nCloses TURBO-6197.\n\nDiscover root Node declarations and resolve a reproducible exact release\nwithout upstream access, binary probes, or lock writing.\n\n```text\nRoot declarations\n  devEngines.runtime > .nvmrc > .node-version > engines.node\n  Intersect independent sources; preserve runtime-array alternatives\n  Select highest eligible injected exact release\n  Return version + declaration provenance\n```\n\n- Support strict npm exact/range requests; accept `node`, `lts/*`, and\nnamed LTS aliases only in `.nvmrc`, following nvm’s native format.\n- Reject those aliases in `devEngines.runtime.version`, `engines.node`,\nand `.node-version` rather than extending their declared syntax.\n- Preserve every authored constraint and identify conflicting source\nfiles.\n- Accept native name-only runtime declarations without inventing a\nversion constraint.\n- Bound source reads and catalog work; reject malformed fields,\nduplicate JSON keys, and contradictory release metadata.\n- Keep discovery separate from artifact selection, downloads, and\ninstallation.\n\n### Manual review\n\nChecked native runtime-array alternatives and optional-version behavior\nagainst npm''s declaration validator, then exercised conflict and\nprovenance cases with injected releases. No live upstream was required.","tree":{"sha":"dfaa10a99db9291210843fe1a46775fedf037076","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/dfaa10a99db9291210843fe1a46775fedf037076"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/77b99832790f30e1e304723661f153314044e791","verification":{"payload":"tree dfaa10a99db9291210843fe1a46775fedf037076\nparent 44ae237b31373477586847d38e07ef616f12f000\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791223730 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791223730 -0600\n\nfeat: Resolve Node versions from native declarations (#14378)\n\n### Summary\n\nCloses TURBO-6197.\n\nDiscover root Node declarations and resolve a reproducible exact release\nwithout upstream access, binary probes, or lock writing.\n\n```text\nRoot declarations\n  devEngines.runtime > .nvmrc > .node-version > engines.node\n  Intersect independent sources; preserve runtime-array alternatives\n  Select highest eligible injected exact release\n  Return version + declaration provenance\n```\n\n- Support strict npm exact/range requests; accept `node`, `lts/*`, and\nnamed LTS aliases only in `.nvmrc`, following nvm’s native format.\n- Reject those aliases in `devEngines.runtime.version`, `engines.node`,\nand `.node-version` rather than extending their declared syntax.\n- Preserve every authored constraint and identify conflicting source\nfiles.\n- Accept native name-only runtime declarations without inventing a\nversion constraint.\n- Bound source reads and catalog work; reject malformed fields,\nduplicate JSON keys, and contradictory release metadata.\n- Keep discovery separate from artifact selection, downloads, and\ninstallation.\n\n### Manual review\n\nChecked native runtime-array alternatives and optional-version behavior\nagainst npm''s declaration validator, then exercised conflict and\nprovenance cases with injected releases. No live upstream was required.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw+eyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4lsQACYmlojafLJjOSuR4wukzCnb\nXK6zQaCnVdpUbER5wTq4tTnNwy4rjt/t2HKwlsxMyBFFid+DoI3frKjkal+m8H4z\nig/fTgPcKNGx8+xQRBi4b/kAgyae/lWpL1xn481admWxB9LyP+A7UEL7yfNOUw7X\n9bKrq7mkPQnBU0iRmPrxc2EF7TtgfHrUqaA8Q6Ey7B8HTzfHB/wYQ0TiZAukcm0/\nyDWkvS9Mg6aO8sDMurTyjplP9PdwVxJH6pGeq8MY3sruWlavS7vDTYm91knQIReH\neDDMsmDeFIUr9nlOt/2nqdPkHJMcoODPNgoTE1tyZr6EcnQd8tr34AaIOJDoREZo\nrgLqUPRHe5H3y85aPhq7LYOMw9Tri2QPEyMMN0Hlo3XvApgY8df57j0GgF804AZN\nSCSn66I8zdVWcD8K7yGYwDLmzMapmxoMSEurKIZ4oFxeDRQE5x/4Ylmev2aTN++p\nlVG8MdWwWRGjhG/FCUwySwarJDlRJjOUHQChBwyKwAo6y+tkD3qZ2VTxPiF/ZCyp\naCs+tONNTVWKrzQIovVzvNAwHJiaIKYWUUyF2AgmO9n1pgS12c33L/F9S7+wQ2RV\n0mxCjpJxGx9ACG6R4qEKvW4CFIJZ+kmJID1di335yi4oC7sOHGR3TLuRcdM4DOpD\n7lvBNylGs1Kz4ZAQf3NZ\n=qFmX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T18:08:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/77b99832790f30e1e304723661f153314044e791","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDc3Yjk5ODMyNzkwZjMwZTFlMzA0NzIzNjYxZjE1MzMxNDA0NGU3OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/44ae237b31373477586847d38e07ef616f12f000","sha":"44ae237b31373477586847d38e07ef616f12f000","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/44ae237b31373477586847d38e07ef616f12f000"}],"sha":"77b99832790f30e1e304723661f153314044e791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/77b99832790f30e1e304723661f153314044e791"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/3623469?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/vercel-gh-bot-3","id":282332853,"login":"vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDOENQOtQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/44ae237b31373477586847d38e07ef616f12f000/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:00:34Z","email":"282332853+vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:00:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: Prune unused pnpm catalog snapshots (#14376)\n\nFixes #14372.\n\n`turbo prune` retained the entire lockfile catalog snapshot after\nremoving workspace importers. With `catalogPrune: true`, pnpm cleans\nunused entries from the workspace configuration before checking lockfile\nfreshness, then rejects those stale snapshots with\n`ERR_PNPM_LOCKFILE_CONFIG_MISMATCH`.\n\nRetain only catalog snapshots referenced by the remaining root and\nworkspace importers, including production, development, and optional\ndependencies. Match references by catalog name and dependency alias,\nnormalize the default catalog protocol, and omit empty catalog maps.\nKeep workspace catalog definitions and cleanup settings unchanged so\npnpm can apply its configured cleanup behavior.\n\nAdd regression coverage for default and named catalogs, root references,\nworkspace-link resolutions, removal of the final catalog snapshot, and\nstandard/Docker output with `catalogPrune` enabled, disabled, or\nomitted.\n\n### Manual verification\n\nUsing the supplied reproduction with pnpm 12.9.1 on Node 24, the\noriginal pruned output fails a frozen install with the reported catalog\nmismatch. With this fix, frozen installs succeed for standard output and\nDocker''s `out/json` output. With pruning enabled, pnpm removes the\nunused `is-odd` workspace catalog entry; with pruning disabled or\nomitted, catalog definitions remain available. Lifecycle scripts were\ndisabled during these installs.\n\nCo-authored-by: vercel-gh-bot-3[bot] <282332853+vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f0ecd6ba2e1d42037948eab76ae25fe038f30066","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/f0ecd6ba2e1d42037948eab76ae25fe038f30066"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/44ae237b31373477586847d38e07ef616f12f000","verification":{"payload":"tree f0ecd6ba2e1d42037948eab76ae25fe038f30066\nparent a0bbc06e112dcd5c513455ed7623c827bdf3b265\nauthor vercel-gh-bot-3[bot] <282332853+vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791219634 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791219634 +0000\n\nfix: Prune unused pnpm catalog snapshots (#14376)\n\nFixes #14372.\n\n`turbo prune` retained the entire lockfile catalog snapshot after\nremoving workspace importers. With `catalogPrune: true`, pnpm cleans\nunused entries from the workspace configuration before checking lockfile\nfreshness, then rejects those stale snapshots with\n`ERR_PNPM_LOCKFILE_CONFIG_MISMATCH`.\n\nRetain only catalog snapshots referenced by the remaining root and\nworkspace importers, including production, development, and optional\ndependencies. Match references by catalog name and dependency alias,\nnormalize the default catalog protocol, and omit empty catalog maps.\nKeep workspace catalog definitions and cleanup settings unchanged so\npnpm can apply its configured cleanup behavior.\n\nAdd regression coverage for default and named catalogs, root references,\nworkspace-link resolutions, removal of the final catalog snapshot, and\nstandard/Docker output with `catalogPrune` enabled, disabled, or\nomitted.\n\n### Manual verification\n\nUsing the supplied reproduction with pnpm 12.9.1 on Node 24, the\noriginal pruned output fails a frozen install with the reported catalog\nmismatch. With this fix, frozen installs succeed for standard output and\nDocker''s `out/json` output. With pruning enabled, pnpm removes the\nunused `is-odd` workspace catalog entry; with pruning disabled or\nomitted, catalog definitions remain available. Lifecycle scripts were\ndisabled during these installs.\n\nCo-authored-by: vercel-gh-bot-3[bot] <282332853+vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw9eyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7oEQALGDq2LOAhwJ5d72iov3WPtO\nDaMMtGj/I5NuiKiRAiv0cKw5g4S8w6vihslNq0SZwvKKNb5YREnZ982b+6+FXdbZ\nLNOmSDtQZZs3IBa5yWjChy2gG0OqsvKmBpHdKzrFeDgQbl6oE8SGxRBQXrjwmhbW\nwRiHoN08enRwlGHGY3MERICf/lkn/NpA97QmLvGXmMZXXDjKLC2xmWq/BzQ5bweT\nMxEeHrNCjDScATJ674qg2JQkO01Vko0gwj9SxIcmfg7tejikvC/iisH1bNPr00OA\nmFekNB9jPbCxeO4OkamMomPqEENj49uryCXpo/hx3MlCnLkhlkeEnVN39xxaIl4C\nWRKD7SiFAfTkcPaMh0xZjLJJO8cJ7iu63g6TMGn65uHbJUCnS0lZozDzNpsBnCyo\nW4mbBH/M/ij+4B9zHxCo9s/eTLMCKuNtOOtgKmZpUWGPOU+XBlfmStm0BjsugHCy\nt4oZkV+BfLj2IU8o7prvs8ua+TFzZAYA6kYV25rGv7tM5sgDC0PcLmohybNPMlC8\n6NbdQDH/jBERqOzg2OOfe3OcarjB9oHiIxTN0ZYoy8AfYq6mGokGJW3ZmGm3oH+5\n4yZZ4ySxjRyHMXWyz14Vx3QyCzy7fFXXLsl/Mb2+I22XMXhx3D5gkgYKAQL5h2N5\nJbxBejH9x01aX5AjFcNs\n=OTNE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T17:00:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/44ae237b31373477586847d38e07ef616f12f000","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDQ0YWUyMzdiMzEzNzM0Nzc1ODY4NDdkMzhlMDdlZjYxNmYxMmYwMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/a0bbc06e112dcd5c513455ed7623c827bdf3b265","sha":"a0bbc06e112dcd5c513455ed7623c827bdf3b265","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/a0bbc06e112dcd5c513455ed7623c827bdf3b265"}],"sha":"44ae237b31373477586847d38e07ef616f12f000","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/44ae237b31373477586847d38e07ef616f12f000"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/a0bbc06e112dcd5c513455ed7623c827bdf3b265/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:01:39Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:01:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Validate setup npm version requests (#14375)\n\n### Summary\n\nCloses TURBO-6297.\n\nAdd a strict setup-only npm request boundary without changing\npackage-graph semver behavior or invoking Node at runtime.\n\n```text\nAuthored request\n  Validate every fragment and resource limit\n  Preserve OR branches of AND comparators\n  Match injected canonical releases\n```\n\n- Support exact/partial versions, wildcards, caret/tilde operators,\nhyphen ranges, comparator conjunctions, and disjunctions.\n- Preserve impossible intersections and authored constraints rather than\nsimplifying them into broader requests.\n- Apply branch-local prerelease opt-in and build-insensitive precedence,\nwith an exact-release identity hook for discovery.\n- Reject malformed fragments, unsafe numeric components, oversized\ncandidates, and excessive parser work.\n- Commit deterministic npm-reference fixtures and a regeneration script;\nNode aliases remain resolver policy.\n\n### Manual review\n\nCompared generated requests/releases against npm''s strict semver\nbehavior. Intentional differences preserve authored constraints where\nnpm drops stable-zero lower bounds or explicit prerelease OR branches,\nand retain exact numeric prerelease ordering instead of JavaScript\nrounding. Test binaries also ran successfully with Node absent from\nPATH.","tree":{"sha":"198633c54c74d324f079e7de12528c623a129917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/198633c54c74d324f079e7de12528c623a129917"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/a0bbc06e112dcd5c513455ed7623c827bdf3b265","verification":{"payload":"tree 198633c54c74d324f079e7de12528c623a129917\nparent 56a41ba007258b385b986dbbc46efd4c89ec5d96\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1791216099 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791216099 -0600\n\nfeat: Validate setup npm version requests (#14375)\n\n### Summary\n\nCloses TURBO-6297.\n\nAdd a strict setup-only npm request boundary without changing\npackage-graph semver behavior or invoking Node at runtime.\n\n```text\nAuthored request\n  Validate every fragment and resource limit\n  Preserve OR branches of AND comparators\n  Match injected canonical releases\n```\n\n- Support exact/partial versions, wildcards, caret/tilde operators,\nhyphen ranges, comparator conjunctions, and disjunctions.\n- Preserve impossible intersections and authored constraints rather than\nsimplifying them into broader requests.\n- Apply branch-local prerelease opt-in and build-insensitive precedence,\nwith an exact-release identity hook for discovery.\n- Reject malformed fragments, unsafe numeric components, oversized\ncandidates, and excessive parser work.\n- Commit deterministic npm-reference fixtures and a regeneration script;\nNode aliases remain resolver policy.\n\n### Manual review\n\nCompared generated requests/releases against npm''s strict semver\nbehavior. Intentional differences preserve authored constraints where\nnpm drops stable-zero lower bounds or explicit prerelease OR branches,\nand retain exact numeric prerelease ordering instead of JavaScript\nrounding. Test binaries also ran successfully with Node absent from\nPATH.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw8njCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdf0QADukCOJgYY/6RIUrbs/WYQug\nnai60S7MacsC3VHjwtfZ/59CQR1Eg5TaifBF2i3oXkLgOy3JEdTGroKa08krbbLC\nD8SJMxzJAqxnmuAGnzEducsxgCQrf8zG/Ijmm7NJuNBnP2JCAUuq5EQhqjokEPsw\nCJOptn1xtiIhtRsiqVfClki3Er8gyURG17Zkj90uJyiwxi7V6zGBWreGHQQs/mf6\nyihVDOwEqKoneOkwAfmoZURqwTF0q3lMIHu4cv4tiYrasZgO+sF+8icxvH8FP88M\nwHuqebu8plDNVNvSco7vELE13xrpBZBR6TfWKiB3i1wDEXkL5GVP5mM0fuFH/Yvj\neSYkOSomqIL