tarred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/fba5351c47fe9b1bb1669d554a8535f2f3376a36/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:52:12Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:52:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Expose task and package tags in `query` (#14343)\n\n### Description\n\nSecond slice of the generic tags work, based on #14342. This PR exposes\nlabels without adding tag predicates or CLI selectors.\n\n```text\nResolved configuration\n├── Package.tags\n└── RepositoryTask.tags\n    └── Package.tags (separate package labels)\n```\n\n- Expose configured package labels and resolved task labels, returning\nempty arrays when absent.\n- Keep task labels separate from package labels, preserving order and\nduplicates.\n- Decode JSON-escaped package labels exactly once at the Query access\nboundary.\n- Add the run adapter, update QueryRun implementations and mocks, and\ndocument the metadata fields.\n\nThe schema snapshot in this PR adds only tag metadata. Tag selection and\naffected-task predicates follow separately.","tree":{"sha":"02fab4d019447c3fd850c02bea22e7030efb388f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/02fab4d019447c3fd850c02bea22e7030efb388f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/fba5351c47fe9b1bb1669d554a8535f2f3376a36","verification":{"payload":"tree 02fab4d019447c3fd850c02bea22e7030efb388f\nparent b4570e0c966561a4cbb09ae529582bad77cf05c8\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1790776332 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790776332 -0600\n\nfeat: Expose task and package tags in `query` (#14343)\n\n### Description\n\nSecond slice of the generic tags work, based on #14342. This PR exposes\nlabels without adding tag predicates or CLI selectors.\n\n```text\nResolved configuration\n├── Package.tags\n└── RepositoryTask.tags\n    └── Package.tags (separate package labels)\n```\n\n- Expose configured package labels and resolved task labels, returning\nempty arrays when absent.\n- Keep task labels separate from package labels, preserving order and\nduplicates.\n- Decode JSON-escaped package labels exactly once at the Query access\nboundary.\n- Add the run adapter, update QueryRun implementations and mocks, and\ndocument the metadata fields.\n\nThe schema snapshot in this PR adds only tag metadata. Tag selection and\naffected-task predicates follow separately.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvRQMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdQ8QAIJD4bTWvLyL5a2kWJYgVsbV\n7Bu1sl+ovkPXv6sYP+A2V+qWM17/kqnr9Zq7z6u43y2jPqJQsBcBHxVZNkVCRu5B\n+BfobeLA/TsqmsA0uN2wYpk3wHDNnOO1fJwYIcsFnf8RbqxXam3hEPQO4UJUsPbH\nai3WZUXKKvQ9GthT0ijUcKZYSKxL+OdfKM/vcanZhJXGlWD09NLaCvNcS7osc3DG\nuCl3Fa4B0ONWm/aAo2bYwrKhf24YZtgYhRFxp08ykVCbO1eI6HFjzdFQDW09im89\n2eMcsC8A7JAVYyyYl5rurhw1uoHDyR6NJkOkbu9bFHAVvl3jm47fZrkLwI6JvOi1\nk8gnoA//akGbN0jbQSPux/yWc3VYwrDmAygDj0oUogCsr8jPxUNlmvlFjRMpZjaU\n0h5AtlWpfI35WAtHsl0+a1GWW9I0xI9y3OINcrkfeb5j+GLd/Q1CuTcM10H48J1G\nluUp/aDUgFDkpGdlT0NT+TrTiNpUMkc08VOir6mHzvFPbDkanBo5/2WXgymHdKfQ\npEqfWk9jc9RJP2DgxzEK41OPgGpxTMBeFqBKzBT8s+STsuvURbqt50k2wudOUk0X\nAg2i/LCeDWFbGu1tbh2EnHMVOspBHC5q1IlX6u6KeEOMLhgh/+1wwTvZd+IyTlX7\nTEsdPiV5kfBSJcg2xurl\n=sA2A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:52:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/fba5351c47fe9b1bb1669d554a8535f2f3376a36","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKGZiYTUzNTFjNDdmZTliMWJiMTY2OWQ1NTRhODUzNWYyZjMzNzZhMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/b4570e0c966561a4cbb09ae529582bad77cf05c8","sha":"b4570e0c966561a4cbb09ae529582bad77cf05c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/b4570e0c966561a4cbb09ae529582bad77cf05c8"}],"sha":"fba5351c47fe9b1bb1669d554a8535f2f3376a36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/fba5351c47fe9b1bb1669d554a8535f2f3376a36"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/b4570e0c966561a4cbb09ae529582bad77cf05c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:47:58Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:47:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: Deflake untracked scan-scope assertions (#14348)\n\n### Description\n\nThe [Windows CI\njob](https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/actions/runs/36639518224/job/109648252434?pr=14343)\nhung in\n`scoped_run_hashes_untracked_files_identically_to_whole_repo_scan` until\nthe test step timed out. The logs do not identify the stalled\nsubprocess, but this test''s scan-scope checks unnecessarily execute npm\ntasks just to inspect debug logs.\n\nUse dry runs for scan-scope logging instead. They still perform input\nhashing and scan selection, without launching package-manager or task\nprocesses.\n\n```diff\n Scan-scope debug-log checks\n   Select tasks and discover inputs\n   Hash tracked and untracked files\n-  Execute npm build tasks\n+  Emit dry-run output without executing tasks\n   Assert the selected scan scope in the debug log\n```\n\n- Preserve the existing hash-equivalence and scan-scope assertions.\n- Add a regression test with an `exit 1` build script, proving that\nlogging the scan scope does not execute the task.\n- Leave the watch test''s real task execution unchanged.\n\n### Testing Instructions\n\nThe new `scan_scope_logging_does_not_execute_tasks` regression must\nsuccessfully collect the scoped-scan debug log despite the deliberately\nfailing build script. The existing tests continue to cover scoped versus\nwhole-repository hashes, ignore rules, fallback cases, and watch\nbehavior.","tree":{"sha":"19bad1ddd7ea501b268dda98104f9faf0a1c6223","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/19bad1ddd7ea501b268dda98104f9faf0a1c6223"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/b4570e0c966561a4cbb09ae529582bad77cf05c8","verification":{"payload":"tree 19bad1ddd7ea501b268dda98104f9faf0a1c6223\nparent fa107aa83463ea1877a3cf5baba447d7e9bda78a\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1790776078 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790776078 -0600\n\ntest: Deflake untracked scan-scope assertions (#14348)\n\n### Description\n\nThe [Windows CI\njob](https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/actions/runs/36639518224/job/109648252434?pr=14343)\nhung in\n`scoped_run_hashes_untracked_files_identically_to_whole_repo_scan` until\nthe test step timed out. The logs do not identify the stalled\nsubprocess, but this test''s scan-scope checks unnecessarily execute npm\ntasks just to inspect debug logs.\n\nUse dry runs for scan-scope logging instead. They still perform input\nhashing and scan selection, without launching package-manager or task\nprocesses.\n\n```diff\n Scan-scope debug-log checks\n   Select tasks and discover inputs\n   Hash tracked and untracked files\n-  Execute npm build tasks\n+  Emit dry-run output without executing tasks\n   Assert the selected scan scope in the debug log\n```\n\n- Preserve the existing hash-equivalence and scan-scope assertions.\n- Add a regression test with an `exit 1` build script, proving that\nlogging the scan scope does not execute the task.\n- Leave the watch test''s real task execution unchanged.\n\n### Testing Instructions\n\nThe new `scan_scope_logging_does_not_execute_tasks` regression must\nsuccessfully collect the scoped-scan debug log despite the deliberately\nfailing build script. The existing tests continue to cover scoped versus\nwhole-repository hashes, ignore rules, fallback cases, and watch\nbehavior.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvRMOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACMkQAC9zDtutwxnTpaknXwg+Bvq5\nPryfnv9uwMgBo/ICJGpRLs2+r9uVX5BCdCgvs6BmRz0YdnYQTtFp+JTcNaV7OBrP\nAH1DjIdbHxU06oIZut1+IDtzp/wxyLz02Za5a3vTPCSOcDsxhX5UpY1DbmyEhDHI\nggDJF/cSwh9McvhoQx2cH+93KsNw3THAgcQ9VzsAFgZ+nBkT3JdQ8vHqT1V6yS0P\nAKWxPKDCSmtBx/y9YoNADgkfuk3l4kZZ5vQfQQAuDdwo8qoPhLdkRtJtn7zNuxVC\n2LEbGRz9dVWLXqp063zf36nBIgazwnReGO+IcaEY1qY5VJsJ4aobtITSM3UnamEg\nDUUoYz3fSXDDbUtn9PSg5wzpHAPmMHNy2QNsjL77KxKFcymi6v96/8KhpJ8AU6uy\nYQb5CN8pqJMlu9H6NM2ZXenR358PBvy+G+XuncMRO0UD7PfEa37bZ25FKVj/dQ9l\nmZmZwtKi4nH9v1tCJVwjL4J0W/xLb3KkeGc08aQL9quPcOfVTDMVnhlnROXhofFQ\nJAshoT18zQmjwrn5BRJnb2gZaupM7kHRgiJJKiXOpVsUASOJMp7sTzWeVISDysTg\necdlUfSbBDla7hbg7+dxxVGnPQMrkhXvrGiB872Yycs/+hKlLy0LnW8qW2ZWiRN6\nM32ZP2qEVt9S56ZTRP0/\n=F7d4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:47:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/b4570e0c966561a4cbb09ae529582bad77cf05c8","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKGI0NTcwZTBjOTY2NTYxYTRjYmIwOWFlNTI5NTgyYmFkNzdjZjA1Yzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/fa107aa83463ea1877a3