cy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/6a1031923f3db91d9b1332bf3c4e250b651580b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T11:39:02Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T11:39:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: Keep Yarn patch resolutions with npm protocol selectors in prune (#14337)\n\n### Description\n\nFixes #14336.\n\nWhen a Yarn Berry `resolutions` selector includes the `npm:` protocol\nbut the workspace''s dependency range doesn''t, `turbo prune` never\nmatched the override while it built the transitive closure. The patched\npackage fell out of the pruned graph, so prune also dropped the\n`resolutions` entry, the patch file, and the `patch:` lockfile entry.\n\n```text\nroot package.json   \"debug@npm:^4.0.0\": \"patch:debug@npm%3A4.4.3#~/.yarn/patches/...\"\napp/package.json    \"debug\": \"^4.0.0\"\n```\n\nThe range comparison only added the default `npm:` protocol to the\nresolution side. It now works in both directions:\n\n```diff\n if resolution range != dependency range\n   && !eq_with_protocol(dependency.range, resolution_range, \"npm:\")\n+  && !eq_with_protocol(resolution_range, dependency.range, \"npm:\")\n   return None\n```\n\n- Adds a unit test for the `npm:`-qualified selector.\n- Adds the issue''s reproduction as the `issue-14336` lockfile fixture,\npruned with `--docker`.\n\n### Testing Instructions\n\nWithout the fix, `pnpm check-lockfiles --fixture issue-14336` fails\nvalidation. With the fix, it passes. I also ran the reporter''s repro\nagainst the new build: the pruned `out/json` keeps the resolution and\nthe patch file, `yarn install --immutable` succeeds, and the installed\n`debug` is patched.","tree":{"sha":"000098f4dbc480d2d182707776a583b529ce40ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/000098f4dbc480d2d182707776a583b529ce40ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/6a1031923f3db91d9b1332bf3c4e250b651580b3","verification":{"payload":"tree 000098f4dbc480d2d182707776a583b529ce40ed\nparent ac801403d9d58fc13331485de7b11b992c2da5d9\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1790681942 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790681942 -0600\n\nfix: Keep Yarn patch resolutions with npm protocol selectors in prune (#14337)\n\n### Description\n\nFixes #14336.\n\nWhen a Yarn Berry `resolutions` selector includes the `npm:` protocol\nbut the workspace''s dependency range doesn''t, `turbo prune` never\nmatched the override while it built the transitive closure. The patched\npackage fell out of the pruned graph, so prune also dropped the\n`resolutions` entry, the patch file, and the `patch:` lockfile entry.\n\n```text\nroot package.json   \"debug@npm:^4.0.0\": \"patch:debug@npm%3A4.4.3#~/.yarn/patches/...\"\napp/package.json    \"debug\": \"^4.0.0\"\n```\n\nThe range comparison only added the default `npm:` protocol to the\nresolution side. It now works in both directions:\n\n```diff\n if resolution range != dependency range\n   && !eq_with_protocol(dependency.range, resolution_range, \"npm:\")\n+  && !eq_with_protocol(resolution_range, dependency.range, \"npm:\")\n   return None\n```\n\n- Adds a unit test for the `npm:`-qualified selector.\n- Adds the issue''s reproduction as the `issue-14336` lockfile fixture,\npruned with `--docker`.\n\n### Testing Instructions\n\nWithout the fix, `pnpm check-lockfiles --fixture issue-14336` fails\nvalidation. With the fix, it passes. I also ran the reporter''s repro\nagainst the new build: the pruned `out/json` keeps the resolution and\nthe patch file, `yarn install --immutable` succeeds, and the installed\n`debug` is patched.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu6NWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaZwQAESrDFufAd/Pw9d9FIAg9kO9\ny2eDPwktZF5HKtUGBP6S5BOX+eyFF/6d8g0c1SVs/hJnUFLrGfMpBZGS6v/Ei2ow\nEv3NswpxxlelFab5JL8uMulgCqcuBcMseJO8RGLwVcNlwt0aKoRFuBMumQ2+HCDn\nHUhx66w9VQbM6QjH5pBfInZdrwmKHYXfa5g1yDpcDlZvOd/dLg/7YlUgz/HSjuJT\n6kzC4S1KlgCknudTlql4YRCxoz4wzddwNlOm9c/vhwqjjQL2jPDNf+UOt6b7c7XC\nIpEa62FjP+Gynnlrv4kY173adXG+xAD0pb1GwrrYGOZGEZNcOsL3jp1sRbjAz18W\nzMgHh4EJgrDmNAt3nGRnnwae6dx8CGQbAnAdVDRrtQs+2Jeflu1gDtV9s9hp3Y1z\nrv+qcFsR2uYsIw9OMESOLFEHgytb0w9mt98XwV8hakfj+RIS8GOxhmxk1pnQLj7n\n5n978Y5chbblXjUZQXW39LoPztQlhgnBIqp7EYf27ZoB6KQewL6WALTDxQvIhffv\nDs5N2xWsTx0IrNRfTJoqvfnyNheprUkV+5iMdJHSBOYq3s3TLCDsjV/A5Qgqi0mk\nXheFV4HBWPX66eBnpnj4t1jsxShYj5HpjPdNvYAeSmJkdF1a1/Lr7krLCVDv+Qol\ng2BVfEjpxM9l2EXRWFBA\n=sRNM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T11:39:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/6a1031923f3db91d9b1332bf3c4e250b651580b3","node_id":"C_kwDOGKvm49oAKDZhMTAzMTkyM2YzZGI5MWQ5YjEzMzJiZjNjNGUyNTBiNjUxNTgwYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/commit/ac801403d9d58fc13331485de7b11b992c2da5d9","sha":"ac801403d9d58fc13331485de7b11b992c2da5d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/ac801403d9d58fc13331485de7b11b992c2da5d9"}],"sha":"6a1031923f3db91d9b1332bf3c4e250b651580b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/6a1031923f3db91d9b1332bf3c4e250b651580b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35677084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonyshew","id":35677084,"login":"anthonyshew","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc3MDg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonyshew","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/commits/ac801403d9d58fc13331485de7b11b992c2da5d9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T05:16:42Z","email":"anthony.shew@vercel.com","name":"Anthony Shew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T05:16:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: Install standalone turbo on Windows with PowerShell (#14334)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Replace the global npm install with the unpinned standalone `turbo`\nbinary in CI. This supersedes #14333.\n- Use the native PowerShell installer on Windows; keep the POSIX\ninstaller on macOS and Linux.\n- Preserve the optional release-CI version or npm dist-tag override.\n\n```diff\n install-global-turbo\n-└── bash → /install (all runners)\n+├── bash → /install (macOS/Linux)\n+└── pwsh → /install.ps1 (Windows)\n```\n\n## Manual verification\n\nExecuted the Windows action''s PowerShell step with a mocked installer\nand npm response in a native Windows ARM64 VM: unpinned installation,\ndist-tag override, and unsafe-input rejection passed. The actual x64\nbinary install requires CI''s Windows x64 runner.","tree":{"sha":"d8edb2d3b1eb5d908fb8b9bfec68c8a808e0499f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/trees/d8edb2d3b1eb5d908fb8b9bfec68c8a808e0499f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/turborepo/git/commits/ac801403d9d58fc13331485de7b11b992c2da5d9","verification":{"payload":"tree d8edb2d3b1eb5d908fb8b9bfec68c8a808e0499f\nparent e2ce8832a152a7b82c22ae15bdc21b3afc3fd2a6\nauthor Anthony Shew <anthony.shew@vercel.com> 1790572602 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790572602 -0600\n\nci: Install standalone turbo on Windows with PowerShell (#14334)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Replace the global npm install with the unpinned standalone `turbo`\nbinary in CI. This supersedes #14333.\n- Use the native PowerShell installer on Windows; keep the POSIX\ninstaller on macOS and Linux.\n- Preserve the optional release-CI version or npm dist-tag override.\n\n```diff\n install-global-turbo\n-└── bash → /install (all runners)\n+├── bash → /install (macOS/Linux)\n+└── pwsh → /install.ps1 (Windows)\n```\n\n## Manual verification\n\nExecuted the Windows action''s PowerShell step with a mocked installer\nand npm response in a native Windows ARM64 VM: unpinned installation,\ndist-tag override, and unsafe-input rejection passed. The actual x64\nbinary install requires CI''s Windows x64 runner.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqufg6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAL5EQAHKaeX6MZvmsuKpnQThL0R/G\nDlSyr08J137yyoND0aEe5f9w3Ec4KKiqTCNluARaF+y6gj0sjzQYpKWx4At/oClS\n6UD6TthZFvDmuh88VTgL1BRbf5U84wyiSdzXdoJ+X76XovdKSjkfYC21dJ3BWJD6\nkBZtMkkHpfY2TeiBXW6qqI3DxuXH7mKB6jvEKaRDrzrjkMY/RpL2yHPJ8EEnlJlO\nN57P6eF6OhJLeun510qyvSVrjfZFBwQHcM9neQNJmCoUFYoB2PwJYeHlYL2DJnX6\nlwHuSX9CBr8/BP5cCMHyCUdFFUtq2JNqrZZhGIqPJXeEX2INpFSI8pCu5ofAWP90\nudAhS9dmbo0hNko/mZ3C6JfMo4Hk0tPpokgMp4S7rfHlIiYHFOKHmRpxwA5HCc9L\n/5ONZbnEbjB4etH2G9zvWOt0vriTABX09l9wwPze3z9V8SA1fcsZLCcygKjHJ1yS\ntW6zA3P9RSkHzJ2THzP+BJOzsnMCPDCb+ekSeF4mLBpPVpwFwSmhBQukN9MkVD21\nafe3mhevUu15DdjnIstIxsgf3ZSlNBzEfQP7DZGS02yIgjpruOsGUmmQva7aZdBq\neJEHTZ1SXEoSaGz/GI5Izo9627BXjqdpKlVDESIYEFzv0UkXmmQjNISqQYCblCIT\nAOO0VvYfbUHL8JArfD4M\n=9LGd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T05:16:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","re